ing a lot of progress. Of course, the blue states are suing us to say that they don't have to share that data, but the corruption is absolutely astounding. The Vice President has now leaned in with his fraud task force. We are now on supercharge, not that we weren't before, but now we're really on warp speed to do everything we can in the next two and a half years to get this under control and to change it for good.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, well, you know all the fraud is going to be in Minnesota, California, Washington state, Oregon, Colorado --\par \par \uc2 ROLLINS: Correct.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- is Colorado give over their information?\par \par \uc2 ROLLINS: No, they haven't. It's a literally -- it's so pervasive everywhere. But here's a good -- I mean, this is a really interesting point. Since we took over, we have actually moved four and a half million people off of food stamps. And Laura, this is before the work requirements have even kicked in under the one big beautiful bill.\par \par \uc2 So, we've gone from forty-three million to around thirty-eight million in just a little over a year, but it's going to begin even more and more and more as we work to take people back to the dignity of work and we kick the fraudsters out of the program. There's so much work to do.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, we ramp up those deportations, mass deportations, you'll really start seeing a drop in food stamps because, obviously, you know, children have to get fed and they're fed through the program as well.\par \par \uc2 Madam Secretary, apparently fake email addresses, apparently, is all it takes to get benefits as well. The Foundation for Government Accountability found that more than 5,000 email accounts were used to sign up for food stamps from some in foreign countries, Canada, China, Mexico. You can't even make this. This is like COVID fraud.\par \par \uc2 ROLLINS: It really is so scary to think if President Trump hadn't won in November of 2024, I don't know that we would have ever gotten our country back. I really don't believe that. Because we had had the first term and then we had four years to sort of get ready and organize and then go really fast, this is why we're uncovering all of this.\par \par \uc2 What you're talking about is this crazy thing called broad-based categorical eligibility. Forty-six states use it, which basically just means, oh, here's an electric bill and here's an email address. There's no identification verification required and anybody can sign up for it.\par \par \uc2 And in the Biden years, the food stamp program grew by 40 percent. Of course they're buying votes, right? They're hoping that using all of this government money will create more voters for them, illegal and legal. And that's why they're fighting so hard against us right now to keep this data from coming in, so that we can really fix the program.\par \par \uc2 But we're going to do it. We're making a lot of progress. And I'm just -- I'm really grateful to the USDA team. It's our inspector general at USDA that has really found those 893 that have been arrested, that are going to trial, they're going to jail. And yeah, we're not going to -- exactly. It is a drop in the bucket. But it's important --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's a warning.\par \par \uc2 ROLLINS: -- where we are, where we were. We've got a lot of work to do.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, it's a warning, though. You play around on this stuff. You got to do jail time. This is theft from the public treasury.\par \par \uc2 ROLLINS: That's right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It happened during COVID. It happens with Medicare. It happens with hospice and fake transportation for the elderly. And it's happening in the SNAP program. But at least you got all the junk food out of that SNAP program, Madam Secretary. So, I'm glad the administration --\par \par \uc2 ROLLINS: Twenty-two steaks at least.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah. Really people are pissed now with that. Madam Secretary,