a military booty call. They're just always up. You call them up. They come over, they do your job. Is that a fair analogy?\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: I thought you're talking about the breakfast the curds and whey.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Oh, very good.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Just kidding. The Kurds been hearing about them for a long time. Great fighting force, good allies of the United States. And looks like that once again, they're going to come in and try to help out here and stabilize.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: We don't always help them.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: We don't, and it is a remark on American power that they still hang around because we are their best option. Turkey is certainly not, Assad was not, etcetera, so you have this opportunity here for a possible way forward. I don't know if it turns out to be true that this has been in the works for some time. That would certainly be interesting. I think that we will learn a lot in the coming days after the main fighting is over, how the strategy was put in place over a longer period of time, and it wasn't over a weekend, as we are talking about now.\par \par \uc2 Thought Karoline Leavitt's briefing was very good, and especially she is saying, so far, thus far, things are really good, and I think we have to acknowledge that and point out that Iran has just decided to take everybody down with it. Like, if we're going down, then we're going to take everyone down with us.\par \par \uc2 So, what Iran did was mobilize the world against it, as well as there's all sorts of things that have happened the last 20 years, but mostly since the last eight years when President Trump was in office, starting with the Abraham Accords.\par \par \uc2 But also you have new leadership in Saudi and Abu Dhabi and Dubai, and they want a younger, more modern type of living and Iran, doesn't. So, Iran wants to take all of them down, and these people have something worth fighting for, meaning our allies. And so, yes, I agree with her. Like, thus far, it looks like we are in a very positive territory.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, imagine if we decided to do this when they had nukes, or you wouldn't ever be able to do it, because you see how they're reacting now without nukes.\par \par \uc2 Jesse, it seems like what Hegseth is saying is, sounds really good, but it only is good until boots are on the ground. Are we confident that that will -- that case will never be?\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: No, but you always want to keep that option open, and so far, that's not where this is going. As Trump would say, we've never seen anything like this. This is two times the firepower that we saw over Iraq and shock and awe (ph). These are B-52s dropping 80,000 pound ordinance. We have artificial intelligence identifying target. Space Force is seeing where these Iranian missiles launch from, and then can take out the launch pad like that. We're shooting down Iranian drones with laser weapons, also kamikaze drones. We're using them for the first time ever in combat.\par \par \uc2 So, this is just an astonishing display of American military superiority, probably officially marks the beginning of 21st Century warfare. We have completely eradicated the two top layers of the Iranian leadership. The Navy is at the bottom of the sea, and their missiles were going from 80 a day to now 20 a day.\par \par \uc2 The case is clear, number one sponsor of terror in the world. They were ramping up their ballistic missile capabilities. They were digging deeper tunnels to enrich again, and their Navy threatens the flow of oil.\par \par \uc2 So, we don't care who rules the country, they just have to play by our rules, whether that's a remnant of the regime or some man of the people. We could also seize their island oil terminal and just turn off the spigot if we don't like who they give us. The objectives are very clear. You completely disarm the rogue nation and then pummel the leadership until a friendlier face pops up.\par \par \uc2 We obviously have the Kurds in play. Obviously the CIA is on the ground, but we're not going to put a timetable on this like Barack Obama. We're not going to tell the enemy when we're leaving. That's stupid. Yes, there will be more casualties. That's horrible. But so far, it's early, only six, and God bless these people.\par \par \uc2 In about a month or two, Donald Trump will be visiting Beijing, and he will then, if this is a successful mission, have complete control over Chinese oil imports. That is a lot of clout, and we hope it works out.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: All right. Jessica, say something horribly negative about this situation.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: OK, I've got one. I have like 10. Jesse just said, we don't care who rules Iran. I thought that we cared about these hundreds of thousands --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I said as long as they follow our rules. We don't want a radical Muslim clerk, and we don't want someone to align with the Chinese.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I'm sure that all the protesters in the streets are heartened to hear the way that you see things, that if people play by our rules and our rules could just be, you know, stop with enriching uranium, but we have been very lax on human rights violations, especially with the Chinese, the Uyghurs, I think, are still basically in concentration camps.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: If you want to spread democracy in the Middle East. Again, that's fine.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Jesse, enough.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No, enough for you, Jessica. What we have in Venezuela worked out pretty well.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes, you took out Maduro in like 20 minutes, and he's in a jail cell. It is not the same analysis.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You want to be realistic about this. We're not going to push democracy on day one at the end of a gun.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: The comp to Venezuela is ridiculous. Maduro went down in what, 24 hours, he awaits trial here. Delcy Rodriguez was in play. We knew exactly who she was. She had control of it.\par \par \uc2 We also had Maria Machado, who we were in conversations with, if you think that going after a theocracy like this, made up of religious lunatics who you cut off the head and a hundred more sprout out is the same. It just makes you look stupid.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's not the same.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Jesse, get your hand down.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's down. It's more challenging.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Fully down, mouth down too.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You are crazy.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I'm not.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's like the State of the Union. They are crazy.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No one who's watching this, by the way, thinks I'm the crazy one.\par \par \uc2 The timeline --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Are you sure about that?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Probably not, I get it, just tweet at me. I see you. I hear you.\par \par \uc2 OK, so the timeline is completely incoherent here. We started just a couple days, and we got to four to five weeks. This morning Pete Hegseth says, as long as we need to succeed and it could be up to eight weeks. We are burning through a billion dollars a day. We are spending what is it --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Now you care?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Listen, just hear.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: About money?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: This is so -- it's so predictable.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Is that still more or less than the Somalians?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Oh. We'll get to that conversation. We're using $4 million missiles to take out $20,000 drones. That is a problem. They talked about that in the briefing yesterday, and Jennifer Griffin also talked about it.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: But that's what countries are doing, that's why drones are the future.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I understand they're the future, but we have --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It's not just our issue. That's everybody's issue.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: But it is our issue today, when you say that this is something that we can go in and we can be surgical and then we can get out, that's why everyone was actually OK in a bipartisan fashion with past things that President Trump has done, because they were actually surgical and short, like project --Operating Midnight Hammer.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I get it, OK. (INAUDIBLE). I mean, no, you don't have a problem with the results. You have always a problem about the process. That's all you have, because the results speak for themselves.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No, they don't, you also like --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Cut the head off. We left the body. That's like Venezuela.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I just said, you left a hundred new bodies in place --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: And they pop up and they blow up. They better have health and dental because no one's taking that job.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Pete Hegseth going back to the press just wants to hurt President Trump when they're talking about dead service members, look back at the coverage after Biden's disastrous evacuation of Afghanistan, and the coverage of those dead service members.\par \par \uc2 And I know that Pete was talking about that, and it is an important component, because there will be boots on the ground, and there will be more casualties, and all of these lives do matter.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Are you predicting boots on the ground?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well, they're saying it's certainly an option. Jim Comer was on T.V. today, saying it's likely.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You don't know if that's true or not, Jessica, you can't see into the future. No one knows what's going to happen.\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: Gregory, is it my time yet? It's been 84 years.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I'm afraid, Kennedy, we're out of time, but we'll have you on next show with the Amazing Kreskin. What's your take on this about on the boots on the ground, we're in the fog of war, any predictions right now are kind of silly