yer.\par \par \uc2 REP. TED LIEU (D-CA): Shame on you, if you had any decency, you would resign right after this hearing concludes.\par \par \uc2 BONDI: The DOW has shattered 50,000 for the first time. This is crazy. They said it couldn't be done in four years.\par \par \uc2 REP. JASMINE CROCKETT (D-TX): You're one of the worst attorneys general in history.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Crockett, all right, things might have been loud, but that didn't stop Congressman Jerry Nadler from getting a little shut eye. Yes. Video catching one of his aides nudging him to wake up. He had things to do. Wake up, Brian.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: I'm up. I -- just everything is devolving. The day before, you had Todd Lyons and Rodney Scott, they just were being screamed at the entire time.\par \par \uc2 I just like to ask everybody in the room, what is your job? I mean, is your job to solicit answers? Is your job to make progress? Are you looking to learn something? Are you just looking to raise money?\par \par \uc2 Because, OK, we're playing the clips, because it's so out of control and embarrassing. And the thing is, for the most part, you know, you had to Todd Lyons or Rodney Scott kind of sit back and take a lot of incoming that was totally unworthy, because a lot of that wasn't their policies at all. They were being yelled at for ICE, and they were mischaracterizing what ICE was doing for another time.\par \par \uc2 But hearing Pam Bondi, they're talking about the Epstein files. Let's be honest, the Epstein files have totally blown up in the Democrats face, two insincere lawmakers, Ro Khanna and Tom Massie, who sat on it for four years, had no interest when Joe Biden was president or Donald Trump was president the first time.\par \par \uc2 Now, all of a sudden, have to do it for the survivors. No one is talking about the survivors now. They're trying to see if they can get Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 And the only thing that came out of the last million 