par \par \uc2 And the big lie that they told over and over and over again, the borders closed, the borders secure. That was the mantra of the Biden, Harris, Mayorkas, you know, administration and their complicit allies in the media mob that never asked a question. They never dared raise the questions that needed to be asked.\par \par \uc2 Now, in response, DHS Secretary \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  issued this statement. Quote, I am recommending for a full travel ban on every damn country that's been flooding our nation with killers, leeches, and entitlement junkies. Our forefathers built this nation on blood, sweat, and the unyielding love of freedom. Not for foreign invaders to slaughter our heroes, suck dry our hard-earned tax dollars, and snatch the benefits owed to Americans. We don't want them. Not one.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, Democrats are now vilifying the very people trying to clean up Biden's disaster. They compared national guard soldiers on the streets of D.C. to what? See stormtroopers, Nazis, gestapo, brown shirts.\par \par \uc2 Democratic congresswoman, you know, now senator, Elisse Slotkin even suggesting that these service members were dangerous to the general public. Let me repeat that. That the National Guard soldiers are the danger to the general public.\par \par \uc2 Oh, is this not whipping people into a frenzy? Is this not demonizing them? Is this not dehumanizing them? Is this not inciteful rhetoric? You decide.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. ELISSA SLOTKIN (D-MI): When you look at these videos coming out of places like Chicago, it makes me incredibly nervous that we're about to see people in law enforcement, people in uniform military get nervous, get stressed, shoot at American civilians. It is very -- a very, very stressful situation for these law enforcement and for the communities on the ground.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By every single metric, safety in Washington, D.C. vastly has improved 