 VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Uh-huh. And what are you doing? You're creating chaos in terms of the president of the United States undermining his authority as commander- in-chief without identifying a single incident in which that occurred? Democrats are now vilifying Americans for simply working their hardest to make the country and the world a safer place, including ice agent who face attacks and threats and doxing and harassment every single solitary day.\par \par \uc2 We chronicle it almost every night on this program. Then you have \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , oh, well, if he has his way, ice agents can't put a mask on, but the people that protect him can. Oregon's attorney general is even threatening to prosecute ICE agents, the governor out there, for doing their job.\par \par \uc2 And make no mistake, this is important work. Just last week, another Afghan national arrested for making terroristic threats and bragging about building a bomb. This in Fort Worth, Texas. Thankfully, he was apprehended.\par \par \uc2 But mark my words, many more violent criminals who don't love our country, who have not been vetted, are still lurking in the shadows. We have seen innocent Americans murdered. We've seen innocent Americans raped. Innocent Americans victims of violent crime again and again.\par \par \uc2 And the hatred and the vitriol, you know, of reckless, dangerous, inciting rhetoric and dehumanization continues. It doesn't stop. Just like the same party, the party of love and the party of compassion, they couldn't stand for the family of Laken Riley during President Trump's joint session speech or the family of Jocelyn Nungaray, a little 12-year-old girl brutally raped and murdered by one of these unvetted illegal immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Can't applaud their families that have been through so much? You don't have a heart. You don't have a soul. You don't have a conscience.\par \par \uc2 Here with the full report, Kevin Corke is joining us.\par \par \uc2 Kevin, what's the latest?\par \par \uc2 KEVIN CORKE, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Listen, Sean, that was an amazing open to the program. And you're right, this is a troubling trend I'm going to tell you about. Another Afghan national, as you alluded to, brought to this country thanks to the Biden administration is threatening American life. But thankfully, in this case, as you pointed out, he was actually caught before he followed through on that threat.\par \par \uc2 Now, Texas court records show that Mohammad Dawood Alokozay was charged at the state level with making a terroristic threat. Now, this is after he posted a video of himself on TikTok indicating he was building a bomb with the intended target of the Fort Worth, Texas area. That again, according to DHS.\par \par \uc2 Now, Alokozay came to the U.S. as part of Operation Allies Welcome under the Biden administration, that effort to resettle Afghans following the disastrous withdrawal from that country back in the summer of 2021. Even more troubling, Alokozay was taken into custody, Sean, just one day before the awful shooting in Washington, D.C. that claimed the life of a young patriot named Sarah Beckstrom.\par \par \uc2 By the way, the other National Guard member and fellow patriot, Andrew Wolfe, he's still in critical condition, but said to be improving tonight. Our prayers are obviously with both families. As for the suspected shooter, well, he is facing one count of first degree murder, as well as three counts of possession of a firearm during a crime of violence and two counts of assault with intent to kill while armed.\par \par \uc2 No one cares about that guy except that he would get justice and be that in this life or the next -- Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Well said, Kevin. And I will see you tomorrow night in D.C. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 We are at the beginning of a very busy news night.\par \par \uc2 Here now with more on the left's violent rhetoric, inciteful rhetoric, dehumanizing rhetoric, along with the developing situation in Venezuela, and some very positive economic news -- it's time for the "Hannity" Washington briefing.\par \par \uc2 We welcome back -- White House Press Secretary Karoline Leavitt is with us.\par \par \uc2 Well, you know, you were very clear and strong in your remarks today. Let's talk about what we know and how dangerous it is and what the president is doing now to undo the damage that he inherited from Biden, Harris, Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 KAROLINE LEAVITT, WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: Well, sure. And thank you for having me, Sean.\par \par \uc2 And I think it speaks to how depraved the Democrat Party has become, that they are more angry at President Trump for deploying the National Guard to make D.C. the safest city in the world than they are at the foreign national terrorist from Afghanistan who ambushed two innocent patriotic national guardsmen in Washington, D.C. It's just despicable.\par \par \uc2 And your audience, the American public cannot forgive, nor can we forget what the Biden administration and Secretary Mayorkas and everybody involved did to our country for four long years. They allowed tens of millions of illegal aliens from all over this world to invade our country's borders and to infiltrate American communities. Many of these individuals were paroled into the country, many of them known terrorists.\par \par \uc2 We know, as Kevin Corke just reported, just a day before this shooting in Washington, D.C., there was another Afghan national who was caught making bomb threats in Texas. Remember, before the 2024 election, there was an Afghan national who was also caught for making bomb threats at election sites.\par \par \uc2 So, these are not people who should have ever been welcomed into our country.\par \par \uc2 And so, while President Trump has done everything in his executive power and through the One Big, Beautiful Bill legislatively to secure the border and that effort has been remarkably successful, we have had zero illegal aliens released into our country as a result of President Trump's effective policies over the past several months. But we must not forget, and we cannot turn a blind eye to the fact that there are still threats in the interior of our country who were allowed in and released in by the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 And so, that's why when the mainstream legacy media and those without a spine in our country say that President Trump's mass deportations have not gone far enough -- far enough, President Trump says no, they haven't gone far enough because we must deport every illegal alien who \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  allowed into this country.\par \par \uc2 And not only do these people serve as a national security threat, they are also draining the resources of American taxpayers. Look no further than the great state of Minnesota that has been run into the ground by Democrat leadership, Governor Walz who is completely incompetent. The Somali migration, invasion of Minneapolis where we now have fraud rings of Somali migrants who are stealing nearly $1 billion worth of taxpayer benefits in that city alone.\par \par \uc2 And don't take it from me. "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " of all places reported on that this week.\par \par \uc2 And so, we must be a country with laws. We must be a country with law and order. That's what President Trump and his entire national security team, Secretary Noem, Tom Homan, the entire White House is working on every day to restore.\par \par \uc2 And the American people cannot forget the four long years of wide-open borders that brought us to this point today.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Over 5,000 flagged for national security concerns. Over nearly 7,000 flagged for derogatory information which would be concerning. They were still allowed into the country.\par \par \uc2 We have -- according to reports -- 885 national security risks that are still at large in the country and that doesn't include the illegal immigration. Got -- known 