e-Sears is making an appeal to parents tying her opponent to controversial bathroom and locker room policies in Northern Virginia schools, running a new ad featuring a mother identified as Abby.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: My son shared urinals with a girl who claims she's a boy. My daughter competed against men in track and the transgender predator who exposed himself in school showers, sick. Spanberger wrote a law to make this stuff legal.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL (voice-over): Spanberger has not taken the charges on directly. The issue is big in this race after Richard Cox, a repeat sex offender, exposed himself to girls in school locker rooms and recreation centers, putting the political spotlight on lax bathroom and locker room policies in Northern Virginia.\par \par \uc2 VICTORIA COBB, PRESIDENT, THE FAMILY FOUNDATION OF VIRGINIA: Parents in Fairfax County are stunned that the prosecutor is not pursuing this. If a sexual predator income a vulnerable space with our young girls is not sufficient for the county to step in, we should consider it a lawless locality.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Cox is a biological male who identifies as a transgender woman. In this encounter with Fairfax County police, Cox claims his civil rights are being violated for being asked to leave a women's locker room. Current Republican Governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  was able to convert parental anger against local school boards into votes. So Earle-Sears is trying to follow that example in the final month of this campaign. Democratic nominee \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  is taking a page out of her party's playbook by hammering her GOP opponent over abortion.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: \uc2 Sears\uc2  wants a near total ban with no exception for rape and incest, and she supports making abortion a felony.\par \par \uc2 WINSOME EARLE-SEARS, (R) VIRGINIA GUBERNATORIAL NOMINEE: We know abortion is wicked. I am speaking.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO TAPE)\