empted murder, gang assault, and weapons possession. They are currently being held in Nassau County, New York.\par \par \uc2 ICE has lodged immigration detainers and will assume custody when those suspects are released from the New York justice system.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney in Los Angeles says enough is enough when it comes to dangerous street takeovers. The events have plagued Southern California for years. Correspondent Bill Melugin has details tonight from Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 BILL MELUGIN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT (voice over): It's 3:00 a.m. Saturday morning in downtown Los Angeles, a city plagued with street takeovers like this one.\par \par \uc2 Right in front of the home of the \uc2 Los Angeles Lakers\uc2 , hundreds of people block an intersection as drivers perform dangerous donuts while others throw fireworks into the intersection.\par \par \uc2 Angry neighbors shoot paint balls at cars parked along the street belonging to the spectators, and they are not the only ones fed up.\par \par \uc2 NATHAN HOCHMAN, DISTRICT ATTORNEY, LOS ANGELES COUNTY: My entire office is absolutely laser focused on going after these illegal street takeovers.\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN (voice over): New Los Angeles County District Attorney Nathan Hochman says he will pursue consequences for the drivers, including reckless driving charges and up to 90 days in jail, as well as the spectators, threatening jail time and a $500 fine just for watching.\par \par \uc2 HOCHMAN: If you want to go ahead and be one of these drivers in illegal straight takeovers, if you want to be spectators in illegal straight takeovers, we are going to hold you accountable. If you're a driver and you want to see that car crushed, literally crushed, as we impound it, go ahead and test us.\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN (voice over): These street takeovers have turned deadly before. In 2022, nursing student Elyzza Guajaca was killed on Christmas day in South