rom Oversight Chairman James Comer. We'll see if they will actually back what Trump floated earlier, which is an extension to his 30 days.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Quickly, Juan?\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: Well, I think it's a slam dunk for Trump politically to say that Democrats are soft on crime. We know that formula works to stir up his base. But I would also remind people this, that conservatives have historically said we believe in local government and states' rights, and we think government is most effective when it's close to the people. And what he is doing is canceling out -- the District has made mistakes on crime. Olivia referred to this. But it's the people who live here, who have the right to make mistakes and govern themselves. And he has just totally abrogated that authority. I think it's not American.\par \par \uc2 CONTINETTI: But the governance in the District is the \uc2 United States congress\uc2 , which delegated the authority to Trump, and he is using that power wisely.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: OK, we'll see where it goes. Panel, thanks.\par \par \uc2 And finally tonight, a SPECIAL REPORT salute.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Come on. Get some air, get some air.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Get on the ground! Get on the ground!\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Check out this video, a dramatic rescue by the Tampa police department caught on body camera footage. Officers rushing to the scene, bursting through a gate, saving a man's life, pulling him from a burning home. They ended up crawling their way to that trapped man. They pulled him out by his legs. Everybody made it out of that house alive and well. Our salute to them.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow on SPECIAL REPORT, we'll get you ready for Friday's U.S.-Russia summit, breaking down where things stand on the battlefield. We'll also have analysis from FOX News senior strategic analyst retired General Jack Keane. I will travel with President Trump on A