mp and his family, you know Trump, knowing Trump will never forget that. That doesn't mean that \uc2 Jamie Dimon\uc2  is going to get -- he's the CEO of \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 , one of the banks that debanked him because of January 6th. It was part of my exclusive reporting in the New York Post. But he's not going to indict Jamie. He's not going to indict \uc2 Brian Moynihan\uc2 . He's always going to look at him a little different. If they ever need a favor, they ain't getting one, and I think that's a bad position to be in if you're a highly regulated bank with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, not -- not smart, and I love how \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  decided he was going to sue the banks for what they did to him, and he did that last March.\par \par \uc2 GASPARINO: Right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We loved your reporting on this, Charlie. Thank you so much for joining us. And coming up, MAGA on the moon. Acting \uc2 NASA\uc2  Administrator, what other job can he have, \uc2 Sean Duffy\uc2  has the details on our next mission.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: When you heard about the Trump administration's plan to green light the building of a nuclear power plant on the moon, you probably either rolled your eyes or said they're doing what? But actually, the idea was first proposed during the first Trump administration, but now the entire project is being expedited.\par \par \uc2 The idea is that nuclear energy systems in space can help our astronauts and research as they keep exploring deeper into space, where solar, of course, isn't available. And of course, we know Trump always thinks big, and although Biden was a space cadet himself, his people didn't make space dominance a priority. But to Trump, the idea of America being beaten by the Russians and Chinese anywhere, including space, is anathema.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: For too many years, our dreams of exploration and discovery were really squandered by politics and bureaucracy, and we knocked that out. We don't want China and Russia and other countries leading us. We've always led.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to defending America, it is not enough to merely have an American presence in space. We must have American dominance in space.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, love it, love it, love it. Here with me exclusively is interim \uc2 NASA\uc2  administrator and transportation secretary, \uc2 Sean Duffy\uc2 . Mr. Secretary, great to see you. Now, I think a lot of people who saw this headline were skeptical. How are we going to do this? And again, why is this so important?\par \par \uc2 SEAN DUFFY\uc2 , TRANSPORTATION SECRETARY: So first off, it's a little bit of clickbait for liberals and they were saying we're have nuclear warheads on the moon and they just misrepresented the story. You mentioned that Trump brought this up in Trump 1. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was studying this during his administration as well. And so, enough of the studies, hundreds of millions of dollars. Let's move, Laura.\par \par \uc2 So, on the moon, I don't think a lot of people realize there's ice. Ice means water. We do have some solar, but if you want sustainable life on the moon, you need an energy source. So, we're going to bring fission to the moon's surface to power our base. It makes complete sense.\par \par \uc2 Now some might say, well, the launch is somewhat complicated, right? These are not active. They're not live. When we launch them into space, we can do it safely. By the way, we have submarines and aircraft carriers that operate on nuclear energy as well. But this is a key component. If we're going to get to the moon and then get to the Mars, we're going to have to figure this technology out.\par \par \uc2 And again, we have to beat the Russians, the Chinese, I think, to get to the Moon first. If you lead in space, you lead on Earth.\par \par \uc2