ications that attacked \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  obsessively, but those publications don't determine who the president is, the American people do, and \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  is the person who determines who his cabinet is, not these publications that I think frankly have lost relevance.\par \par \uc2 BRENNAN: This is a country founded by immigrants.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well this is a country founded by --\par \par \uc2 BRENNAN: This is a unique country.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: This is a very unique country and it was founded by some immigrants and some settlers but just because we were founded by immigrants doesn't mean that 240 years later, that we have to have the dumbest immigration policy in the world.\par \par \uc2 BRENNAN: These people are vetted.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Just like the guy who planned a terrorist attack in Oklahoma a few months ago? He was allegedly properly vetted and many people in the media and the Democratic Party said that he was properly vetted. Clearly, he wasn't. I don't want my children to share a neighborhood with people who are not properly vetted and because I don't want it for my kids, I'm not going to force any other American citizens' kids to do that either.\par \par \uc2 BRENNAN: No, and that was a very particular case. It wasn't clear if he was radicalized when he got here or while he was living here.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: I don't really care, Margaret. I don't want that person in my country and I think most Americans agree with me.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Here with reaction, FOX News contributor Joe Concha, the host of "Tomi Lahren is Fearless" on Outkick, and the new FOX Nation weekly special "A Hundred Days with Tomi Lahren".\par \par \uc2 Welcome both of you.\par \par \uc2 Tomi, we start with you. You know, for nine years, I look at the media. They threw everything they had at this guy and the American people heard it., They rejected it and they lost. They peddled every lie, they peddled every conspiracy theory, and they lost.\par \par \uc2 And now,, it's -- see -- now they -- now they've lost their audiences and now they just doubled down on all that they know, hating Trump 24/7, doubling down on stupid which I'm actually fine with because that that increases the odds that my ratings go up.\par \par \uc2 TOMI LAHREN, OUTKICK HOST: Well, listen, Sean, there's something that the young Gen Z folks say. They say get out and touch grass and that's exactly what some of these legacy media so-called anchors need to do. They need to get out. They need to interact with everyday Americans, maybe come to Tennessee, maybe go to Florida, maybe go somewhere in the Midwest, and actually talk to Americans out there that voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and are quite pleased with what he's doing.\par \par \uc2 The approval rating which CNN had to admit to themselves is higher than it's ever been, and that's actually unheard of for a president in his second term and albeit in the second week of his presidency.\par \par \uc2 So I think also when we're talking about those clips of face the nation, I do hope the American people were tuning into to that segment even if they're not watching that network on a regular basis because what Vice President J.D. Vance did is really school that network and the viewers they have left on the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 And when she's saying, oh, we don't know if this person was radicalized before they came to our country illegally or after the fact, that reminds me of on ABC News when Martha Raddatz prior to the election said, only a couple of apartment complexes are being taken over by violent criminal alien gangs. It's quite obvious that they don't interact with average everyday Americans, but perhaps they should. It might do them good.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Nine years, they through every lie, every conspiracy theory. They never reported on any of his failures. They lose, Joe Concha, and then they double down on dumb and stupid. Okay, I'm fine with it.\par \par \uc2 JOE CONCHA, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yeah, and look at what we've seen over the past seven days, Sean, during the president's first week, I mean, it's been one craptastic narrative after the other. I definitely picked the wrong week to stop sniffing glue.\par \par \uc2 I mean, first, there were the salute truthers when it came to \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and that alleged Nazi salute that even the \uc2 ADL\uc2  says was no such thing. I mean, Musk only visited Auschwitz last year and denounced antisemitism without ambiguity, but that never made its way into the reporting for some reason.\par \par \uc2 I guess when you're on the wrong side of every issue and you can't talk policy, these kinds of Hail Marys are all Democrats and are allies in the media have. And then there was a few anchors on cable and broadcast news demanding to know why, including Margaret Brennan, why Trump hasn't lowered the cost of groceries and eggs yet. I mean, after all, it has been a whole days since the inauguration and yet the expectation is that four years of rapid inflation can be fixed with an executive order in one week -- go ahead, I'm sorry.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Hey, no, no, Joe, I want people to know what you're talking about, that literally -- well, you promised on day one, the prices would be down, and I'm like, what are you talking -- these people are so dumb. I'm like, all right, let's get our economic policies in place, yes. Let's get energy prices down, let's produce more and that's their argument at this point?\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  didn't the price of eggs -- well, we've got you know, the chicken flu, avian flu going on, whatever that is.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Yeah, that's right. It begs the question, Sean -- yeah, that's right, it begs the question. Do stupid people ever hit a point in life when they realize that they're actually stupid?\par \par \uc2 And finally, speaking of stupid, there was coffee gate that the panic and fearmongering over Trump threatening the country of Colombia with heavy tariffs and then liberals losing their collective minds over their \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  being more expensive. Well, after about five minutes of resistance, Colombia's president as we know completely capitulated the threat worked, and the media threw a pie in its own face again. I mean, there's more examples here, Sean, but we only got finite time as you know.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me, last word, Tomi, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says tariff, let me interpret this for the media that clearly does not want to understand him, that is the first lobby in the beginning of a negotiation. Am I right or wrong?\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Right.\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: You're exactly right, and it's incredibly effective which is what Joe just discussed. I think it was a couple of hours before we saw a complete reversal. Colombia wanted to be the big dog in the park and then they realized that they weren't, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  quickly reminded them, probably while he was golfing by the way which is also iconic. They're not doing the Democrat Party any favors, the legacy media, because the Democrat, elected officials and politicians are watching this and they're thinking that they have a chance and they simply don't. Go out and talk to real Americans.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's actually getting entertaining to be honest, to watch them lose their minds and go right back, revert to form, and go right back to Nazi, Hitler, Stalin, Mussolini, racist. I mean, it's like a broken record, put it on a loop.\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, all right, first, \uc2 PETA\uc2  was coming for college football mascots. Now, they want to put an end to another beloved animal tradition. We'll explain, and they want to put me on a plant-based diet. Let's see if they can convince me, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. The American tradition of Groundhog Day is just around the corner and \uc2 PETA\uc2  is pushing to make a major change to the beloved holiday. In a news release last week, the animal rights organization -- organization suggesting that Punxsutawney Phil, that's the groundhog who predicts weather, there will be -- whether it's going to be a long winter or early spring and the star of the show, be replaced by a, quote, weather reveal cake, similar to a popular gender reveal cake trend.\par \par \uc2 PETA\uc2  cited that groundhogs are shy animals who actively avoid humans and criticize the exploited use of Punxsutawney Phil as a, quote, a town's once a year fake meteorologist.\par \par \uc2 Here with more, \uc2 PETA\uc2  spokesperson Ashley Byrne.\par \par \uc2 By the way, last time you were on, we -- we went long in the previous segment. I did not cut you off early as some in the press had said. We're glad to have you back.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I have a question before we get started -- before we get started, do you support any limitations on abortion?\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY BYRNE, PETA COMMUNICATIONS DIRECTOR: You know, \uc2 PETA\uc2  doesn't take a stance on abortion any more than Operation Rescue takes a stance on veganism.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, wait a minute, but you care about, you know, ethical treatment of animals, do you support any restrictions on late term abortion? This was -- this would be months seven, eight and nine, when a child is viable outside a mother's womb on its own. Do you support -- do you support that practice?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: We represent people -- we represent people on both sides of that issue. We are not a political organization. We're nonpartisan.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I didn't ask you. You care so much about animals. I'm wondering you care about human animals?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Of course, we care about humans and we represent humans on both sides of the abortion issue.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So a viable child you don't care that could live outside a mother's womb, you don't care about that person?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: You know, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , Operation Rescue, no one asks them what their stance on animal rights is.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You don't have the courage to say that a viable child inside a mother's womb that could live outside the womb is a life that should be protected but you're worried about a groundhog. That doesn't make sense.\par \par \uc2 I have another question.\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So okay my understanding is that you communicate to my staff that you want me to be on a plant-based diet. Is that true?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: We would love to send you a plant-based meal so that you could see how delicious vegan be.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What's going to be in it?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: You know, I'm not sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Juicy steak.\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: You know, there is actually there is delicious juicy vegan keto steak that we could send you. It's fabulous.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: A what steak?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: It's a -- it's a vegan steak. You know, Sean, I used to love steak.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: A vegan steak. I'm sure it's great.\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: I used -- I used to love rare bloody steak and the vegan steak now are fantastic.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's delicious.\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: It really is.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, let me ask you a question. i have a serious question.\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Uh-hmm.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Is a plant a living -- is -- are plants living?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Of course.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay. So you want to send me a murdered plant?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Well, you know, every time you eat an animal, you eat the product of far more murdered plants. You need to feed an animal a lot of plants to get a tiny bit of meat. I love that you care so much about plants rights, but --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I mean --\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: That's -- it's just basic math.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Listen, one of the reasons they couldn't get California water and this is not a joke is because of a plant they were protecting, that is endangered.\par \par \uc2 All right. Let's go to the groundhog --\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Well, the other reason is the dairy industry which sucks up so much of their water.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Well, I'll tell you what? I'll try your plant-based diet if you eat a medium rare steak that I send you.\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: You know, Sean, I ate many medium rare steaks in the past. I'm very happy with my vegan steak now, and like I said, we'd love to send you one.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'll give you one more.\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: I would never do that because I know that cows picking and screaming to their deaths.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I eat the steak. --I mean, I'll eat the plant-based steak garbage whatever you're going to send me and you eat my steak.\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Sean, a cow goes kicking and screaming to her death to make that steak. I don't want anything to do with that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You don't want anything to do -- well, how do you know plants don't feel pain?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: You know, again, first of all, plants don't have a central nervous system. They don't scream when you cut them. And again you have to feed a lot of plants to an animal to get a very small amount of meat. So if you're concerned about hurt -- if you're concerned about hurting plants, you still want to go vegan..\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, not really I think god gave us dominion over the animals and I believe they were put on this earth for our use, and that's my belief.\par \par \uc2 All right. Last question --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Sean, I've been -- I've been -- I've been reading the bible my entire life and don't you think that dominion implies some responsibility as opposed to the way we desecrate God's creation in slaughter houses and on factory farms, living in their own waste --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When Jesus told the apostles to drop the nets and the nets get filled with fish --\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Confined so they can't turn around.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- are you saying Jesus murdered the fish?\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: I think that Jesus would look at a -- at an animal who can't turn around in a gestation crate and would not be okay with it. It goes against all --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He fed the crowds --\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: Yes, but --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- fish and loaves.\par \par \uc2 BYRNE: But a pig farm is a desecration of God's creation.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm out of -- all right, your interpretation of the bible.\par \par \uc2 More "Hannity" straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. That's all the time we have left this evening. As always, thank you for being with us. Thank you for making the show possible. Please set your DVR so you never, ever, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 I've got some good news. In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled, Greg Gutfeld is standing by to put a smile on your face. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020250128el1r00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Climate Fanatics Vs. President Trump; Trump's Message To Davos: America Is Back; Trump's ICE Raids Have Begun; Trump pardons 23 pro-lifers; Husband of pardoned pro-lifer joins the Angle; Movie about sex change gets 13 Oscars nomination; Justin Baldoni, Blake Lively lawsuit gets messier; Common sense is back in America; New woke phrase alert, non-transgender women\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Laura Ingraham, Bill Melugin, Raymond Arroyo, Charlie  Hurt \par \uc2 6,983 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 January 2025\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 VIQ Solutions, Inc. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: Tomorrow on Special Report, we mentioned President Trump visits disaster areas in North Carolina and California. Remember, if you can't catch us live, set your DVR, 06:00 p.m. in the East, 03:00 p.m. on the West Coast. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight, and every night. That's it for this Special Report. Fair, balanced and still unafraid. The Ingraham Angle starts now.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle, and thank you, as always, for joining us. Trump zooms Davos. That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 The Bond villain behind the elite's annual gathering in Davos is obviously nervous. Klaus Schwab kicked off the annual confab by trying to reassure attendees that they still run the show.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KLAUS SCHWAB, EXECUTIVE CHAIRMAN, THE \uc2 WORLD ECONOMIC FORUM\uc2 : The world faces critical challenges, extreme weather events, misinformation and disinformation, increasing divisions within societies, within countries. The future is shaped by us, and particularly shaped by us here in this room.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Shaped by us in the room. Warnings of disinformation. Can't make this up. This is the epitome of uninformed arrogance, but he's just another globalist Mastodon on the verge of extinction. But still, let's compare the response to Trump at the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  in his first term to how he was received today. It was quite something to behold.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SCHWAB: Of course, I'm aware that your strong leadership is open to misconceptions and biased interpretations. Therefore, it is so essential for us in the room to listen directly to you. The importance of American leadership and your personal leadership is fundamental and paramount. We are here to hear your mission and policies related to revitalizing the economy and addressing the global challenges.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, so it goes from tolerating Trump at Davos, that first soundbite, to kind of well, acknowledging grudgingly that he's a force to be reckoned with. It's quite the change in tone. But this morning, Trump treated his Davos appearance kind of like a \uc2 Zoom\uc2  call with a message to clueless Klaus.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I'm pleased to report that America is also a free nation, once again, on day one, I signed an executive order to stop all government censorship. No longer will our government label the speech of our own citizens as misinformation or disinformation, which are the favorite words of censors and those who wish to stop the free exchange of ideas and frankly, progress.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It was so refreshing to watch from beginning to end. It was Trump's message stood really in stark contrast to the Davos dimwitz on almost every issue. And remember, they are not going to stop fighting as much as they can to destroy gas powered cars. The entire oil and gas industry.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANTONIO GUTERRES\uc2 , SECRETARY GENERAL, UNITED NATIONS: Our fossil fuel addiction is a Frankenstein monster sparing nothing and no one. All around us, we see clear signs that the monster has become master.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Lofty rhetoric, but the real monster scenario is found in the world where they have all the power, and individuals in free nations are forced to submit, while Trump's going to have none of that.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I terminated the ridiculous and incredibly wasteful Green New Deal. I call it the Green New Scam, withdrew from the one sided Paris Climate Accord and ended the insane and costly electric vehicle mandate. The United States has the largest amount of oil and gas of any country on earth, and we're going to use it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Green heads were exploding from the Swiss Alps to China. Of course, China is banking on its ability to totally annihilate the American automobile industry by sucking us all into electric vehicles. Now on trade, Trump was just as blunt.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: The EU treats us very, very unfairly, very badly. They don't take our -- essentially, don't take our farm products, and they don't take our cars. Yet, they send cars to us by the millions. They put tariffs on things that we want to do. We have, you know, hundreds of billions of dollars of deficits with the EU and nobody is happy with it, and we're going to do something about it, but nobody is happy with it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The agenda is now and always will be, America first.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : My message to every business in the world is very simple, come make your product in America and we will give you among the lowest taxes of any nation on earth. But if you don't make your product in America, which is your prerogative, then, very simply, you will have to pay a tariff.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But it wasn't just business issues tackled at Davos, the gender benders. They're also panicking that they're losing power. Now, who knew it was a global priority to protect drag shows.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SARAH KATE ELLIS\uc2 , PRESIDENT, \uc2 GLAAD\uc2 : What we've enacted is free speech for algorithms, not free speech for citizens. We're seeing an uptick in violence in the United States against LGBTQ people, everything from attacks at drag shows to trans women being murdered on the street.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And once again, Trump beamed in and laid waste to that insanity.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: My administration has taken action to abolish all discriminatory Diversity, Equity and Inclusion nonsense. America will once again become a merit-based country.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: My favorite part, though, is when he chose to address the CEO of \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  directly. Now, remember the bank had shared account holders information after January 6th, and then flat out denied that other conservative businesses access to their services was even happening, they thought, oh no, everybody is getting access.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And I don't know if the regulators mandated that because of Biden or what, but you and Jamie and everybody, I hope you're going to open your banks to conservatives, because what you're doing is wrong.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Of course, \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  claims nothing nefarious ever happened. But the fact is, the globalist titans of industry and politics and media, they gather at Davos, and they're never going to be comfortable with what Trump represents. They might put on a good act, but never will they accept it. An America that is unapologetic, an America that is bold, an America that sometimes brash. They don't want that, but too bad, because Trump has all the momentum. He returned from the political grave to win the presidency, and he is inspiring, not just our own citizens, but those seeking a better life across the globe.\par \par \uc2 Now, over the weekend, I had the chance to chat with Italian President \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  and watched the buzz around Argentina's reformer President \uc2 Javier Milei\uc2 . I met populist politicians from Sweden, from Poland and the Czech Republic. All of them, all of them are thrilled about our new American president.\par \par \uc2 So eight years ago, Trump was a speed bump on the way to global control. Today, he is the prophet of pragmatism. We all felt more connected than ever. We all feel more connected than ever. Thanks, in large part, also to social media. Think about it. What on earth would we do without \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and X? Why do you think the Davos big wigs are so keen on censorship? Trump's \uc2 Zoom\uc2  message to all of them, all of them who thought America was on our heels, who profited off the decline of the American worker is clear.\par \par \uc2 Your schemes to control us, to censor us, to rip us off, to shame us are over. You're officially on notice, and that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Victor Davis Hanson, Senior Fellow at the \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2  and Batya Ungar-Sargon, News Week opinion editor. Victor, let's start with you. What do they fear most at Davos, about Trump?\par \par \uc2 VICTOR DAVIS HANSON, SENIOR FELLOW, HOOVER INSTITUTION: Well, that was very strange, because the Davos people that run it, he shredded every, every one of their most cherished ideas, you know, of open borders, illegal immigration, new Green Deal, he just shredded. I thought their heads were going to explode when he called it the new green scam. And he called oil liquid gold.\par \par \uc2 So I thought the questions were going to be so angry, but, you know, I looked at them very carefully after I heard them on the transcript, and Schwarzman and Moynihan, all these international big bankers were kind of like, well, we're not supposed to say this, but are you serious? You're really going to give us liquid natural gas? You're not going to cut it off.\par \par \uc2 Trump said, no, my word is my bond, I will give it to you. Are you really serious that you're going to encourage investment? And it was almost like what he did with the tech lords on the domestic area. He, you know, when he got in Andreessen and he got Elon and Bezos, and he basically said, I want you to make us rich. Go to it. And they thought, wow, we're not supposed to like this, but it's great. And these bankers were kind of shocked, like we're Davos people. We're supposed to get angry.\par \par \uc2 But the more we hear this, and I know it's a little over the top, they thought, but it's wow. He's going to let us make money, and we're going to have capitalism free and the United States is going to really back us up and give us all the liquid natural gas we want, and there's going to be -- I got the impression that the Davos people that run it were pretty shocked that he won over the people who were asking him the questions would basically, are the world's financiers? I think they're actually secretly happy that he's there because they understand that he's a capitalist and he's -- yes, he's our capitalist green.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I just love the fact that he zoomed in, I was just like, treating it like any other office meeting Batya. That just cracked me up. The screen above the crowd, it was like Charlie's Angels disembodied, but the Spanish Prime Minister, Perez -- Pedro Sanchez, excuse me, he talked about the digital identity wallet, the European digital identity wallet. Let's listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PEDRO SANCHEZ, PRIME MINISTER, SPAIN: We are allowing people to roam freely on social networks without linking their profiles to a real identity. If we must push forward the principle of pseudonymity as the functioning element of social media and force all these platforms to link every user account to a European digital identity wallet.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Batya explain what that would be in the age of the new tech world that we live in. What would that be? A digital identity? What's the problem with that?\par \par \uc2 BATYA UNGAR-SARGON, JOURNALIST: Sorry, that's not going to fly here. This is the land of the free and the home of the brave. What we just oversaw was the total capitulation of the global elites to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the tribune of the American working class, the same people who have endlessly mocked him and laughed at him and booed him and tried to destroy him are now on their knees Laura, begging for a scrap of his approval. And the reason for that is what you led with. They are terrified of him because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's vision that nation states must exist, that national borders are crucial, and that a nation owes something to its citizens.\par \par \uc2 This view has simply triumphed over their view that you can endlessly pillage the middle class and the working class economically and culturally. They think you measure the health of an economy based on how many private jets a billionaire has, and Trump thinks you measure the health of an economy based on whether that billionaire's cleaning lady and plumber can afford to buy a home. And it's \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's nationalism that is winning the day. Thank God. You love to see it. It is just delicious.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, one thing is for sure, Victor, a lot of those elites gathered at Davos, their ideas were responsible for wrecking the world, whether it was foreign policy, non-stop wars, open borders, they're still pushing for unfettered migration and support for migration, the handling of the pandemic, the lies about gain-of-function. I mean, what haven't they wrecked, frankly, except their own portfolios.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: Well, their suicidal. Europe is suicidal. When the EU was formed, their GDP was almost like ours, and now we're almost double. And they did that through a national collective suicide. But again, I think all of these Davos masters were a little shocked because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  talked over their heads, and he appealed to the innate logic of these capitalist bankers, and he's basically saying, you know, I like you guys, but you don't understand who's your friend and what's in your interest. And it's the MAGA, and I'm here to help you, join us, because I wouldn't want you to suffer if you don't, and you will suffer just like you did to yourself.\par \par \uc2 And that's a very powerful argument. I think the Davos shepherds thought that the sheep are going, you know, wandering away from their control to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I think he won a lot of people over, even with that tough talk, and they didn't like it, but the bunkers and the financiers and the international people loved it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, what was hilarious to watch close up was \uc2 Javier Milei\uc2  in that St. John Church on Inauguration Day for the service in the morning. You know, if people were just flocking to him, and he walked by the Vice Premier of China, right, who nobody paid any attention to. People were just -- Meloni and Milei, people just wanted to be close to. I think we have a soundbite from Javier. Let's watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JAVIER MILEI\uc2 , PRESIDENT, ARGENTINA (VIA TRANSLATOR): Slowly what once seemed like the absolute global hegemony of the woke Left in politics, educational institutions, in the media, in supernational organizations, or even in forums that Davos has begun to crumble, and the hope for the ideas of freedom is starting to emerge.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Batya, real quickly on that. I mean, he, \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 , the rest of these populist leaders are the future.\par \par \uc2 UNGAR-SARGON: They absolutely are, Laura, and the reason for that is because they love the people that they represent. The elites absolutely hate the working class. They have so much contempt for them. And you can tell when a leader loves the people and serves the people. That is what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  represents is this return of service. I am here to represent what the people elected me to do.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, well, and they'll raise the boogeyman of disinformation and misinformation, as Klaus Schwab has done, and the fact that Trump went right at that today was just -- that was just music to my ears. I could have watched that all day long, Victor, Batya both, thank you so much. And coming up, Republicans alr