en. It's like the nomenclature about illegal aliens, that's changed too. But what's it going to be next?\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, CO-HOST, FOX & FRIENDS WEEKEND: Exactly. You know, I thought it was inappropriate to misgender other people, but apparently that's what this lawyer, who is, I don't know whether male or female, is doing by coming up with this whole new gender.\par \par \uc2 But you know, who ever thought that we would need an executive order to basically lay out what any child in the second grade knows, which is there are two genders. Nothing wrong with, you know -- obviously, there are a lot of people who are confused as we have seen, but forcing the rest of us to bow to their confusion is insanity.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Charlie, as we're finding out, the more we look into it, a lot of kids become confused in public schools, and private schools for that matter. And a lot of parents speaking out about that, whatever people want to call it, grooming or propaganda or gender bending. But kids hear a lot of stuff in school that is not related to reading, writing, and arithmetic.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is going to have to figure out if there's a way for the federal government to gradually start defunding the schools that continue to do this.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Yeah, and of course, it's not, you know, we're talking public schools here. Public schools have gotten in on it. You know, obviously the universities have gotten in on it, and it is propaganda. And you do enough of it, and people start to, it starts to affect people, especially people who are already sort of vulnerable in that department.\par \par \uc2 And you know, in Northern Virginia, just this week, a sex offender, registered sex offender, was arrested hanging out in a girl's locker room at a swimming pool without any of his clothes on because he was claiming that he was somehow a woman. And it took the school district like a week to go and arrest the person, the man, because they didn't know what to do.\par \par \uc2 This is the kind of insanity that I think just shows that the left has gone so far over the edge that it takes something like an executive order from the president to say, look, enough of this nonsense. And I think that the popularity for this is going to only grow because I think that we've scratch the surface of frustration that most normal people have about this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Charlie, bingo, and it's why, as you've talked about before, it's why private schools, Christian schools, homeschooling, online schooling is taking off all across this country. Charlie, as always, thank you. Great to see you. All right, that's it for us tonight. Make sure to follow me on social media. Jesse Watters is next.\par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020250124el1n00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Forget China, Democrats Focus On Smears; California Desperately Needs A Return To Common Sense; California Leadership Can't Be Trusted To Manage Aid; Laura Ingraham And Sen. Tuberville Discuss Hegseth Senate Confirmation Hearing; Ingraham Discusses Issue On \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2 ; Hegseth and Warren In A Catfight At Hegseth Confirmation Hearing\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Laura Ingraham, Jimmy Failla \par \uc2 7,589 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 January 2025\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 VIQ Solutions, Inc. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: Remember, if you can't catch us live, set your DVR, 06:00 p.m. in the East, 03:00 p.m. on the West Coast. You can follow me on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and X @bretbaier. All kinds of stuff on there. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this Special Report. Fair, balanced, and still unafraid. The Ingraham Angle is now.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. As always, thank you for joining us. Swamp whine, that's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 Now what makes official Washington nervous, especially the bureaucracy protectors in the Democrat Party are true change agents. People with guts, people with determination to challenge the status quo.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETE HEGSETH, DEFENSE SECRETARY-ELECT: Two months ago, 77 million Americans gave President Trump a powerful mandate for change, to put America First at home and abroad. I don't have a similar biography to Defense Secretaries of the last 30 years, but as President Trump also told me, we've repeatedly placed people atop the Pentagon with supposedly the right credentials, and where has it gotten us? He believes, and I humbly agree, that it's time to give someone with dust on his boots the helm. A change agent.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Then children and small dogs had to cover their ears because the sound from the Democrats and the committee was classic. I think it was kind of an unpleasant mix of resignation and bitterness. We bring you the swamp whine.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes or no, did you lead an audit.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: And the way my leadership has been stated --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes or no, did you lead an audit, yes or not, what are you afraid of, you can't answer this question. Yes or no, did you lead an audit? Do you not know this answer?\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: Senator, every part of my leadership of these organization has been misrepresented --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, or no. Yes, or no, did you lead an audit? I will take that as a no.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: You said in your statement you don't want politics in the DOD, everything you've said in these public statements is politics. I don't want women. I don't want moms. What's wrong with a mom, by the way, once you have babies, you therefore are no longer able to be lethal.\par \par \uc2 SEN. ELIZABETH WARREN (D-MA): You're quite sure that every general who serves should not go directly into the defense industry for 10 years. You're not willing to make that same pledge.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: I'm not a general, Senator.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, to watch the Democrats, it was painful to watch that. But look at the bright side. Hegseth hasn't even been sworn in yet, and he's already discovered a new technique for enhanced interrogation. Let's just force all those high value prisoners still at Gitmo, the few that are left to listen to this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I like that Angus King from Maine, he looks, get me out of here. All right. Well, they're all screeching because they all know Pete Hegseth is going to be confirmed. So today was purely political theater.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Denigrated. You have also denigrated members of the LGBTQ community,\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, well, they loathe Hegseth, because instead of being a puppet of the hill, Hegseth will actually implement Trump's policies. Now, that will be a market change from the first Trump administration, when the military leadership and senior aides often resisted Trump's agenda. They were roadblocks to it. \uc2 Fiona Hill\uc2 , senior Trump White House aide. Remember, she had worked for \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  and Obama. She's still fighting Trump.\par \par \uc2 And of course, there's the neocon chimney sweep, \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , who's batting, you know, zero on most of his predictions. And then there is Alexander Vindman, who triggered the first Trump impeachment. He's a hero on the Left. And there were the generals, Milley, McMaster, and Mattis. They were all highly credentialed, served their country proudly, highly educated and often spectacularly wrong. But setting aside their post 2020 nastiness, it often seems like they thought they were the commanders-in- chief, not Trump, like they felt that they knew more than he did.\par \par \uc2 But really, they're all just stuck in a cold war mentality. The fact is, America, even with our selfless brave troops, has not been able to win a major war outright since World War II. Think about it as wild, trillions of dollars in spending, then we lose thousands of our best troops in Iraq and Afghanistan, fight essentially to a draw, forever wars that triggered new problems.\par \par \uc2 And instead of talking about the need and examining all of this, need for real military reform, instead of preparing to work with President Trump on ways to make our Pentagon more efficient, the best Senate Democrats could do today was fringe fear-mongering and gotcha nonsense.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Did you take your staff, including young female staff members to a strip club?\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: Absolutely not. Anonymous smears.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: So you can't tell me whether someone who has committed a sexual assault is disqualified from being Secretary of Defense.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: Senator, I know in my instance, and I'm talking about my instance only, it was a false claim.\par \par \uc2 SEN. MAZIE HIRONO (D-HI): Will you resign as Secretary of Defense?\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: I've made this commitment on behalf of the men and women I'm serving.\par \par \uc2 HIRONO: I'm not hearing --\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: Because it's the most important deployment of my life.\par \par \uc2 HIRONO: Not hearing an answer to my questions. So I'm going to move on.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Flipping pages then Senator \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2  came in for the slam dunk.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 MARKWAYNE MULLIN\uc2  (R-OK): How many senators have showed up drunk to vote at night? Have any of you guys asked him to step down and resign for their job? And don't tell me you haven't seen it, because I know you have. And then how many senators do you know have got a divorce before cheating on their wives? Did you ask them to step down? No, but it's for show.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Ouch, and of course, it would not be a Senate confirmation hearing without the liberal female senators obsessing on their favorite subject, abortion.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HIRONO: Current DOD policy allows servicemembers and eligible dependents to be reimbursed for travel associated with non-covered reproductive health care, including abortions. Will you maintain this common sense policy?\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: Senator, I've always been personally pro-life. I know President Trump has as well, and we will review all policies, but our standard is whatever the President wants on this particular issue. My advice I will take a look at.\par \par \uc2 HIRONO: So, if the President tells you that --\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: I don't believe the --\par \par \uc2 HIRONO: -- policy will not be maintained. You will not enable our servicemembers to seek reproductive care. So --\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: I don't believe the federal government should be funding --\par \par \uc2 HIRONO: I'm not hearing answers to my question, Mr. Chairman.\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: -- for abortion.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You ever wonder for a second when you watch these hearings. If, I mean, we watch them so you don't have to, but when you're watching these hearings, and you wonder what would happen if they lost their pages in front of them. I mean, I have to read a teleprompter, right? But I write, write my script. But if, if you haven't written your questions and you rely on an aide to write your questions, what happens when the papers go away? They just should take away all papers and let the whole thing go that way for a while. That would be fun to watch.\par \par \uc2 But I mean I'm sorry that's lazy Mazie Hirono. In a Trump administration, abortion will not be considered a core mission of our military. Thank you very much. And Republicans on the committee focused on the issues that actually matter, China, our cyber security, all the things that our military needs to get a handle on. So let's be clear, the reason Democrats oppose Hegseth has zero to do with his personal foibles or even his managerial skills. They want to stop him because he will implement Trump's agenda. Period. Which includes a Pentagon Accountability Project.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: Accountability is coming, because everybody in this room knows, if you're a rifleman and you lose your rifle, they're throwing the book at you. But if you're a general who loses a war, you get a promotion, that's not going to happen in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's Pentagon.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And what else won't happen, a Pentagon that worries about fighting climate change more than fighting our enemies.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: My Secretary of the Navy, should I be confirmed, sir, will not be focused on climate change in the Navy, just like the Secretary of the Air Force won't be focused on LG powered fighter jets, or the Secretary of the Army will not be focused on electric powered tanks.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: At that point, steam was coming out of Chief Princess running mouth Warren's ears. Of course, Democrat activists that bet that it was all on, you know, just main -- they bet the farm on mainstreaming transgenderism in our military. That thought that was here to stay. They're livid. They're livid that Hegseth will get the woke out of our warfighting, including at our service academies.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: You have to rip, root and branch the politics and divisive policies out of these institutions, and then focus them on creating and preparing actual future military leadership. When that changes, Senator, I truly believe under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , we will have a recruiting renaissance.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Boy, we need a recruiting renaissance. We're down what 50,000, 60,000, 70,000, and we need a military that knows how to kill our enemies and win our wars, because as Hegseth said time and again today, the U.S. military, it's not a social program. It's not a charity, and it's not supposed to promote a particular ideology. It exists to defeat the enemies of the United States of America. Period. If too long, we've gotten away from that mission, and the results have been absolutely disastrous for us and for the world. Today, for the first time in years, we can actually see what a reformed and successful military would actually look like. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Senators \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2  and Tom Cotton, both sit on the \uc2 Senate Armed Services Committee\uc2  were there today. Senator Mullin, let's start with you. Now your colleague \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2  just announced that she will back Hegseth. That is huge. Do you anticipate any Republican defections given how well Hegseth did today.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: I think Pete just absolutely nailed it, Laura. And thank you for having me on, by the way. I wasn't surprised at all for Joni making that announcement. I thought she played her hand right, meaning that she did exactly what she said she was going to do. She was going to hold until the hearing. She came out immediately, said she was going to support because of the performance that Pete had today, and then, you know what happens with \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  and \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2 , I think they both said they want to listen to the hearing too.\par \par \uc2 I know Susan personally who paid a close attention to it. I believe, without question, Pete's going to be confirmed, and I think you're going to have a strong support from all the Republicans, men and women alike. I think he is the right person for the job, and President Trump did a wonderful job by picking him to be the next Secretary of Defense.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Senator Cotton, I think a lot of Americans who caught little snippets of this today were shocked, frankly, to find out that we are doing a lot of this woke stuff in the military. People don't cover it like we do, and follows every iteration of a change in policy in the military, but really it has hurt, in many ways, our military readiness and hurt our recruiting, which I think he talked about today.\par \par \uc2 SEN. TOM COTTON (R-AR): Yes, Laura, unfortunately, political correctness run amok and social engineering has harmed our military, therefore harmed our national security. As you said, it's probably declined recruiting numbers the point that we're at a recruiting crisis and it's harmed readiness. Look, our troops don't deserve their pronouns on their ID tags. They don't need to do privilege walks. They don't have to go through repeated training sessions about diversity, equity and inclusion. What they deserve is hard, realistic training to help them -- prepare them to defend this nation at wartime. The kind of training that Pete Hegseth has conducted and that he's run, that's one of the reasons why \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  picked him to be Secretary of Defense and stuck through him -- stuck with him through thick and thin.\par \par \uc2 So, I do think pretty soon, Pete is going to have the requisite number of votes to be confirmed in the Senate, and when that happens, I hope the Democrats will not delay or otherwise obstruct this nomination. If they want to vote against him. That's fine, but President Trump deserves to have his Secretary of Defense on the job promptly.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And Senator Mullin, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  claims that Hegseth is unfit for the job. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): He is, by outward appearance, woefully unfit for a job like Secretary of Defense, unfortunately for Mr. Hegseth, his testimony thus far has failed to address the disturbing questions that plague his nomination. It appears Mr. Hegseth's strategy is to follow the five D's of dodgeball, dodge, duck, dip, dive and dodge.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This is just an unserious -- unserious former Senate majority leader. He's reading his remarks. He can't even speak extemporaneously about such an important confirmation battle, and that's the best he can do.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: Well, what's unfortunate is where was \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  calling out the President of the United States currently, President Biden, who is woefully unfit to serve, and he's the one that has followed the five D's by dodging reporters for the last four years. That's his staff at the White House openly covering, the Left media openly covering for him. I mean, where was the call out? The hypocrisy that runs through the Democrat Party is so thick, it's laughable.\par \par \uc2 I mean, what about Rachel, you know, the Undersecretary inside of, inside of \uc2 HHS\uc2  who doesn't even know her own pronoun, or Sam, the guy who worked in the Department of Energy who couldn't figure out of his own luggage. Or, if you want to talk about being unqualified, Pete Hegseth, the gentleman or not -- Pete Hegseth, I'm sorry. \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , the gentleman that's over the Department of Transportation, the gentleman who truly was a mayor and now he's over transportation. Where were their call out on those individuals, right?\par \par \uc2 It doesn't matter, as long as it applies to them. Because, listen, if you're a Democrat, you're qualified for everything, evidently.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Senator Cotton, if they thought that, Hegseth was going to be a big stumbling block for Trump. They probably wouldn't have given him much trouble at this hearing, and they were pathetic today. Nothing hit Pete, right? I mean, they think he's actually going to do what Trump directs him to do, with consultation with military experts, but that's what they're really worried about, correct?\par \par \uc2 COTTON: Yes, they are, Laura, just look at the issue that I discussed with Pete today, and that's women in ground combat roles. Sometimes people talk about women in combat like women have been in combat for a long time as pilots or as medics or as mechanics, but when you talk about the infantry and artillery and special forces, there's certain irreducible physical demands, nothing Pete Hegseth can do will make an M240 Bravo machine gun way less than 47 pounds. He's not going to make an artillery shell way less than 100 pounds. A soldier in full combat battle rattle weigh less than say, 250 or even 300 pounds.\par \par \uc2 Those are irreducible physical demands, and we need high and gender neutral standards for those jobs to make sure that all of our troops are safe and ready to fight. The Democrats, though, kept coming back to the issue because they don't care about that. They'd rather have social engineering and quotas to meet their desired end state, as opposed to having a fit, ready fighting force to defend this nation.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I think Senator Mullin one thing that most Americans do want is an end to these forever wars.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: That's right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I know there's a big debate still, I guess, kind of in the Republican Party, where people just want to keep shoveling money at the Pentagon, 900 billion and counting, no audit, and they were getting on him for an audit today. But most people are like, look, this is not 1984 or 2004 we are out of money, and we have to smartly budget in every department, including the Pentagon.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: That's right. What we have to do is we got refocused, we got to get refocused inside America and say, what is our wants and what is our needs? Our needs is to have a strong military, because we got to have peace through strength, right? President Trump brings that to the White House. We've got to have a military that's capable and able to back that up. Now, it doesn't mean we continue to throw money at it. We are wasting a tremendous amount of money, billions of dollars, inside the Pentagon, and we've got to get a handle on it. I think that's why they fear when you have somebody like Pete Hegseth who's willing to go in there, because he doesn't come from the rank and file. He doesn't come from just racking and stacking someone else to come in and carry on as usual.\par \par \uc2 He's going to bring change. And that's why they also fear Elon, because they're going to go in there and figure out where the money is going to. We waste so much money, and yet they can't tell us where it's going. It's the only place in the world that you can be over budget and behind on delivery on a project that you bid and still get rewarded more and more money to do it. It's absolutely absurd. That doesn't work in the private sector.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Well, Senator Cotton, do you believe the Pentagon will finally pass an audit? It's failed seven times with Hegseth at the helm.\par \par \uc2 COTTON: I hope so. Pete said today that was a priority of his. As Markwayne says there are certain things we need to be spending more money on, like commercial off the shelf technology, software solutions that are readily available. We don't need our military trying to design new systems. There's other things that we need to do to stop bad past practices like cost plus contracts that encourage these cost overruns and budget overruns. There's a lot that we can do inside the Pentagon to eliminate waste and inefficiency and reinvest that money in the tools that our troops need and for that matter, more troops.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, and our manufacturing policy shouldn't be a giveaway to China under any circumstances and then shift the focus to China only to enrich China on the other side, that's also, I know, a priority of this administration. Senator Mullin, I know you helped prep Pete, good job there. And Senator Cotton, as always, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 And just ahead, can California's liberal leaders actually be trusted with what more than $100 billion of your money, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The climate change agents have boxed themselves into a corner. Now they're defending California Democrats against criticism that they didn't properly prepare for the wildfires on grounds that there was really nothing elected officials could have done.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WHOOPI GOLDBERG, THE VIEW CO-HOST: There was a fire catastrophe in California. Had to do with wind. You know how they always say, oh, the wind. It actually does. The winds move things, and sparks move things. And it doesn't matter how much water you have if 900,000 buildings go up at the same time. It's too soon to be saying, oh, it's Gavin's fault, it's nobody's fault.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But if that's the case, that as Whoopi said, it's not really anyone's fault, why would any sensible person, certainly any middle income earner remain in California. If claiming misinformation or just throwing up your hands is the only answers to every legitimate question about why these fires raged out of control for so long without enough water and so forth, then we should just expect a mass exodus from California, certainly all the people who are affected. It doesn't matter how much money is thrown at the rebuild, because, look, no one could have prevented it. It could happen again. And who wants to go through that hell another time?\par \par \uc2 But a depopulated California isn't what anyone should want, because that would lead eventually to the state's financial collapse. Republicans, I think well, you really look at a far more optimistic for California's future, because we believe that a return to basic common sense is what's desperately needed here. That means new leadership, goodbye DEI and sanctuary cities and hello excellence in America first, then and only then will there be a real chance to return the Golden State to its glory days, the 80s, the early 90s.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE JOHNSON (R-LA): Again, common sense is the theme here. You know, if \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  and local leaders made decisions that made this disaster exponentially worse, which it appears there were, should there be some consequence of that? Should there be some sort of safeguard on the funding?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Safeguard on the funding, they went crazy about that today. Well, when Democrats are in charge, we know they do stupid things like shutdown a wildfire prevention project to protect a shrub. Back in 2019, the L.A. city leaders planned to replace wooden power poles near the Pacific Palisades with steel ones after the area was identified as an elevated fire risk, but an amateur botanist complained that an endangered bush was going to be affected, so the project was shut down.\par \par \uc2 Now look, there's no converting 99 percent of these die-hard California Leftists, these green, woke, pro-illegal alien corruptocrats, they have to be sent packing out of politics at least. So for California to put out the financial, the criminal and the cultural fires that they set decades ago, you need a total new change in approach and political leadership.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now Alabama Senator Tommy Tuberville, who wants conditions on any aid that goes to California. Now, Senator, I want everyone to understand this. I believe the people of California need help. They should get it, but the media are already claiming that Republicans are playing politics with disaster aid. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Does these fires burn around Los Angeles? Political fights are also raging. House Speaker Mike Johnson suggesting that any aid to California maybe should come with conditions because of the decisions of leaders made before and during the fires.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I talked to the Maryland governor about that, and that was just horrible that people like you, Senator, would put any strings on this aid, after this devastating fires.\par \par \uc2 SEN. TOMMY TUBERVILLE (R-AL): What a disaster, Laura. You know, they have no governance there. They have no leadership. You see, what's going on in all these blue cities and blue states around the country and they just got outed again. In California, they get outed every year of what they've done and what they've not done. \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , since I've been here, has been their sugar daddy. He's bailed them out with the CARES Act in 2021, $30 million, $40 million -- billion dollars. He bailed them out because they're dead broke. We turn around with Inflation Reduction Act. We did the same thing a couple years ago. We bailed them out again.\par \par \uc2 Folks, their sugar daddy's gone. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a new sheriff in town. They have nobody to pay their bills. They're going to have to go to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and say, we need your help, and that's fine. We'll help them, but there's got to be some stipulations, Laura, on what we do, how we do it, when we do it, and what we're going to get out of. The American taxpayers are sick and tired of watching what's going on out there with people that are stealing the money, no governance and have no clue what they're doing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, you get the sense, as with most big government projects, Senator that the money will be going to friends and people who are politically connected or have the same environmental agenda, even though today, \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2  and yesterday, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  said, oh no, we're going to streamline a lot of this permitting. I don't think they have any credibility on any of that, not with our tax dollars.\par \par \uc2 TUBERVILLE: No. And what's going to have to happen is the new \uc2 EPA\uc2  Director that President Trump is going to bring in, he's going to have to get involved. He's going to have to get involved in what's going on in California. It's obvious that these people have no clue whatsoever of what to do, how to do it, and so our new \uc2 EPA\uc2  Director can get involved in this, put some stipulations down on how we're going to help them. And again, as you said, we need to help California. It is a beautiful state. Unfortunately, a lot of that state don't believe in all this blue madness, but we're going to help everybody out.\par \par \uc2 And unfortunately, the American taxpayers across the country are going to pay that, even the people in North Carolina that are under devastation as we speak, in Hawaii as we speak.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, well --\par \par \uc2 TUBERVILLE: -- and she's absolutely amazing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: A lot of people are worried about land grabs and, you know, losing their single-family home to high rises with high density, affordable housing. A lot of people are concerned about that, as well, Senator.\par \par \uc2 Hegseth hearing -- we've addressed this on the show, but the left is apoplectic tonight because I think they know he's going to get confirmed. He did incredibly well, I thought, acquitted himself, you know, brilliantly today.\par \par \uc2 TUBERVILE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Do you think the Democrats laid a glove on him?\par \par \uc2 TUBERVILLE: No.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You were there and no --\par \par \uc2 TUBERVILLE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- nothing.\par \par \uc2 TUBERVILLE: He knocked it out of the park, Laura. I was a little bit concerned going in. You know, he hadn't been in a situation like that. He handled it perfectly. They went after him. Their mission was to seek and destroy.\par \par \uc2 Schumer said, we're going to go after every one of these nominees. He was the first. He put them on their back. He absolutely destroyed them. And if anybody votes against him on the Republican side, we've got a question their intelligence because he will be the perfect person to get our military back.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Senator, just for the record, have you seen anyone show up drunk to vote in the senate like Senator \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2  said today -- that kind of raised a lot of eyebrows. And I remember back in '80s with \uc2 Ted Kennedy\uc2  would, you know, he is legendary, but anything you want to tell us tonight about any of your colleagues? Just among us chickens here.\par \par \uc2 TUBERVILLE: Well, yeah, no, I don't know any underlying stories, and there are probably some out there. Now, there's times that we'll start and have started voting at three or four in the afternoon and go until the next day at noon, 20 hours, 21 hours straight, and that might make some of us look like we've had a long night at the bar, but I don't see any of that. I really don't.\par \par \uc2 But it was -- I was set beside Markwayne. You can probably look at my facial expressions when he's doing all that. It is -- it was a fun day to watch the Democrats kind of crawl under the table, understanding that they'd overstepped their bounds.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Senator. We -- at least, we have that settled tonight. Senator, thank you. All right. Is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trying to upend a key part of Trump's America First agenda on his way staggering out the door? Coming up.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT AND PRESIDENT-ELECT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA (R): I would not let \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  be sold to Japanese, by the way. I would stop it if it hasn't been completed by the time I'm president.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA (D): U.S. steel has been an iconic American company for more than a century and it should remain a totally American company. That's going to happen, I promise you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, he promised, and many were surprised when it seemed like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  agreed with Trump on not letting U.S. steel sell to Japanese company. It's called \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 . Now, Biden even blocked the sale earlier this month, citing national security concerns, which are obvious.\par \par \uc2 But then, or whoever's pulling a string did something very strange. Biden delayed enforcement of that order until June. Here comes all the lobbyists, which means there's a chance this deal could still go through. But my next guest believes that, of course, \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  should and will stay U.S. - owned. Joining me now is Cleveland Cliff CEO Lourenco Goncalves. Lorenzo, thank you for joining us.\par \par \uc2 You're getting huge pushback and I know the lobbying dollars are flowing into Washington to try to turn Trump in favor of Nippon's purchase of U.S. steel but you want to buy U.S. steel as a U.S. company. What do Americans need to understand about this, given the fact that your bid comes in a little lower than, apparently, Nippon would offer here?\par \par \uc2 LOURENCO GONCALVES\uc2 , CEO, CLEVELAND CLIFFS: Laura, it's a great pleasure being with you. My offer is the only one that's acceptable for the United States because \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  was blocked on national security grounds. \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  did not present a plan that could work. And clearly, \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  would never create a situation in which they would -- workers in America first. We are the only ones that can implement the plan of President Trump and that's coming. We can't wait another five, six days to have this thing going.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Lourenco, U.S. steel told "The Angle" that your remarks are another attempt to shift attention away from the illegal monopolistic conspiracies that you're engaged in -- all in the face of declining performance at your company. And U.S. steel and Nipon are also suing you for, I guess, you know, the equivalent of Torsious interference with, you know, negotiations, illegal and coordinated actions.\par \par \uc2 So, they are -- they are pushing, pushing on all fronts. They have a lot of journalists, globalists on their side here against a U.S. company buying U.S. steel. But the attacks are now getting pretty personal, Lourenco.\par \par \uc2 GONCALVES: Yeah, but you know, when you hit me, you're going to be hit back 10, 20 times more. I can't wait to discuss these things in court. But that's a distraction. That's just to put a smoke screen on top of something that people don't really understand.\par \par \uc2 Japan has been destroying our American steel industry for decades. Japan overcapacity, Japan overproduction in steel is the biggest problem we have ever had in this country. Japan actually bought China.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How many times has -- Lourenco, Lourenco, just -- so, I believe this is correct, that \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  has been sanctioned, what, seven times for illegal dumping. I believe that's correct. They violated anti-dumping provisions and they've done an enormous amount of damage to the U.S. steel industry. And then, they're going to be rewarded with being able to buy this? Trump can't, Trump can't in no way change his mind on this. It would be a disaster if he did. Lourenco, final word.\par \par \uc2 GONCALVES: Exactly right. Exactly right, Laura. Twelve times. And the last time was two months ago in a period that they were already bidding for U.S. steel. So, at the same time that they were bidding for U.S. steel, they were dumping steel in our marketplace. And now, they are trying to do what's called tariff jumping.\par \par \uc2 Tariff jumping is you make -- first, you make the company that's competing against you weaker. They are doing that right now. We just described the situation on prices here in the United States. And then, they come and try to buy. So, we are going to discuss all that in court because this is bad behavior.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, this is a vulture. This is vulture -- and I don't like the phrase vulture capitalism -- it's overused. This is vulture capitalism on the international scale with national security implications. Lourenco, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 We're going to be watching this case very carefully. I know President Trump will do the right thing here. Now, Kamala isn't feeling the MAGA magic? Well, why is she such a sore loser? Next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Just six more days until our four-year Biden-Harris nightmare comes to an end, thank God, and sanity will return to Washington.\par \par \uc2 The MAGA inaugural extravaganza is going to include Carrie Underwood singing the national anthem. The Trump garbage truck is going to join the parade and the Village People -- they're going to perform "YMCA" -- but not everyone is excited.\par \par \uc2 Enter sore loser \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . She's bucking tradition and not inviting J.D. Vance to the V.P.'s residence before he moves in. She also went viral after posting a photo from \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 's funeral -- here it is. She's in it along with Biden, Bush and Obama, but the guy standing next to Obama -- he's cropped out. That guy was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Looks like someone still hasn't gotten over November's defeat.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Clay Travis, founder of "OutKick". Clay, weren't the Democrats the ones who said Trump couldn't accept the results of the last election? But they're supposed to be our moral superiors, I understand.\par \par \uc2 CLAY TRAVIS, FOUNDER, "OUTKICK": Oh, totally they are. And let's start with Kamala not inviting J.D. Vance to the vice president's residence. He's got three kids -- is my understanding. He's got a wife who's having to relocate all that whole family. Anybody who's ever moved a family, it's the bare minimum to allow them to come in and actually see the place before they arrive.\par \par \uc2 It's the height of petty, but for someone who managed to lose all 50 states in terms of the trajectory of the election, something we haven't seen in decades, and to lose to a Republican in the largest fashion since 1988, I hope that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  stays petty and bitter like this.\par \par \uc2 And I hope Democrats give her another chance because remember Laura, what they're saying now is she only had 100 days. That's about 99 and a half days too many for anybody who's ever spent any time with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . But maybe I'm wrong. Maybe they should go ahead and make her the nominee for 2028. I think everybody would sign up for that right now.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, well, we know that, you know, Trump didn't invite Biden to the White House but Biden had already been to the White House. Obviously, he was vice president. So, it wasn't like he was unfamiliar with the White House. But -- but Clay, there's another sore loser, it seems like, at least. \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  -- she's also skipping Trumps inauguration. "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " says that, "\uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 's upcoming absence also renews attention to her candid in open disdain of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Though she attended Trump's inauguration 2017, photographers captured her troubled expression that day as she and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  left. Clay, she's - I think, almost a billionaire, but man, she's bitter.\par \par \uc2 TRAVIS: Well, and it's not only not attending the inauguration. I was surprised this didn't get more attention. You showed the picture that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  shared, you know, who was noticeably absent and not because they were cropped out.\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  -- so, she wasn't