neral who serves should not go directly into the defense industry for 10 years. You're not willing to make that same pledge?\par \par \uc2 PETE HEGSETH, DEFENSE SECRETARY NOMINEE: I'm not a general, Senator.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's such an easy line. It's such an easy setup. Is that really - - that's the best she could do?\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Well, listen, you can't expect her to know his rank if she doesn't know her own DNA, OK? There is that concern. If you can't get your origin story right, you're probably going to botch somebody else's. But I love this so much because for anybody watching at home who missed the hearing, the conflict comes down to this.\par \par \uc2 Pete Hegseth, once a military that can save Private Ryan, the Democrats want a military that can transition Private Ryan, Ok? I think we should choose wisely here. The soldiers want Hegseth. The loonies with the blue hair don't. That's everything you need to know.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, the screeching of those women was just -- that was -- I'm telling you, play that in Gitmo. You'll get all the information you need from those enemy combatants. All right, speaking of women in combat, things got heated between Nancy Mace and Jasmine Crockett during a different committee oversight hearing. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. JASMINE CROCKETT (D) TEXAS 30TH CONGRESSIONAL DISTRICT: I can see that somebody's campaign coffers really are struggling right now. So, she's going to keep saying trans, trans so that people will feel threatened. And child listen, I want you all to tell me whether or no -- I want to find out --\par \par \uc2 REP. NANCY MACE (R-SC): I am no child. Do not call me a child. I am no child.\par \par \uc2 CROCKETT: I want to find out --\par \par \uc2 MACE: Do not do that. I am not a child. I am not a child.\par \par \uc2 CROCKETT: Chairman, I am reclaiming my time. If you want to take it outside --\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Mr. Chairman, the Committee is not in order.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: OK. All right.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That was a manner like, get me out of here.\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: I know, seriously. Every time I watch Jasmine Crockett speak, I feel like she's testifying on a show called "The Stupid People's Court". It's so hard to watch. And yes, she always goes to that other insult with Nancy Mace or anybody who dares counter some of her limited thought process.\par \par \uc2 But good on Nancy Mace for stepping up for herself here. And lest we forget, Nancy Mace was a \uc2 Waffle House\uc2  waitress. So, she is not t taking nothing from anybody. Like if we really wanted to secure the border, you send the women who police a waffle house at two in the morning down there. Tom Holman can take the rest of the year off, we'd be fine.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Have you been to a \uc2 Waffle House\uc2 , like, in the middle of the night after one of your shows? Have you?\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Of course.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How many times?\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Is this an intervention from wardrobe again? I told them I'm trying.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Jimmy, I would go there before my radio show. When I was out in California, I would host, and it was 6 A.M. to 9 A.M. because of the time change. It used to be 9 A.M. But obviously, we're out there. So, we would go, it's not as Raymond would come, and she was helping me.\par \par \uc2 We'd be sitting at the \uc2 Waffle House\uc2  at like 4 A.M. in L.A. I think it was near Wilshire -- anyway. We would sit there and just watching the people come in, you don't need a comedy routine. That blueberry compote on the pancakes -- it's all you need to know, ok? All you need to know.\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Amen. Amen.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Jimmy, great to see you. Everyone, be sure to check out Jimmy's comedy specials. They're on foxnation.com and they're awesome. Thank you for watching tonight. Make sure to follow me on social media.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2025 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2025 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. All materials  herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be  reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020250115el1e00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Shutdown Battle Morphs Into A Meme War; Democrats Vote To Shut Down The Government; "Trans" Sex Offender Targets Girls' Locker Rooms; Chicago raid targets Tren de Aragua members; School allowed criminal to work with children, accepts resignation; Trans, drag Democrat runs for California State Senate\b0\par\par\uc2 John Roberts, Laura Ingraham, Mike Tobin, Jason Chaffetz, Raymond  Arroyo \par \uc2 8,169 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 January 2025\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 VIQ Solutions, Inc. \par \par \uc2 JOHN ROBERTS\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: -- Justice Department sue six states to force them to share state-wide voter registration list escalating a high stakes fight over federal authority in election oversight. Thanks for watching Special Report this evening. I'm John Roberts in Washington. The Ingraham Angle is coming up next.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. As always, thanks for spending time with us. It's only day one of the Schumer shutdown, and Democrats are already making fools of themselves. First, boasting on their way out of town that the shutdown was their choice.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. SHRI THANEDAR (D-MI): We got to make sure Americans have the health care that they need, and if that means they got to shut this government down, so be it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I thought that was some kind of comedy skit. How did Michiganders elect that goofball? He has zero concern about the disruption to federal employees and other Americans. It's not a good look. Even The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  is warning Democrats about falling into the, quote, shutdown trap, saying that Left-wing Democrats entered the shutdown from a position of weakness and that chances are slim that the two parties could ever come to terms that Democratic activists would view as a decisive victory, yet the party's base wants them to fight anyway, even if it means holding the government hostage.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, that is exactly what the Democrats are doing. \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  is getting outplayed and outmaneuvered, not just on the shutdown itself and the substance issues, but even in the meme wars involving cute sombreros and Mexican music.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. HAKEEM JEFFRIES (D-NY): It was a xenophobic stereotype, which is why we've heard from many Latino organizations denouncing what took place. I'm not going to dwell on the president's erratic behavior in terms of the meme or the A.I. deep fake videos. The broader problem is, it's deeply unserious, and this is a serious moment. We need to reopen the government. We need to enact a spending agreement that's bipartisan, that actually meets the needs of the American people. And we need to address the Republican health care crisis.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Health care crisis. We're going to get into that too. Thought Obamacare was supposed to fix all this. But the vice president continues to run circles around them and intellect and humor.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 J.D. VANCE (R), U.S. VICE PRESIDENT: I think it's funny, the president's joking, and we're having a good time. You can negotiate in good faith while also poking a little bit of fun at some of the absurdities of the Democrats positions, and even, you know, poking some -- some fun at the absurdity of the Democrats themselves. I mean, I'll tell \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  right now, I make this solemn promise to you that if you help us reopen the government, the sombrero memes will stop.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The sombreros are out, if you actually get some common sense. That's a fair bargain. But Democrats are not amused. They're blind to the obvious and deaf when convenient.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHN BERMAN, CNN ANCHOR: Every Republican who's gone on TV, the last 12 hours or so has called this the Schumer shutdown. What do you say about that name? Senator Schumer, can you hear me?\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): I can't hear.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's like that old commercial from the 70s. Sorry, honey, can't hear you, water is running. Well, they say hearing is the last thing to go, right. But we know Schumer's hearing is perfect when the woman speaking is AOC, because she's acting like she's the boss of him.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. ALEXANDRIA OCASIO-CORTEZ (D-NY): I saw some Republican members of Congress saying, oh, well, if we have this shutdown, it's because of AOC. Well, if that's the case, my office is open, and you are free to walk in and negotiate with me directly.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Negotiate with me directly. OK, boys, look out, Democrats. That's what I call an intra-party wedgie.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: There was a thought from the Republicans that AOC is directing this, and she said that senators are welcome to go to her office directly. Is she driving that?\par \par \uc2 REP. NANCY PELOSI (D-CA): Why are you saying such a ridiculous thing?\par \pa