ently George Pudlo, but I don't know for sure because Wikipedia doesn't allow deadnaming, and I didn't want to be too hard, didn't feel like it was worth too much time.\par \par \uc2 But it could happen because he's running in a place called Silver Lake, and Silver Lake is peak childless millennial in Los Angeles. It is a very trendy place to live. It is kind of grungy and dirty and unpleasant most of the time, but it's also very walkable and vibey and bohemian. You got a lot of great restaurants. Shout out to Courage Bagel. So, it's one of those things where it could conceivably happen because a hard leftist is going to win this area. So, who knows?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I don't think it's dirty. I've been to Silver. Why do you say it's dirty? Silver Lake is dirty? It's very trendy. I mean, I've been there a bunch of times. I wouldn't describe it dirty.\par \par \uc2 MARLOW: I'll take staff for you next time I'm there.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You got to take me where you go there.\par \par \uc2 MARLOW: At least places where I would go to eat.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Okay. All right.\par \par \uc2 MARLOW: Yeah, I will.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. I'm just trying to stick up for the little bit of the Silver Lake crowd. All right, Jason, the non-binary drag queen also wants to create a slush fund to pay for trans health care. Check this out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MAEBE A. GIRL: This includes committing $500 million to offset the impact of federal funding loss for transgender health care in our state. Unsurprisingly, the top three communities being targeted by the Trump administration and right-wing talking heads are the communities with the least amount of political power. Transgender people, undocumented immigrants, and unhoused people.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Jason, we have to pay for the --\par \par \uc2 JASON CHAFFETZ, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yeah, this is -- this is -- this is -- yeah. Look, this is \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 's California. I'd love to see where he weighs in on this one. This is California today. I mean, I have no doubt that this person has the ability to perhaps get elected. I think California has gone that woke, that crazy. They've checked in, like you said, every single woke box they possibly can.\par \par \uc2 And sure, another $500 million. Why not? I mean, how many billions of dollars in debt in California, thanks to \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 ? Yeah, this person, look out. This is where California is headed.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I saw -- I saw some memes, you know. And they were very kind of positive. You know, elect the bearded lady. I mean -- I don't know. I mean, you never know what -- you know, look, very lots of makeup, lots of accoutrements there. But, you know, it could be appeal to a lot of people, I guess, in California given what has happened in California. But moving on, kids, The View's Joy Behar asked Zohran Mamdani point-blank an important question. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOY BEHAR, CO HOST, THE VIEW: Let's talk about President Trump because he had a lot to say about you.\par \par \uc2 ZOHRAN MAMDANI, MEMBER, NEW YORK STATE ASSEMBLY: Dear friend of mine.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 BEHAR: Number one, he's attacking you as a communist. Are you?\par \par \uc2 MAMDANI: No. I'm a Democratic socialist. That means I believe in dignity for all people.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BEHAR: At least more than that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Alex, dignity for all people. We all want dignity, don't we, Alex?\par \par \uc2 MARLOW: Of course, we do. It is a (INAUDIBLE). It implies to us who don't believe in social economic policy, don't want dignity for people. Now, he laid out his economic plan on "The Breakfast Club" radio show this week. It's going to lead to a mass exodus of small businesses because you're going to have a new corporate tax. And he wants to put a wealth tax on this class warfare thing. It is just going to force all of the wealthiest people in the city to move down to Florida.\par \par \uc2 I mean, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  must have been waving one of those noisemaker things over his head when he sees this stuff. He is just going to get an influx of new rich people.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And then a few months ago, Jason, it was -- you know, the white neighborhoods are going to have to pay more. He had to -- that was actually in one of his, you know, platform documents, like white neighborhoods. He was asked about that. He's like, well, that's not exactly. It was just a manner of description. I'm paraphrasing. But none of these is good. It's all Commie Land.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: It is Commie Land. He said, oh, dignity for all. You know, except if you make money. If you actually employ people, then we don't need any of you. And if you got a small business, maybe a grocery store, oh, there's no room for you because we're going to do that instead of the private sector.\par \par \uc2 And so, no, he has -- don't tell me it's about dignity for all. That's a bunch of crap. Look at what the socialists stand for. They want to take over and run the elements of production and capital. And there is no reason for people to continue to stay in New York City. They're going to flee. They already have been. But this is going to accelerate it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, comrades. Thank you very much, Alex and Jason. And coming up, shocking new Biden cheat sheets emerging. "Seen and Unseen" with Raymond Arroyo is next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's time for "Seen and Unseen" where we reveal the stories behind the headlines. With us is Fox News Contributor Raymond Arroyo. Raymond, we knew that Biden was having some memory issues and that he used, you know, little cheat sheets note cards, but we didn't realize the extent of it.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, you know, Laura, Fox News Digital acquired these new cheat sheets that Biden used not just for talking points. They were facial recognition cards for people like Denzel Washington, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , people he'd known his whole career, Laura. \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , Dick Durbin. I mean, wasn't anyone concerned when he kept checking the cards and then looking at their faces. I mean, they should have asked some questions.\par \par \uc2 But had people probed a little deeper into the National Archive files, Laura? Would you like to see what they might have found?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah. Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Okay. They might have found a card like this. Jill Biden, Jilly, your wife. She's also the first lady. Follow her orders at all times. Or this one. Commander, the dog, this is your dog. If he begins to growl, throw Secret Service agent his way. That worked out well, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Uh-huh.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: And, of course, there is the card for the Air Force One staircase. Approach with caution. Hold on to the railing. Hmm.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I think he needed -- those cheat sheets can -- sometimes come in handy, Raymond. I'm just --\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- glad Commander is okay, even if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  might be still struggling a little bit. Now, he must have missed that last card, though.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I don't think that worked very well. Again, we're learning all these details now, but we knew it all.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We saw it in real time.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: That's exactly right. That's exactly right, Laura. These people covered this up. And the fact that these things are emerging, they all knew his wheels weren't testing the tarmac.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Please.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Somebody should have sent up a warning flare, you know. But the remarkable thing is while the party is trying to forget Biden, okay, they practically pushed him off stage. They can't let another former president go.\par \par \uc2 We covered the Luigi Mangione musical, I'd give you, and this is coming to New York. No lie, Laura. 44, the Obama musical.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (MUSIC PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Okay. That's (INAUDIBLE).\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, I'm going to get you some tickets. I'm sure that'll be coming to the Kennedy Center soon.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Hmm.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: But I'll be like, Bacalaca (ph) Obama.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 You can't make these lyrics up. Move over, Irving Berlin.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So, they have a scene where he tells the intelligence agencies to redo the assessment to, you know, try to nail Trump on the Russian stuff. I can't wait to see how they set that to music. That'll be good.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 All right, Raymond, another Chicago fixture. The archbishop of Chicago, Blase Cupich, had announced a church honor for a pro-abortion senator. Dick Durbin, 10 bishops, opposed the honor. And the pope was asked about this, and this caused --\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- the bigger scandal. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 POPE LEO XIV, SOVEREIGN OF VATICAN CITY STATE: I think that it's very important to look at the overall work that a senator has done during, if I'm not mistaken, 40 years of service. Someone who says I'm against abortion but says I'm in favor of the death penalty is not really pro-life. So, someone who says that I'm against abortion, but I'm in agreement with the inhuman treatment of immigrants from the United States, I don't know if that's pro-life.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah. Wow.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wow.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: That is unfortunate, Laura. I mean, this moral ambiguity here, you can trade --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Hmm.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I'm sorry. With apologies to the Holy Father. He knows this. And again, this is an off-the-cuff interview. It is not dogma. But it's awfully confusing. Social media is exploding with people so upset about this because you can't say a grave, always evil act like abortion, is on the same par with unfettered immigration or the death penalty.\par \par \uc2 By the way, the death penalty is the church's response to those who take innocent lives. The church has always, from Augustine to Pius the 10thm to John Paul the 2nd, said they don't prefer it, but the death penalty is an option and morally listed if it's carried out without vengeance. The Holy Father has a cleanup act to do here.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, boy.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I think he was trying to protect his friend, Blase Cupich and Dick Durbin.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Hmm, hmm, hmm.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: This is a bad way of doing it. And, you know, today, he blessed an iceberg, Laura. You know, not -- not -- not the ice agency but an iceberg. It was a climate change event at the Vatican. Put up the video, guys.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You can't make this up. You know, if you're going to do a \uc2 U.N.\uc2  kind of climate stunt, call Greta Thunberg. We know where she lives. The Vatican shouldn't be engaging in this nonsense.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, brother, Holy Father. Oh, boy. Raymond, thank you very much. That's it for us tonight. Make sure to follow me on social media. Thank you for watching. Remember, it's America now and forever. Jesse Watters takes - -\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2025 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2025 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020250102el1100001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 Now, RFK Jr. Meets Senators on Capitol Hill; Colorado Police Probe Robbery at TDA-Linked Apartment Complex; Trump Says, Looking to Cut Up to $2 Trillion in Fed Spending\b0\par\par\uc2 Martha MacCallum; Aishah Hasnie; Alicia Acuna, Paul Mauro, Katie  Pavlich, Clay Travis \par \uc2 8,945 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 December 2024\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: The Story with Martha MacCallum\par \uc2 HUNDD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 VIQ Solutions, Inc. \par \par \uc2 [15:00:00]\par \par \uc2 MARTHA MACCALLUM, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: All right. Thank you guys. Good afternoon, everybody. I'm Martha MacCallum and this is The Story.\par \par \uc2 Breaking right now, \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2 , President-elect Trump's disruptor nominee for Health and Human Services Secretary, is in these very important meetings behind closed doors with lawmakers on Capitol Hill. His plans for the foods that we eat, his stance on vaccines, very important. Also there's an issue of the issue of abortion, I should say. So, all of this paves the way for one of the nominees that President Trump would like to see moved along in this process and those hearings are going to get started just a couple of weeks from now.\par \par \uc2 Senior National Correspondent Aishah Hasnie following all of RFK Jr.'s movements on the Hill today. We understand he is still in a meeting with Senator Hawley, Aishah. What are you learning there?\par \par \uc2 AISHAH HASNIE, FOX NEWS SENIOR NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Martha, he just walked out. He just left his meeting with Senator Hawley and I believe he is going to a holding room to wait until his next meeting, which I want to say it's with GOP \uc2 John Thune\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He has got a packed day. He's meeting with nine different Republicans today. That is a lot of meetings, so it's one after another. And so far, so good, at least according to this nominee, watch how he thinks this is going. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: How are the meetings going? Any comment?\par \par \uc2 ROBERT F. KENNEDY JR\uc2 ., FORMER INDEPENDENT PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Really productive. Really good.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HASNIE: Really productive, really good, he says.\par \par \uc2 We just got some new photos from his meeting with Senator Tommy Tuberville, and he's been getting a warm welcome among Senate Republicans. Tough questions on a variety of stances, but a warm welcome.\par \par \uc2 And like I said, he meets with GOP Leader \uc2 John Thune\uc2  today. But those that still have yet to have some face-to-face time with him, they've got some lingering questions.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOHN KENNEDY\uc2  (R-LA): I want to talk to Mr. Kennedy about his abortion stand. He's all over his map, all over the map.\par \par \uc2 I don't know what's in his heart and what he really believes because he said so much stuff, some of which sounds like he's from outer space.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HASNIE: Okay. And, Martha, just a little bit of news that RFK Jr. made a few moments ago, he told reporters that he is open and wants to meet with Senate Democrats as well. Of course, he's been a longtime Democrat, comes from a longtime Democratic family, and there are plenty of Democrats that want to sit down with him as well. They have questions about vaccines and abortion as well. Martha?\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, he may get some across-the-aisle support. It's going to be interesting to watch. Aishah, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 So, let's bring in Zen Honeycutt, who is founder and executive director of Moms Across America. Kelly Ryerson is one of the group's board members. And their mission is to raise awareness about GMOs, genetically modified foods and toxins in our food supply and how they impact our children. RFK Jr. has served as an advisor to this group. Ladies, great to have both of you with us.\par \par \uc2 Zen, let me start with you and I want to start by playing something, because this is the kind of conversation that's going on with a lot of parents around the country. Here's what they were talking about at The View. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I keep being surprised by how many girlfriends of mine I talk to are kind of interested in what he's saying, not at all on vaccines, but on food in America.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: And if you can't read it, you should not be eating it.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We live in a country where we are -- crap is put in our food that makes us sick, and then pharmaceuticals come in and throw pills at it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: You know what, I for one am very glad that this conversation has gained traction in the country and people are looking at labels. These are personal choices about what you put in your body. Zen, This has been a passion of yours for a long time. Give us a quick thumbnail sketch of why.\par \par \uc2 ZEN HONEYCUTT, FOUNDER AND DIRECTOR, MOMS ACROSS AMERICA: Well, because Kennedy, what he's speaking up for is the safety of our children. And, you know, he's risking his life every day to do this. You look at historically his dad, his uncle, you know, basically killed in the line of duty of defending democracy. And he's a 35-year environmental health lawyer, right? He has been standing up for Americans for a very long time.\par \par \uc2 And what we're seeing is bipartisan support for this food issue. You know, poison is not partisan. Cancer is not choosy. It's time for Democrats and Republicans to come together and vote for a man who is risking his life to protect the health of our children and this country.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, Kelly, you know, on a personal level, what got you involved in this fight?\par \par \uc2 KELLY RYERSON, BOARD MEMBER, MOMS ACROSS AMERICA: I became involved in this fight because I found my two children really struggling with chronic illness, migraines, ADHD, gastrointestinal issues.\par \par \uc2 [15:05:04]\par \par \uc2 I myself have an autoimmune condition. My friends seem to all have an autoimmune condition.\par \par \uc2 And I really started to take a look to see what exactly am I putting in my body. That's where I landed on glyphosate, which is the active ingredient in the weed killer, Roundup. And that's where I met RFK Jr. because he was one of the attorneys fighting \uc2 Monsanto\uc2  on behalf of the plaintiffs saying that Roundup causes cancer. And now it's the most widely used pesticide.\par \par \uc2 I think it's interesting that before that person was questioning his views on abortion, because this is someone who's fighting for the fertility of our country. These pesticides are robbing us of our fertility, very specifically crossing glyphosate crosses the blood testes barrier and lands in semen. It kills sperm. So, we wonder why we have sperm counts that are down 50 percent over the last 50 years.\par \par \uc2 HONEYCUTT: And, Martha, if you look at the issue of abortion that what the Democrats were talking about last year, a million babies were aborted. That is a tragedy. And if you look at women's reproductive rights, 7.2 million women in this country are struggling with infertility. That is an issue that's seven times larger. We should be talking about the right to be able to procreate and what are our politicians doing to protect that. And Kennedy is going to stand up for women's rights in that area as soon as he gets elected into -- you know, gets confirmed into this position.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, Kelly, this is President-elect Trump yesterday on the issue of school vax mandates. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Do you think schools should mandate vaccines?\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , U.S. PRESIDENT-ELECT: I don't like mandates. I'm not a big mandate person. So, you know, I was against mandates. Mostly Democrat governors did the mandates and they did a very poor thing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Kelly, you know, all of our kids have to be vaccinated to go to the school system. There are some people who aren't comfortable sending their kids to school with other kids who weren't vaccinated against things like polio. Yesterday, \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr.\uc2  said that he supports the polio vaccine. Where do you stand on this?\par \par \uc2 RYERSON: What I think is having watched RFK Jr. dig through vast piles of data to come to his different decisions on pesticides, I agree that the same thing should happen with any pharmaceutical drug, including vaccines, if they haven't been tested, which is what he claims, and is sued on behalf of all of us to this fact, then I think that we need to look into it and see if they're harmful or not.\par \par \uc2 I mean, that's just common sense. That shouldn't be something that's controversial. Look and see if they're fine or look if they're causing a problem. That's all.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes. You know, Zen, it's this connection and the pharmaceutical companies do a lot of amazing work. There are a lot of people alive today because of the drugs that are created by our pharmaceutical companies. However, this issue of vaccines and making them mandatory, people have a lot of questions about the combination between making something mandatory and the business at pharmaceutical companies that surrounds that. Quick summary thought on that for me, if you could.\par \par \uc2 HONEYCUTT: Yes. Well, look at California. They had a 95 percent vaccination rate before the pharmaceutical companies got greedy and before they started really pushing the Democrats to mandate it. And now the rates are falling, because when it was mandated, the parents began to say, wait a second, why are you forcing this on us? And like myself, my kids are vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 I looked at the ingredients and said, wait a second. I don't feel comfortable with these ingredients. In fact, some of these ingredients could have glyphosate weed killer in them because the animal parts are being fed grains that are sprayed with glyphosate as a drying agent In fact, we sent five childhood vaccines to be tested. Every single one of them was positive with glyphosate weed killer and another scientist corroborated it.\par \par \uc2 So, we think that this push to mandate is not a good idea, especially for people who have MTFHR gene mutations and cannot detox properly.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: All right. Zen and Kelly, very interesting. Obviously, you've gotten very closely involved in this issue and we'll see where it goes. We'll see how this hearing process that gets underway in a couple of weeks goes for RFK Jr. to be \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary. Thank you both very much. Great to have you with us today.\par \par \uc2 RYERSON: Thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, two big exclusives. Ahead this hour, Republican Congressman Dan Crenshaw is in the classified briefing right now on these suspicious drone sightings. So, he's going to join us and Let us know what he can share with us and why is this classified this briefing if everything that's up there is nothing to be worried about.\par \par \uc2 So, the co-chairs also of the newly formed House DOGE caucus, which is also meeting today to jump start our big cuts to our spending, what have they identified so far, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [15:10:00]\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Shocking story out of Aurora, Colorado, as police investigate what they call an evil and vicious kidnapping at an apartment complex, yes, that apartment complex, that has been terrorized by members of the violent Venezuelan gang, Tren de Aragua. Police are not confirming if the suspects are part of that gang, but they say they are believed to be undocumented Venezuelans accused of tying up and beating two people last night, stabbing one of them and robbing the home.\par \par \uc2 Senior Correspondent Alicia Acuna has the whole story for us as she reports live from Denver. Hi, Alicia.\par \par \uc2 ALICIA ACUNA, FOX NEWS SENIOR CORRESPONDENT: Hi, Martha. The Aurora Police chief says that the two victims who are a man and a woman are also Venezuelan migrants. And he says they were brave to call 911.\par \par \uc2 The details of this crime are just horrific. Police detained up to 15 suspects believed to be Venezuelan migrants as well who they say broke into an apartment, took the victims to another unit where they were bound, pistol whipped and the male was stabbed.\par \par \uc2 [15:15:01]\par \par \uc2 They were terrorized for more than four hours before the victims promised not to call police if released, and they were. And the victims did call authorities.\par \par \uc2 Today, the police chief had strong words for the White House.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TODD CHAMBERLAIN, AURORA P.D. POLICE CHIEF: I had a discussion with an individual from the White House. And that occurred back on September the 23rd, I believe. And that person basically told me that, hey, once these immigrants get across the border, that's all we really care about. And to me, that's a problem.\par \par \uc2 And so, \uc2 Aurora\uc2 , we are now in the process, as many other cities throughout this nation, of trying to pick up the pieces of an incredibly bad system that was in place.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ACUNA: This is the same complex, as you mentioned, Martha, where that Ring camera captured armed TDA members. The chief says there's no question last night's attack was committed by gang members but can't yet confirm that these are TDA.\par \par \uc2 Today, the Aurora City councilwoman who sounded the alarm on this issue had