energy, there's still a buzz on Capitol Hill. We had a packed caucus room, much more -- many more people attended than we thought. We had over 50 Republican members, 3 Democrats. And it was really, I think, the first thing is to build trust before these two parties that haven't trusted each other, but we're going to have to trust each other if we're going to go forward.\par \par \uc2 REP. PETE SESSIONS (R-TX): I think we spoke, Martha, specifically about working together, bringing all the ideas into a format where we not only gather them, but then have debate and discussion about them. This is about making the government more efficient also.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Okay. Those are great beginnings, but, you know, we've heard specifics from Musk and Ramaswamy about places that cuts can be made, education, agriculture making employees come back to the office if they have still been out for four years since COVID.\par \par \uc2 Watch this. There's broad spread support for this. Watch this from Jon Stewart and \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2 . Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JON STEWART, CO-HOST, THE DAILY SHOW: I had a conversation with the deputy secretary of defense where we were talking about the $850 billion budget and you would have thought like, I asked what underwear she was wearing, like her response to being questioned about the lack of passing an audit on $850 billion. It was --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Multiple times, multiple times.\par \par \uc2 STEWART: Just, you know, went like, how dare you? The arrogance of it was wild.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, Congressman Bean, did you talk about specifics in there about where the cutting begins?\par \par \uc2 BEAN: We talked about specifics on the format of how we're going to go forward. Watching your video there, we do have to get people back to work. Our office is overrun with casework because they can't get federal workers on the phone. We're going to take