at he has said he would not pardon his son.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He is not pardoning his son which he could do. These are federal charges. He is not doing that. That is a power -- he has a power for both of those.\par \par \uc2 He is not doing it because he is living what it means to have a rule of law in this country.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You think you'll ever trust the legacy media again? These channels.\par \par \uc2 But just, you know, they just took Biden at his word and regurgitated it. Why would anyone in their right mind take Biden at his word? We on this channel, on this show, we tell you the truth.\par \par \uc2 We've been right about Richard Jewell, going back to the beginning. We were right about UVA. We were right about Duke lacrosse.\par \par \uc2 We were right about Freddy Gray in Baltimore. We were right about Ferguson, Missouri. We were right about Obama's radicalism. We were right about vetting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  which they wouldn't do. We were right about Russia collusion.\par \par \uc2 We were right also about FISA abuse and I can keep going on, and they're always wrong, they peddle lies, and conspiracy theories for a living.\par \par \uc2 Joe, a habitual liar, serial plagiarizer, since the 1970s, and for the legacy media, it was all means to the end, support the Democratic Party, do it at all costs.\par \par \uc2 Thankfully, they no longer have influence over freethinking Americans that have in the beginning they sought out talk radio. They sought out FOX News. Now, they still trust talk radio and FOX News, and they have social media who -- \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  said we're all now in the media business. And you can post things on your own and pass on information to your friends.\par \par \uc2 The Kamala files that I tried to deputize people with. The Democratic Party will soon lose control the Senate, the House, the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, \uc2 House Judiciary Committee\uc2  Chairman Jim Jordan, House Oversight Committee Chairman James Comer.\par \par \uc2 Is this over, Jim Jordan?\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM JORDAN (R-OH): Well, we're going to look at David Weiss. Remember, the Congress has a strong history of looking at special counsels, getting a report from them, bringing them in for a hearing or deposition or maybe both. So we're going to look at all that.\par \par \uc2 But I love what you said your monologue, Sean, the Biden presidency started with a lie and it ended with a lie and as you pointed out, there were all kinds of false things in between. But remember, October 2020, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said in that debate, the Hunter Biden laptop story according to 51 former intel officials is a Russian information operation. That was a lie and he knew it at the time.\par \par \uc2 And then, of course, yesterday, after saying he wouldn't pardon his son, he turns around and does the very thing. Lie at the start, lie at the ending and a terrible four years in between. Thank goodness President Trump is going back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: James Comer, let me ask you. In your mind, is this over? Is this over for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ? Is it over for his brother? Is it over for other family members that were paid monies here? Or does this continue?\par \par \uc2 Does \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  need to think about pardoning these family members and maybe himself?\par \par \uc2 REP. JAMES COMER (R-KY): Well, remember, the House Oversight Committee referred Jim Biden as well as \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  to the Department of Justice for perjury. We deposed \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and he lied under oath and we brought Jim Biden in for transcribed interview and he lied under oath. That's a fact. That's in a report that Jim Jordan and I signed and published to the American people.\par \par \uc2 So I would fully expect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  -- to pardon Jim Biden and remember in our investigation we found that family members including \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  profited from the influence peddling schemes, where they were shaking down our adversaries around the world for tens of millions of dollars and then they created all these shell companies and laundered the money through the shell companies. And this is according to six banks, six banks said this in the suspicious activity reports that were filed with treasury that they were laundering money and they sent the money and incremental payments to 10 different Biden family members.\par \par \uc2 So I think that the new Trump Justice Department is going to have a lot on its platter. I look forward to consulting with them to see if we can be of any further assistance. But right now, I think the ball will be in Attorney General Bondi's court.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So let me be clear, James Comer, do you believe other Biden family members committed crimes? And do you believe that a new attorney general if they are upholding the law would be with -- it would be within their jurisdiction to go forward with indictments? And what about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  himself?\par \par \uc2 COMER\uc2 : I believe two other Biden family members definitely and knowingly committed crimes. In addition to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , you have Jim Biden and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  obstructed my and Chairman Jordan's investigations, he lied multiple times. He lied about his knowledge and involvement.\par \par \uc2 We had sworn testimony from Bobulinski and Devon Archer that said that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  knew all along what was going on. He was selling the brand, his brand. He was selling access to our enemies around the world and he lied just like Jim Jordan said in the debate about the laptop and he lied like when he said he wasn't going to pardon his son.\par \par \uc2 So, yes, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in my opinion has committed crimes. Jim Biden we saw he took in all these loans, he didn't pay any interest, didn't pay any principal, had no loan documentation. At what point do those loans become - - become income. They never paid taxes on.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, why did he get those loans? You know, what was he doing? All the people that wired money to the Bidens were shady characters, either adversaries or people that were in trouble needing assistance, needing a prosecutor fired, needing a pardon, they were needing something from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the big guy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Same question, Jim Jordan, and do you believe that that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  should think about pardoning the people that James Comer just mentioned and maybe himself?\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Well, well, Sean, I assume he's already looking to do that for his -- particularly for his brother as Jamie pointed out when we deposed him, he said things that just didn't square with what the evidence that we had, and the facts that we had gathered so we'll see.\par \par \uc2 I do think it's interesting you pointed this out the time, the broad -- the length of this from December -- excuse me -- January 1st, 2014 to December 1st, 2024, 10 years and 11 months.\par \par \uc2 Remember, three of that -- of 11-year time frame, three of those years was when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was vice president. So he's making sure even though the statute of limitations has run for any involvement to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  had with \uc2 Burisma\uc2  and taxes he owed for that unbelievable amount of income he got from that energy company in Ukraine. So I think he -- that that is something that I think is just huge because remember with \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  got put on the board, he wasn't qualified to be on the board he told us that himself in an interview.\par \par \uc2 The heads of \uc2 Burisma\uc2  asked him to weigh in with his father to relieve the pressure they are under from the prosecutor in Ukraine, and then fourth, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  goes and does just that and he uses our tax money American tax dollars to say if you want the loan guarantee money, stop going after \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , my son's on the board and getting paid tons of money and that happened. That's what we were looking at a Democrat said, oh, there's nothing there, but somehow \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has to pardon for all that time frame? I think that's suspicious in and of itself.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Chairman Jordan and Chairman Comer, thank you. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Here with more reaction, FOX News legal analyst, Gregg Jarrett, Harvard law professor \uc2 Alan Dershowitz\uc2 , "Just the News" CEO, editor-in chief, John Solomon.\par \par \uc2 John, start with you on the news side of this, and all three of you were very, very active and helpful in terms of going in deep and hard and helping to unpeel the layers of the onion involving \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , Elena Baturina, Kazakhstan, other countries.\par \par \uc2 John, where do you see in terms of the new administration, to me, this goes way beyond Hunter, just \uc2 Burisma\uc2  alone, and what about all the people that benefited financially and what about Joe?\par \par \uc2 JOHN SOLOMON, JUST THE NEWS CEO AND EDITOR IN CHIEF: Well, listen, I think there's something that a lot of people aren't thinking about tonight but it is -- it has great roots in the O.J. Simpson case.\par \par \uc2 All right. You can't bring criminal charges against \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  but there's nothing that prevents the Trump Justice Department from filing a fraud case and seeking civil remedy and taking money from him and other members of the family on allegations that they reported false information they committed fraud. Those are things that are still on the table. A pardon doesn't protect you from civil actions.\par \par \uc2 It also doesn't protect you from no he no longer will be able to deny or say, I don't want to testify in any proceedings because I invoked my Fifth Amendment right against incrimination, the president took that away from him so he's going to have to testify if he's compelled, and there's a strong possibility a civil case could still be brought and by the way the proof for a civil case much lower than a criminal case.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What do you think, Gregg Jarrett -- it seems to me based on a lot of investigative reporting by you and John and others that there are and what we just heard from both Congressman Comer and Jordan that there are a lot of other family members impacted here? What should a new incoming attorney general be doing with that?\par \par \uc2 GREGG JARRETT, FOX NEWS LEGAL ANALYST: They should be digging through the files assuming they haven't yet been shredded by the big truck parked out in front of the DOJ. You know, this sweeping pardon, Sean, is not only beneficial to Hunter but it's self-serving for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  himself because there is of course compelling evidence that the father actively aided and abetted his son's financial scheme, selling access, promises of influence.\par \par \uc2 I mean, that's what China, Ukraine, Russia and other countries were buying in exchange for tens of millions of dollars funneled into Biden control shell companies. By his pardon, the president didn't just wipe out Hunter's two convictions -- no. He granted clemency for a decade, 11 years to be precise, of other uncharged crimes in which the document show the father was implicated as an accessory.\par \par \uc2 So by foreclosing any future charges against the son, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  effectively impedes further inquiry into his own crooked role. And by protecting his son, he is protecting himself, the Ukrainian quid pro quo, the $5 million Chinese pay to play deal.\par \par \uc2 So this grant of clemency so broad as it is, is far more cunning and devious than meets the eye.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, I've said many times, Professor, that I want the weaponization of justice to end in this country and I want a permanent, I want the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , I want our intelligence community restored to their former greatness.\par \par \uc2 But there is a lot of evidence that we know of in this case that does implicate not president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  but Vice President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . You know, the WhatsApp message, I'm sitting here next to my father, the laptop from hell. I give half of my income to pops, exchanges with I believe Eric Schwerin that said, you know, which account should I pay for pops home repairs for example.\par \par \uc2 In other words, that he was a beneficiary and evidence that he met with some of these foreign business partners. What should happen?\par \par \uc2 ALAN DERSHOWITZ\uc2 , FORMER HARVARD LAW PROFESSOR: Well, this is a gift to Pam Bondi and a gift to the House Judiciary and Senate committees because they have taken away his Fifth Amendment privilege. He is now the star witness going forward for years and years and years. This may end up not being a great benefit to a \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Look, if Biden was smart, what he would have done is he would have announced that he is pardoning all the nonviolent protesters on December 6th, he's pardoning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he's pardoning all the people that were prosecuted because they were close --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You mean January 6.\par \par \uc2 DERSHOWITZ: -- to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and he -- January 6 -- and he's also pardoning -- he's also pardoning \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . He would have been able to do it on principled ground, but instead it's a one-off and it looks like it's designed to protect the Biden family.\par \par \uc2 But it to backfire because Pam Bondi could convene a grand jury, could start investigations, the Judiciary Committee, calling \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  who no longer has a Fifth Amendment privilege unless they try to concoct an argument that, well, maybe he violated some state law. I don't think that's possible, in light of the combination of the statute of limitations and the pardon, I think he can be called to testify against his father, against his uncle, against any associates. So I don't think we're going to see -- yeah?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Exit question for all of you. Should \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pardon himself and other family members involved? John Solomon, yes or no?\par \par \uc2 SOLOMON: I won't advise, but I don't -- I think he will before we're done, I think he will before January 20th.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I agree with you.\par \par \uc2 Gregg?\par \par \uc2 JARRETT: I absolutely think he will. He shouldn't if he cares one whit about the rule of law and justice in America.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Professor, last word, yes or no?\par \par \uc2 DERSHOWITZ: So I'm a dissenting -- I'm a dissenting view here. He is not going to pardon anybody else. He has exhausted what he wants to do in terms of his son. He shouldn't pardon anybody else. I don't think he will.\par \par \uc2 We'll see and we'll come back, and you can complain about me or I can complain about you. We'll see what happens on January 20th.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. When we come back -- thank you all -- the media melting down after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  nominated Kash Patel to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Plus, Trump derangement syndrome, it has hit a new low. You won't believe what the left is doing now. Well, you'll get a special take from Adam Corolla straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  he made it very clear over the weekend that change is coming to Washington, D.C., in the swamp. In fact, his pick to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , former \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2  chief of staff Kash Patel is now causing a total complete meltdown on the left. Key Republicans they are on board, including people like -- well, now, \uc2 Trey Gowdy\uc2 , that works here with us in FOX, Texas Senator Ted Cruz, House Speaker Mike Johnson, both say Patel is well-qualified prepared, to bring integrity back to the bureau.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  issued a very stern warning to