rump will be sentenced on criminal charges. That's next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ALINA HABBA, SENIOR TRUMP ADVISER: It should be dismissed. It should never have been brought. And if Judge Merchan wants to have any dignity, any - any dignity from the American people in the robe, in the office of all attorneys and judges and the DOJ, he should stop this nonsense right away.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: All right, Trump attorney Alina Habba arguing the president-elect's New York criminal case should be tossed. We are awaiting the judge's decision, due by Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 And we are back with our panel.\par \par \uc2 Juan, I'm guessing you don't agree with her.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: Well, to me, I am not sure about the law, but I am sure about this, that what I've heard from my conservative colleagues this morning is, President - former - elect president - President-elect Trump won the popular vote. I think it's very hard right now for the Justice Department or any judge to say this president-elect must go to jail. It just seems like, wow.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: It could be something short of jail. I mean there - there could be - if he decides the case survived, then there's a sentencing issue.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: Yes. So, he's an elderly man, right. And typically, that would be factored in, as well as the fact that he was convicted and penalties paid. So, you're right, there are other ways that he could be penalized.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Kevin, what do you think he does? I mean, Judge Merchan has moved and moved and moved this thing. It feels like we're due for a decision.\par \par \uc2 KEVIN ROBERTS\uc2 , PRESIDENT, THE HERITAGE FOUNDATION: Well, our Fox friend and legal scholar, Jonathan Turley, said it right. He calls in a circus. And maybe the circus master will finally realize the gig is up. That's what I'm hoping for. That's what will be right and just. Even people who didn't