rt by December 2nd. Looks like he's going to step down.\par \par \uc2 But there is more potentially to come. NBC News reporting this, "the looming question in the weeks ahead is whether Smith's final report detailing his charging decisions will be made public before Inauguration Day. The special counsel's office is required under Justice Department regulations to provide a confidential report to Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , who can choose to make it public."\par \par \uc2 Do you think, Stef, at this point, the DOJ's like, all right, we're - we're closing this chapter, or is that - or that one last dig at, here's what we are alleging the president did?\par \par \uc2 KIGHT: I mean you can see it going either way. But, you know, I do think that the Justice Department has been very aware of the political dynamics. And it is hard to imagine that Trump winning as resoundingly as he did as he's entering office that the Department of Justice would decide to release something like that right at the end. I find that hard to believe, but you never know.\par \par \uc2 And there also is the question of, the American people also want to know what - what has been going on there. What are the findings? What is behind the decision-making at the same time. So, that could also be an argument for releasing a report like that, and explaining to the American people, this is what the investigation has looked like, this is what has come out of it. Whether that would be helpful to the political conversation is another question.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: I think there's one other factor, which is there may be other people who could be charged and other people who have gone to jail because of January 6th. So, the question is, will it have impact on these other cases?\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Yes. We'll have to wait and see.\par \par \uc2 But I also want to note this week that FEMA administrator \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2  is going to be on Capitol Hill after the wake of this story where a FEMA worker, a canvasser, there were notes that she had that said to avoid Trump homes. And she is saying that came from above her and she is being scapegoated and it was about making sure they avoided confrontations. Apparently that had been their experience with some homes.\par \par \uc2 Here she is talking to our Trace Gallagher on "FOX NEWS AT NIGHT."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRACE GALLAGHER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Did this also happen in other our place? This was Florida. But did it happen in North Carolina? Did it happen in other places?\par \par \uc2 MARN'I WASHINGTON, FIRED FEMA WORKER: Georgia as well. Just ask the crew leads and the specialists. They will discuss their avoidance and their de- escalation methods in the field.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: OK.\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON: And I think Ms. Criswell would be happy to know what's going on, truly.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: I mean, Juan, when this happened, \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2  talked about this employee. You know, it was reprehensible. We've taken care of this. This person's no longer with up. But this woman is saying she got his orders from someone else, and that it is more widespread than we know. I mean how much of a grilling do you think the administrator will get this week on The Hill?\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: Well, it should - it should be looked into. It's wrong. You can't do that. I mean if you discriminated against anybody, against poor people, people living off the grid or whatever, those people deserve help in the midst of crisis.\par \par \uc2 Now, I will say that what we heard from Republican governors and Republican mayors and county officials was that FEMA was out there and doing their job. So, it's inconsistent with that. But I don't know the truth of what this woman said. And if - the idea that anybody would be left by government unattended at a moment of need is wrong.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Stef, I mean, this is one of those, now that we're kind of into a lame-duck period, it's one of the hearing that might actually get attention.\par \par \uc2 KIGHT: Yes, and I do think it's important for hard question to be asked about this situation. And I think it's very unfortunate. You know, this was - it could have been an isolated innocent. It could have been a broader issue. But it comes in this context of already massive distrust in FEMA. It already comes as people feel like they can't turn to the government to take care of them, to protect them in their hour of need, when they're faced with disaster.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, I have family near Asheville. I went and visit and volunteered a little bit after the storm there and heard from people who really did not feel like they were being served the way they should.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, I would also love for that woman who's now been dismissed to testify on The Hill because she sounds like she genuinely wants to help the administrator understand what has been going on. Maybe she'll be part of the hearing too. I'm not a member of the commission, so I don't have any control over that.\par \par \uc2 OK, panel, thank you very much. We'll see you next Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, a sneak preview, an in-depth look at the lives of catholic saints, flaws and all, by a world-renowned Hollywood heavyweight. It's coming to Fox Nation.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: We've got a fascinating new series debuting on Fox Nation today. The first episode of Martin Scorsese presents "The Saints" is available on foxnation.com. The series takes a deep dive into religious figures as people who struggle just like we do. Scorsese sat down for an interview on the set of "The Saints" to talk a bit about the episode on Joan of Arc.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MARTIN SCORSESE, EXECUTIVE PRODUCER: A 14-year-old girl hears voices. The voices of saints, the word of God. They tell her to dress in men's clothes, organize an army, lead French soldiers into battle to put the Armagna Pin (ph) on the throne (ph), which she does. She becomes a political liability. She's captured. She's tried. She's condemned. She's burned at the stake. And at that point a dove soars from out of the fire. So, I think that's very compelling.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Martin Scorsese presents "The Saints" is available exclusively on Fox Nation starting today.\par \par \uc2 And a quick note, my podcast, "Livin' the Bream" drops today. This week I sat down with Alabama Senator Katie Britt to talk about the changes and challenges coming to the Senate when it flips to GOP control in January, and about her book, "God Calls Us to Do Hard Things." "Livin' the Bream" anywhere you like to get your podcasts.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us today. Thank you for joining us. I'm Shannon Bream. Have a wonderful week. We'll see you next FOX NEWS SUNDAY.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXN000020241117ekbh00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Republicans Now Have Control Of The House, Senate And Presidency\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Tammy Bruce, Tomi Lahren, Brett Velicovich, Leo  Terrell \par \uc2 8,085 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 November 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And it is a new day in America and in just a matter of weeks, Republicans will officially take control of the White House, the Senate, the House of Representatives, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a clear mandate to fix what is broken and there are many things.\par \par \uc2 So make no mistake, big changes, they are coming to the Washington, D.C. swamp. Now, whether it's the city's bureaucrats, whether they like it or not, whether left-wing extremists, the liars, the alarmists, like it or not, well, here is President Trump moments ago from beautiful Mar-a-Lago which is worth $1.5 billion, not $18 million.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , PRESIDENT-ELECT OF THE UNITED STATES: And Mike Waltz who's going to be doing a little other work for us in the very near future. We just nominated him and he's going to be doing a great job in the administration.\par \par \uc2 We have a man who has a seriously high IQ. You know, I'm a person that believes in high IQs, and his is about as high as they get. He launched a rocket three weeks ago, and then he went to Pennsylvania to campaign because he considered this more important than launching rockets that cost billions of dollars. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  -- Elon.\par \par \uc2 Another one who's another great mind and a great guy and so popular, and I think he's right. He wants to make people healthy. It's driven him pretty wild over the last number of years.\par \par \uc2 Today, I nominated him for, I guess if you like health and if you like people that live a long time, it's the most important position, RFK Jr..\par \par \uc2 Won the White House, recaptured the Senate and now as of today, recaptured the House. Thank you very much, Congressman, and on track -- looks like we have it -- the largest margin in the national vote in presidential year since 1928. That's a long time ago. Well, that's interesting, that's when this house was built, 1928.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's pause for a second and imagine for one second that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was the president-elect. Well, no, let's not go there.\par \par \uc2 That speech does cap what was another very busy day for the president-elect as he continues to fill out his cabinet at a rapid pace, as the president- elect just mentioned. Today, Trump nominated \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  to run the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 . In a statement he put up on X, Kennedy vowed to advance \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's vision to make America healthy again.\par \par \uc2 So, tonight, a word of advice, tune out the noise and the hysteria all predictable from the state run media mob, he wants to bring back polio and the measles, they're going crazy as usual, and, of course, the Washington establishment.\par \par \uc2 Let's listen to what RFK Jr. is actually saying. Here is another part of the statement, quote, together, we will clean up corruption, stop the revolving door between industry and government and return our health agencies to their rich tradition of gold standard, evidence-based science. I will provide Americans with transparency and access to all the data so they can make informed choices for themselves and their families.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy's goal is and always has been to increase government transparency. And by the way, the free flow of information and then guess what? Let you the American people make your own decisions about your health care, about your food, about the issues of vaccines for your children. He's saying -- liberals I think would like this -- that he's pro-choice but he's pro informed choices. In other words, you know that's called freedom.\par \par \uc2 Now, despite what you might hear from the dishonest, well, frankly dead legacy journalists, he's not on a mission to ban medicine. He's not on a mission to ban your food. He's definitely not anti-vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ROBERT F. KENNEDY JR\uc2 . (I), FORMER PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: What my job is not to do as little top down control as possible and just get good information to the American people. So we don't have good science because the agencies deliberately don't do that science because they don't want people to know what they're eating. What I'm going to do is make sure that Americans have good information, good -- the best gold standard science about their food and medicines and then leave the choice to them.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: You have been a crusader on questioning vaccines. Are there specific vaccines that you would seek to take off the market?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: Oh, I'm not going to -- I'm not going to take away anybody's vaccines. I -- and I've never been anti-vaccine. I've just --\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: You will not -- you will not take any vaccine that is currently on the market?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: I'm not -- if somebody -- if vaccines are working for somebody, I'm not going to take them away.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, truth, transparency, that matters. This is a government that is supposed to be for the people, by the people, not a cabal of unelected bureaucrats making secret, sometimes arbitrary, sometimes beneficial to them decisions and then imposing their values and beliefs on the American people and their children through dictates and mandates.\par \par \uc2 And you might remember, oh, the CDC, the six feet of social distancing guidelines, we now know it was totally random, none of it was based on, quote, the science. What about the government's war against the very real science of natural immunity? God forbid if \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  ever talked about that.\par \par \uc2 What about the claims that the COVID vaccines were 99 percent effective? If you got the shot, you're not going to get COVID, and by the way, you won't infect others which turned out to be a complete lie.\par \par \uc2 What about those federal and state mask mandates? Remember them, the ones the Democrats loved -- the mandatory shutdowns, the mandatory lockdowns?\par \par \uc2 Look at this 2023 headline from "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 ", quote, the mask mandates did nothing. Will any lessons be learned? Here's the lesson, government secrecy, deception control doesn't work, and it's not the American way.\par \par \uc2 It did not save lives. It did not prevent the spread of COVID. It just caused misery, isolation fear and there are still some brainwashed people liberals leftists in this country. Actually, occasionally, I'll be driving. I'll look over. I'll see somebody alone in their car with a mask on. Like why? Why do you have a mask on?\par \par \uc2 Now, freedom of information, freedom of thought, freedom will return to Washington D.C. And RFK Jr., to his credit, is the right person to lead this effort at \uc2 HHS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now, can America to do better on issues like obesity and heart disease and strokes and diabetes? Can we get rid of chemicals and hormones in our food like Europe? You know, it is time to make America healthy again through accountability and through transparency.\par \par \uc2 Now, this will be one of the major themes from the new Trump administration, freedom from bureaucracy, the freedom to choose for you and your family, the permanent state has become too bloated, too restrictive, too powerful, and it is pushing the American dream out of reach for so many people.\par \par \uc2 But that's all about to change and not a moment too soon, because America is the last place on Earth where your dreams no matter how big can still become a reality.\par \par \uc2 A few years ago, critics doubted \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and his vision for space. Oh, after decades of government in action, well, Musk was able to revolutionize high speed satellite Internet, he created new cost-effective Starship transport systems, he launched more than a hundred rockets into space this year alone.\par \par \uc2 He also is the guy that our government needs to go to space to save astronauts that are currently trapped in space. Remember, he's the guy that got communications to people in remote areas after Hurricane Helene, and by 2030, he is planning a manned mission to Mars. This is all possible in spite of your government, not because of your government.\par \par \uc2 The American people can and will lead the world into a brighter future but the -- but freedom in all things, including health care, must be restored. Look at it this way, when government promises you free housing and health care and education and child care and early child education and guaranteed government healthy food and this and that -- well, $93 trillion.\par \par \uc2 How's Social Security and Medicare work it out for you because they're both headed towards insolvency? How did they promise to keep your doctor and your plan and save on average $2,500 a year? Well, millions of Americans lost their doctors, lost their care and we are all paying about 250 to 300 percent more per year for healthcare, 40 percent of Americans have one Obamacare option choice and that's it.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here with reaction, Dr. Mehmet Oz is with us.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Oz, good to have you. Thanks for being with us.\par \par \uc2 DR. MEHMET OZ, PROFESSOR EMERITUS, COLUMBIA UNIVERSITY: Glad to be with you, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let's talk about our current health care system. You know, we have, what, $4.5 trillion health budget for chronic illness, we have the world's biggest health bill, 77 percent of young adults can't qualify f