racy, racist, fascist, Nazi, to welcome to the White House? How are you? It's so good to see you. Everything going well in your life.\par \par \uc2 How did that happen, Monica?\par \par \uc2 MONICA CROWLEY, PODCAST HOST: Well, you know, Sean, there's spin in a campaign and like legitimate criticism of your opponent and then there's just outright lying and propaganda. And what we saw coming from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and the Democrats over the course of this entire campaign was just a continuation of the lies, smears and attacks on President Trump that really began nine and a half years ago when he first came on the scene.\par \par \uc2 So smearing him and ratcheting up the rhetoric and the lies that he is literally Hitler, we're all garbage, death to democracy, that kind of rhetoric did not fly because it was so clearly false. And now, what President Trump with his massive victory has shown is that he has exposed all of them for the liars that they are and they don't even believe their lies, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, Leo, a part of me really believes that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  feels vindicated. He was kicked to the curve by Pelosi and Schumer and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and the likes of \uc2 George Clooney\uc2 , and he's kind of thinking in his head, I told you so. I've got to imagine there's vindication there.\par \par \uc2 LEO TERRELL, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Oh, yeah, there's vindication. I mean he's happy Kamala lost, let's be very clear. But let me just pound on this issue.\par \par \uc2 The big lie was told not only by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , told -- it was told by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . It was told by the legacy media, and what was the collateral damage to all the line that Trump was Hitler, Trump was a racist, Trump had -- was a threat to democracy? They almost cost this man his life.\par \par \uc2 The people reacted to this -- this 24/7 bombardment. Trump was the worst person on earth, it was a big lie, Look at the demographics, look at the demographics, Blacks, Hispanics, Jews, union workers voted for this alleged racist. The Democrats knew it was a lie but they would do anything for power and control. But the collateral damage that we almost lost the president because some idiots believe all these lies. That's the big story.\par \par \uc2 And Charlamagne Tha God, shame on him because he carried the lie without having any facts to support it. It's insulting. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  owed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  an apology.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: There is a real danger. When you tell people things that are not true, you tell old people he's going to take your Social Security and your Medicare, you're lying and scaring old people. He's going to take away IVF treatment, limit access to contraception, he'll support a national abortion ban, you're lying.\par \par \uc2 When you say he's Hitler, Stalin, Mussolini, a Nazi, a fascist -- Monica, they are putting into the minds of deranged people that you battling real evil and it's all a show? And there's -- is there not a real danger to all of that -- all of that rhetoric?\par \par \uc2 CROWLEY: Oh, absolutely, Sean. And in fact, we have seen this throughout history, with tyrants who come to power. They use this kind of inflammatory language to dehumanize their opponents, to dehumanize entire sections of society and they leveraged that to try to dehumanize President Trump, so they could justify in the public's mind the lawfare, trying to jail him, trying to bankrupt him.\par \par \uc2 And to Leo's point, you know, we saw two assassination attempts on this man. So they were trying to lay the groundwork in the public's mind psychologically, that all of that was justified because he posed an existential threat to, quote, democracy. But the truth, Sean, is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  poses an existential threat to them, to the system, to the permanent administrative state and their absolute grip on power.\par \par \uc2 So do you see how they warped and twisted the language? But to your point, that kind of inflammatory language gets into the minds of sick people.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Dangerous.\par \par \uc2 CROWLEY: And becomes extremely dangerous and there is no place for it in this country. And I think we saw with President Trump's resounding landslide victory that the American people have rejected that, too.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me give last 30 seconds -- Leo.\par \par \uc2 TERRELL: Well, I'll tell you right now, isn't it amazing after the election, the calmness of this country now. We're respected more overseas. The stock market's doing well. Trump is working on making America great, the temperature has been dropped.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the legacy media, they owe \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  an apology, a big time apology because this should never have happened to him.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, I hope you not -- you don't have relatives that are cancelling Thanksgiving and Christmas.\par \par \uc2 More "Hannity" after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left tonight. And as always, thank you for being with us. Thank you for making the show possible.\par \par \uc2 Now, don't forget to set your DVR so you never, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled, why? Greg Gutfeld, he's standing by, will put a smile on your face. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020241115ekbe00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Trump Makes More Key Cabinet Appointments\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity \par \uc2 8,073 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And tonight, we are at the end of another huge day for the incoming Trump administration. The brand new Department of Government Efficiency is in full gear with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  leading the way. Coming up, Vivek will join us. He will be here for an exclusive interview.\par \par \uc2 Also, House Speaker Mike Johnson will be here after a big endorsement from President Trump and unanimous support from house of Republicans who just renominated him as speaker. We're also going to show you the president- elect's triumphant return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 But, first, more huge nominations are now rocking the Washington swamp. Breaking only moments ago, we learn that Florida senator, my senator, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , has officially been picked for secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, former Democratic congresswoman turned Republican, \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , was nominated as the director of national intelligence and the third pick of the day is causing a bit of let's call collective radical left-wing meltdown among elites in Washington. On Truth Social, President Trump announced that Florida Congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  has been tapped to serve as the next U.S. attorney general, the head of the DOJ.\par \par \uc2 Now, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  is a lawyer, four-term congressman, longtime ally of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who aggressively helped expose political weaponization at the DOJ of Harris and Biden. So, naturally, the pearl clutching, breathless hysteria on the left has been non-stop. It's gotten bad. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Well, Katie, I've