t -- that's what this new Democratic Party is about.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Obama's A.G. wingman, \uc2 Eric Holder\uc2 , of course, that's nothing compared to his actions in office. Where was the outrage over Holder's -- remember the Mexican gun running scheme that led to the murder of a U.S. Border Patrol agent? Where was the hysteria over Holder's secret federal surveillance of reporters at the A.P., oh, and the FOX News Channel. That seems awfully relevant to the legacy media, right?\par \par \uc2 Did anyone in the state-run media mob, did they ever speak out against the FISA abuse, the weaponization of justice against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , from 2016 on? What about the DOJ's witch hunt based on, let's see, Russian disinformation that was bought and paid for by Hillary Clinton. That was the basis of those FISA warrants.\par \par \uc2 You know, that dirty Russian disinformation dossier that was used as the bulk of information to secure four FISA warrant applications to spy on candidate Trump, his transition team and President Trump.\par \par \uc2 Did anyone at the state-run legacy media mob ever condemn this ever? No, the opposite occurred. They peddle these lies and conspiracy theories for three years.\par \par \uc2 By the way, no wonder, they've had no impact in this last election cycle. No wonder Americans do not and should not trust them. Did any Democrats or legacy media people lose sleep over the documented widespread anti-Trump bias at the DOJ the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , where was the moral panic over the scheme to pre- bunked what was the very truth Hunter Biden laptop story.\par \par \uc2 We had 51 former intel officials never had to explain a thing. They never examined Hunter's laptop. They never saw Hunter's laptop. They didn't know a thing about Hunter's laptop, but they all in unison were proclaiming looks like Russian disinformation only a few weeks before an election that according to poll's had an impact on the outcome of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Were they ever held accountable? No. To this day, does anyone in the media mob care that it was wink and \uc2 Tony Blinken\uc2  that organized the disinformation campaign of the 51 former intel officials? No.\par \par \uc2 What about the unequal system of justice. Let's see, wasn't Mar-a-Lago raided over the issue of top secret classified documents. But didn't \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  -- didn't they just get a little polite talking to after having troves of top secret classified document in Joe's case in four separate locations and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . Why -- why were their homes raided? Does that seem like equal justice under the law?\par \par \uc2 How come Hillary Clinton can destroy 33,000 subpoenaed emails, we'd never heard of it before, with Bleach Bit and then destroyed devices with hammers and remove SIM cards and nobody in the Democratic Party, not one person, nobody in the legacy media mob, they never -- they never cared a whit, they didn't care at all. They hit it. They defended it.\par \par \uc2 Anyone on the left concerned that a former president -- current presidential candidate got hit with 34 stacked felony charges based on this ridiculous novel legal theory after the statute of limitations were long passed brought by a left-wing attorney general who campaigned on getting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? Did they ever speak out about that?\par \par \uc2 What about Catholics and angry parents that show up at school board meetings that were labeled extremists and terrorists or potential terrorists? Why were they -- why were peaceful pro-life protesters, why would they targeted?\par \par \uc2 Over the past decade, we have witnessed spying, censorship, lawfare, corruption, intimidation, extreme political bias, all from the Harris-Biden DOJ and, of course, you got \uc2 James Comey\uc2 , you had the whole Mueller investigation, three long years, Russia, Russia, Russia, the state-run media mob. They're now only worried about \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This is feign, selective, moral outrage and frankly it's ridiculous. Now, for years, the DOJ and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the Washington field office have been totally completely out of control. We have been chronicling this regularly. They have had a get Trump by any means necessary mentality, and the American people eight days ago, you saw through all of it.\par \par \uc2 You didn't listen to the media, the celebrity endorsements, the people putting on the concerts for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  because they have no impact. They have -- they have so overreached so often, people are sick of it. And now, they've completely lost the trust of more than half of the country and now change is coming to Washington, change that was promised.\par \par \uc2 And despite his time in Congress, Gaetz is not a Washington insider. Nobody would call him that. He is not well-liked by the city swamp creatures that might be a plus of my book. But does he have an unyielding fearless ability to disrupt the status quo, whether you agree or disagree, and this is exactly why he became \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's pick for attorney general.\par \par \uc2 Again, this is not business as usual. After last week's election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a mandate to reform what I call these once great institutions to end once and for all the weaponization of justice in America, to restore principles that I and so many of you hold near and dear to your heart, equal justice under the law, equal application of our laws, flush out the political bias that the DOJ, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and our -- in our intelligence community restore these departments, these agencies to their original missions, not -- not political and their former greatness.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  used to be formerly one of the great the greatest law enforcement agency on earth. Our intelligence community, the greatest on earth. We've got to get them back to where they were.\par \par \uc2 Now, conservative -- as conservatives, we deeply believe in these principles and what has been done to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over nine years and to Republicans can and should never ever, ever happen to any American, Democrat or Republican, ever again. In other words, Republicans they must pledge to never do to Democrats what was done to them and what was done to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and what was done to Trump allies.\par \par \uc2 And today, after years of lawfare and two attempts on his life and non-stop media outrage and comparisons to Hitler and Stalin and Mussolini, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returned to the White House for a meeting with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in what could be a sign of things to come, the meeting apparently went very well. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was all smiles as the 45th, 46th and 47th president exchanged kind words. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Well, Mr. President-Elect and former president --\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , PRESIDENT-ELECT OF THE UNITED STATES: Thank you very much, Joe.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: -- and -- Donald, congratulations.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: And looking forward to having a, like we said, smooth transition -- do everything we can to make sure you're accommodated, what you need. And we're going to get a chance to talk about some of that today. So --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Good.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: -- welcome. Welcome back.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you very much. And thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 And politics is tough. And it's, many cases, not a very nice world, but it is a nice world today. And I appreciate it very much -- a transition that's so smooth it'll be as smooth as it can get.\par \par \uc2 And I very much appreciate that, Joe.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: You're welcome.\par \par \uc2 Thank you all.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: President Trump told "The New York Post" that Biden was very gracious that it was very enjoyable, the meeting, and based on White House pictures, Joe and Jill Biden seem very happy to see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And the first lady even reportedly handed Trump a handwritten letter for his wife Melania, welcoming her back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Now, keep in mind, just this week the vibes were kind of different when Jill and Kamala were seated next to each other at a veterans day event as you can see right there.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake, it is a new era in the Washington swamp and it appears and I hope it's true, that Trump will have a new ally in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 . The newly minted majority leader \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , he is pledging to work to get the president's agenda through, time will tell. Here's what he said.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOHN THUNE\uc2  (R-SD): It's a new day in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  and it's a new day in America. The American people have loudly rejected the failed policies of the Biden, Harris, Schumer agenda, and this Republican team is united. We are on one team. We are excited to reclaim the majority and to get to work with our colleagues in the House to enact President Trump's agenda.\par \par \uc2 We have a mandate from the American people, a mandate not only to clean up the mess left by the Biden, Harris, Schumer agenda, but also to deliver on President Trump's priorities.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Time is short. There's a lot of work to be done but now is the time for Republicans to work together and get \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's agenda across the finish line.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now with more is \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Great to have you back.\par \par \uc2 Let us talk about all that your family has been through and the utter silence not only of Democrats but the legacy media which for nine-plus years has been after your family and in the end, all their reporting, all their hysteria, all their screaming and yelling and ranting and raving and proclamations of whatever about your father-in-law were meaningless. It had no impact on the American people.\par \par \uc2 What does that say to you?\par \par \uc2 LARA TRUMP, RNC CO-CHAIR: Yeah, well, the American people don't buy it, Sean, and you know, you had the proof of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for four years in the White House previously, and that's why the American people overwhelmingly came out on November 5th and voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his America First policies, and it's incredible to see how people are so upset about, you know, the \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  pick and they're very worried I think about some sort of revenge or retribution by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But let's be very clear, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said my revenge will be success and success will bring us together and unify us. Take a look at that meeting he had with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  today, by the way. Could not have been nicer, could not have been friendlier.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was all smiles there and you saw the way that those two men got along, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was very professional in that meeting. Listen, no one understands more so how broken some of these systems are and how they need to be restored in the faith that we as the American people have need to be restored in these systems more so than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They were all weaponized against him. He doesn't want retribution. He wants success for America and the American people. He wants energy dominance. He wants us to regain our standing on the world stage.\par \par \uc2 He wants to make community safer and make life better for the American people and he knows that the best way to get his revenge is the way that he has always done it, Sean, it's proving his critics wrong and every single time they say \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can't do it, he can't get the job done. Guess what? He always comes through for the American people.\par \par \uc2 I think we're poised as he says to see the golden age of America and it'll be thanks to \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Your husband \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  was quoted in "The Daily Mail" saying that his father has no interest in retribution and even said that he would likely strongly consider pardoning \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  as a sign of goodwill. And now, we have this issue involving \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , and I've got to believe \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  who's been fighting against weaponization will make a strong statement against it with a promise never to do it. Your reaction.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Yeah. I think that's exactly right. I think that we want to get back to an America where we look at each other not as Democrats or Republicans but as Americans and that's what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been fighting for he's fighting whether you voted for him or not, for you out there, for your life to be better and for the America first policies, again things like closing our border and keeping our streets safer, giving respect back to our law enforcement officers.\par \par \uc2 These are things that are going to really positively impact people's lives. I think that if it is not already done by the time January 20th rolls around, you may see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pardon \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  because, Sean, we should put all this in the past. We should start focusing on actually doing effective things for the American people, with people like \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  that you heard about today, that is going to actually impact people's lives. You should never see any of these systems weaponized against an American citizen like what has happened to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  multiple times.\par \par \uc2 No one -- again no one understands this better than he does, and no one wants to see it brought to an end more than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: "The New York Post" is with the appointment of Senator Rubio to be the next secretary of state is saying that you apparently are a top choice of Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  to replace \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 . Have you had any conversations with Governor DeSantis? And I guess more importantly would you be interested in being I guess my senator because Marco's leaving me?\par \par \uc2 Would you -- would you consider -- would you throw your hat in the ring? Would you want -- would you want that job on the heels of the great job you did at the \uc2 RNC\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Oh, well, thank you. Yeah --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I think we -- just what I wanted the answer. Can we -- is there any chance we can get her back? I think America would like to hear that answer. If we can -- we're going to get it right back up and get an answer to the question. You can't make that up.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here with reaction also is Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , the great state of South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Now, you can't make that up, just -- just when I'm about to get the answer.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 LINDSEY GRAHAM\uc2  (R-SC): Yeah, yeah, like, it's either the Chinese or somebody in Florida that wants this job, I don't know.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I did. I'm one way or the other, I'm getting that answer. I'm going to have her call in if I have to.\par \par \uc2 How would you feel about that by the way?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: I would be like over the top excited. She busted her ass to help President Trump win. She helped the Senate. She helped the House.\par \par \uc2 She is a co-chair of the \uc2 RNC\uc2 . There was no cheating. She raised a ton of money.\par \par \uc2 Nobody understands the American first agenda better than \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 . She's a great mother, a very sharp young lady. I would love to have her as a colleague. That'll be up to Governor DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 But we could not do better on the Republican side than \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, I tend to agree with you. I hope you heard my opening monologue and I mean what I say after all that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been through, and the weaponization of our DOJ. And it's so sad to me that great agencies like the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the CIA have been so politicized the way they've been. Anybody that is not in favor of restoring those a agencies and those -- to their former greatness and those departments to their former greatness to me would be disqualifying.\par \par \uc2 Let's get to the issue and that is you know the hysteria on the left about \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  and Matt has been in the forefront with Jim Jordan of fighting against weaponization.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Does he not deserve a chance to be heard?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Well, not only does he deserve a chance to be heard, every president deserves a chance to pick their cabinet. Elections do matter. When I say elections have consequences and I vote for Democratic nominees that I would not have chosen, I am some kind of great statesman.\par \par \uc2 When I apply that same standard to a Republican president I'm somehow a lackey. I am telling you exactly what I'm going to do. I did it for Bush, I did it for Obama, I did it for Biden, and I'm going to do it for President Trump.\par \par \uc2 He won the election. He deserves a chance to pick his cabinet. I am predisposed to allow him to do that.\par \par \uc2 I think \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  is very bright. I think he's qualified. He'll have a hearing and he'll have some tough questions to answer. But to every Republican, please follow a process to give President Trump the ability to pick the people he thinks can do the job and give Matt a chance to --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And you have a history of that. You --\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: I do it for everybody. I do it for everybody.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And in fairness to you, you are being consistent and I wish Democrats would be as consistent as you are. By the way --\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: They're not going to be --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Stay right there, don't go anywhere because we have \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  back. So hopefully --\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: And the answer is? And the answer is?\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Someone didn't want --\par \par \uc2 HANNTY: And the answer is -- you got a ringing endorsement when you fell off the air from Lindsey.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Oh.\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM: Yeah, LaraTrump.com, LaraTrump.com.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, here we go, here we go.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: Well, listen, I -- I was so truly so honored to be at the co- chair of the \uc2 RNC\uc2  through really the most historic election I think of any of our lifetimes and I was really honored to do it and proud of our team because we accomplished, Sean, everything that we set out to do.\par \par \uc2 We wanted to make sure that we got out our voters. We want to make sure people voted early. We wanted to make sure we had a world class election integrity team and that we actually gave voters the confidence to come out and vote knowing their vote would matter and their vote was would count and there would be no funny business.\par \par \uc2 And obviously, we broke records of fundraising and all the things. So everything we set out to do we did and to be able to serve in this role has really been the honor of a lifetime. Likewise, if I am able to serve I would love to serve the people of Florida. This is my home state now and has been for three years. This is where Eric and I live and truly to have that opportunity I think would be incredible.\par \par \uc2 No one knows better than I do. The America First agenda or the goals of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the coming four years .So if I asked, I would love to consider it, but I have yet to have a conversation with Governor DeSantis, so we will have to see.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And both of you agree, Lindsey, that any nominee of any president, they should be able to choose the cabinet