arlier today when asked about his meeting, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  was short on details as per usual. What a shock. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS SENIOR WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Did President Biden invite Vice President Harris to this meeting with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tomorrow?\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: This is a meeting with the -- with the president and the president-elect. This is the norm that the incoming president and the current president sit down in the Oval Office and have a discussion, and that's how -- that's what you're going to see tomorrow is the norm.\par \par \uc2 What we -- what we normally would see uh when we are talking about a peaceful transition of power.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: President Biden says that he's not going to pardon his son Hunter. Is he going to ask \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to do that?\par \par \uc2 JEAN-PIERRE: I don't have anything else to share about that. I'm not going to get and go down a rabbit hole on this. I've been very clear. The president's been very clear when we've been asked this question.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: In reality, this is not business as usual. In fact, that will be a running theme throughout the second Trump term. And as for \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and that pardon, the president-elect is not ruling it out, for the sake of national unity. We will find out in the days weeks and months to come.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, President Trump said he wouldn't take it off the books despite the egregious lawfare by the Biden administration and the fact that Hunter is, quote, a bad guy or a bad boy to, quote, him exactly.\par \par \uc2 Now, Melania Trump, on the other hand, well, is not quite as forgiving and I don't blame her. According to "The New York Post", she declined an invitation to meet with Dr. Jill Biden tomorrow, citing the unprecedented raid at Mar-a-Lago authorized by the weaponized Department of Justice of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  saying, quote, a source saying, she ain't going.\par \par \uc2 A source familiar with Melania's decision told "The Post", Jill Biden's husband authorized the \uc2 FBI\uc2  snooping through her underwear drawer, and the Bidens are disgusting and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  -- remember this -- they both had top secret classified information. Joe had it in four separate locations. Their homes were not invaded.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  never had used Bleach Bit or used hammers and removed SIM cards and broke up devices. But this weaponization of justice must forever, Democrat, Republican, and it has got to stop. The DOJ, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  being politicized, intel agencies politicized, they now need to return for forever to their original non-political purpose and their former greatness. That has got to be the goal.\par \par \uc2 But the Bidens will soon be out of the White House once and for all. And on January 20th, 2025, the reckoning will begin in the Washington swamp. The monolithic far left city that does not represent the whole of America is about to be rocked to its core but despite the fearmongering on the left, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is not threatening democracy. He's not threatening our Constitution.\par \par \uc2 America's massive bureaucracy on the other hand will soon face a very heavy dose of reality. Again, this is not going to be business as usual. That is not what the American people voted for. The decentralization of power as our founders intended is very much on its way to D.C.\par \par \uc2 And the new Department of Government Efficiency will take an ax to government waste fraud and abuse. In fact, Trump now plans to eliminate the entire Department of Education, send that money directly to the states. They would better know how to use it.\par \par \uc2 Other departments like the \uc2 EPA\uc2  and the \uc2 Bureau of Land Management\uc2  can soon be relocated outside of the Washington swamp and expect to see a major overhaul of the DOJ, DHS and the \uc2 FBI\uc2 's Washington field office. Government agencies have been unaccountable and frankly out of control for far too long.\par \par \uc2 And a pervasive far-left bias has tarnished America's once great institution. They need to be restored. The only way to carry out, the MAGA agenda, and restore equal justice under the law is to reform America's bloated anti-Trump bureaucracy.\par \par \uc2 Now, this will be a tall order, but it is one of the most important things the president must do at the very beginning of his administration. The stakes are high, the problems are big, the border, it must be secured immediately, millions of criminal illegal immigrants including gang members, cartel members, drug dealers, people that we know are murderers and rapists, those that are known terrorists, they must be found. They must be deported.\par \par \uc2 Peace, law and order must be restored in every small town and every big city and around the world. America must now lead the way with energy dominance, innovation, development.\par \par \uc2 Americans should not have to settle for a townhouse instead of a home with a backyard. Trump can and will restore the American Dream and get government off of your back. It's called freedom.\par \par \uc2 For far too long, Democratic elites in Washington, they have exerted their powers like petty tyrants. Those days, hopefully, will soon be over and end, and America will start functioning like a true republic once again.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now with reaction, FOX News contributor Katie Pavlich, along with Outkick founder Clay Travis.\par \par \uc2 Good to see you both.\par \par \uc2 Katie, let's talk about the picks.\par \par \uc2 KATIE PAVLICH, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Good to see you, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I mean, the president's moving at rapid speed. Your reaction to some of the selections, including our friend, our colleague Pete Hegseth.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: Well, everyone's at the same -- on the same page, and when it comes to Pete Hegseth, I was texting with a colleague who's a former Pentagon official and she said that DOD employees are going to have to take mental health days tomorrow with this news because Pete Hegseth is dedicated to taking wokeism out of the military, which if you love the U.S. military and you love this country, you have to do.\par \par \uc2 They've been distracted. We live in a very dangerous world and he's vowed to get rid of generals he doesn't care who you are, but if you're distracted from the mission to take care of your virtue signaling and your wokeism, he wants you out of there that goes for a number of different agencies.\par \par \uc2 And I think generally, President Trump has chosen people who are in Washington but not of Washington. They understand how this place works. They know that the bureaucracy is going to bite back and they're ready to fight against the lawyers and to do civil service reform to make sure that the Washington, D.C. is working for the American people, not working for the unelected bureaucrats who think they're entitled to use it, to weaponize it against people who they disagree with in the middle of the country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Clay Travis, when \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  came into office, he had a mission to rebuild our military. At that point, it was a different type of military but bring us to a 600 ship navy. He talked about what he called at that time a gap of vulnerability and that meant that we were falling behind militarily.\par \par \uc2 I believe America is now currently in this a very similar place and that is we don't have hypersonic missile technology but China, Russia and I believe North Korea do. We have wokeism all throughout the Pentagon, all throughout our military. Recruitment is way down.\par \par \uc2 This is now going to be a big task. America is going to have to spend money to catch up and to surpass technologically the weaponry the sophisticated weaponry of war that is used today. Your reaction?\par \par \uc2 CLAY TRAVIS, OUTKICK FOUNDER: What, well, well, first of all, congrats to Pete. I was on live with him a week ago when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was winning from Kid Rock's honky talk on Broadway, in Nashville, and I would just like to say, if I had known he was going to be secretary of defense, I might have had a few less beers, Sean.\par \par \uc2 But I mean, I love this. He is exactly what our military needs and more importantly, I love everything that I'm seeing from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's cabinet. He's moving fast. He's surrounding himself with people who are loyal, people who recognize that our government is broken and it's time to start fixing things.\par \par \uc2 And let me say, this attorney general pick, you were perfect on this leading in, \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 . It is the most important decision that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has to make because of all the broken parts of our government right now, the Department of Justice I think is the single most broken. And you were talking about pardons, here's how I would suggest Trump should start off. Pardon every January 6th or pardon \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  even though he doesn't deserve it and pardon Eric Adams because I think New York city's mayor, they're coming after him because he called them out on the failures at the border, say, we're done with political prosecutions. You can argue for anything, the First Amendment is alive and well in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's America, but we're not putting people in prison because of what they advocate for politically.\par \par \uc2 And I got a badass attorney general who's going to make sure the next four years, it's big in America.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Can he pardon Adams or is it going to be a state charge that Adams is facing?\par \par \uc2 TRAVIS: Right now, I believe they're federal charges right from the Southern District of New York. That doesn't mean that they might not bring state charges, too, but he could pardon Eric Adams. I would encourage him to do so and just sweep it clean and say this era is over. They came after me, I beat their ass at the polls, and I'm not letting them do it to anybody else.\par \par \uc2 I think it would be an important message and I think it would go a long way towards really setting the tone for what this new era is going to be.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: To me the most important -- go ahead. Go ahead, Katie.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: I was going say, it's -- it's not just these cabinet picks which are very important in terms of people not saying that they're there to keep tabs on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . They're there to serve the president in the executive branch, but there are thousands of positions that are political appointments inside the federal government that last time around during the first term, there were lots of holdovers who worked directly against President Trump's agenda.\par \par \uc2 All of those people are going to go. There are lots of people who are about to step up to the plate to work inside the administration, and the deputies inside of these agencies for these cabinet officials, in addition to the U.S. attorneys, for example, in the southern district of New York or in places across the country are going to be very key to making sure that the government is reformed and that they're focused on the right things, not on political weaponization of the system that belongs to the American people.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Clay, let me go back to this issue though of a weaponized DOJ and a politicized \uc2 FBI\uc2  and politicized intelligence agencies. This has to be wiped out forever so it can never happen again. To me, those will be the most important appointments not just the AG, it's going to be the 30 people that also are immediately below the AG.\par \par \uc2 It's not just going to be the \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, but the -- but the top 30 or 40 or 50 people below him, and the same with the CIA and other intelligence agencies. So, to me, you know, we've got to create a scenario where the DOJ can never be weaponized again and these institutions can never be politicized again. That to me would be cleaning out the swamp.\par \par \uc2 TRAVIS: You're percent right about that sean which is why I think that's the most significant message \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has to send from the absolute star. Katie's right, there's a lot of people at all sorts of levels.\par \par \uc2 But you got to have an AG that actually has a spine of steel because you know they're going to come after him or her with everything they possibly can, you got to have somebody that'll stare them down and say, I'm not making the right decision this week I'm making the right decision for the next hundred years because don't forget when they raided Mar-a-Lago and they brought charges in New York and they brought charges in D.C. and they brought charges in Florida and Atlanta, and I know some of those are state charges, they broke 250 years of established precedent that you don't try and put your chief political rival in prison.\par \par \uc2 Thankfully, Trump won the race but he has to your point grab this stuff from its foundation and tear it apart and ensure that it never ever happens again and that's why these choices that he has to make starting with attorney general I think are the most important of what has already been an excellent cabinet roll out so far.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And return the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to its former greatness. Return our intel agencies to their former greatness and lead them that way. That would be a great accomplishment.\par \par \uc2 Katie, great to see. Clay, thank you.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: Sean, can I just say one more thing quickly? Just one more thing quickly?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Go ahead.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: I just want to say, in order for there to be a cleaning out of the bureaucracy, there has to be accountability for the violation of civil rights for Americans. This FEMA story where they were given a directive, you know, agency-wide to not give aid to Trump supporters --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Crazy.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: -- people should go to jail for that. They should be charged with violating people's civil rights and until you have actual accountability for these people. Nothing is going to change.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Katie and Clay, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Now on X, the current governor of Arkansas, \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , had some very kind words for the former governor of Arkansas -- that being her father, our friend \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2  -- who was just nominated to be the U.S. ambassador to Israel.\par \par \uc2 Governor Sanders wrote, quote: There is no one President Trump could have picked with a greater love for the Israeli people and commitment to the unbreakable bond between America and Israel than him.\par \par \uc2 Joining us with more, President Trump's nominee to be ambassador to Israel, \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Governor, I agree with your daughter. I think she is a better governor and a lot smarter than me, so we both take second place.\par \par \uc2 But in all seriousness, I look at Israel, the size of the state of New Jersey and I look at them now battling a four or five-front war between \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 , Islamic Jihad in the north, you got \uc2 Hamas\uc2  out a Gaza in the south, you got the Houthi rebels and you got ballistic missiles being fired directly from Iran, that is, you know, supplying all of this weaponry because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  allowed them to get rich by not enforcing sanctions.\par \par \uc2 How quickly do you believe \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can impact that -- that conflict in the Middle East?\par \par \uc2 MIKE HUCKABEE\uc2 , FORMER GOVERNOR OF ARKANSAS: Sean, I think he's impacting that conflict before he's even sworn in. You're seeing a scrambling all over the Middle East of countries suddenly trying to behave differently because they know a new sheriff has come to town.\par \par \uc2 And this isn't a one bullet Barney with a bullet in his shirt pocket. This is the real deal. I mean, this is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that they are afraid of, and I'm just ecstatic that he has asked me to be part of what I think is going to be -- not just a realignment of political parties and many institutions in America, but really, the world, to bring peace that we desperately need.\par \par \uc2 And quite frankly, when I look at all these people that he's picked, I'm incredibly impressed with all of them. I feel like that I'm a -- you know, a 1995 Ford pickup trying to enter the Indy 500. I don't see myself in the same view as I do some of these wonderful people he's picked.\par \par \uc2 But I'm honored beyond even description to be able to serve my country --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HUCKABEE: -- and this president in a nation that I've been traveling to since July of 1973 when I was 17, made about a hundred trips there, and I couldn't be more grateful to this president for giving me the opportunity to serve the country and him.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I'm sure you're going to work very closely with my friend Steve Witkoff. He was announced today as the special envoy to the Middle East. Like you, he knows the area well.\par \par \uc2 I think, you know, one of the more interesting picks will be \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 . And I've never been a globalist. I find the United -- \uc2 U.N.\uc2  to be historically, virulently antisemitic and anti-American.\par \par \uc2 I don't trust \uc2 WHO\uc2 . We know they covered for China during COVID.\par \par \uc2 I don't like the WEF. I never like the Paris accords. The Iranian deal is asinine, the worst deal ever made.\par \par \uc2 So I would imagine if the \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  that lectured the pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  professors before Congress -- if that \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  shows up at the United Nations, that's going to be a little bit of a shakeup the likes of which maybe we haven't seen in our lifetime. That could be entertaining.\par \par \uc2 HUCKABEE: It'll be very entertaining but more importantly, it's going to be a great revelation of what's wrong at the \uc2 U.N.\uc2  and why for many years, I've never understood why we kept dumping money into it.\par \par \uc2 I've often said get a jackhammer, hammer the thing right off and float it into the East River and invite any country who thinks they could enjoy it to have it.\par \par \uc2 She's not going to be invited to a lot of after 5:00 cocktail parties in Manhattan where she'll be saluted by the swells.\par \par \uc2 But that's not why she's going and is why she's going to be terrific in that position. She's bold, strong, unafraid, and will take nothing off of any of them.\par \par \uc2 And we need to be bold. There's no reason that you have people like Iran and communist China on human rights committees, talking about human rights when they violate them more than anybody.\par \par \uc2 So it's time for a complete reset of our internal and international relationships. That's what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is clearly setting out to do and I couldn't be more delighted to see this take place.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, one thing that has to happen if the world ever wants to have real peace and safety and security, we can never allow the Iranian mullahs with their radicalism to get nuclear weapons which they are desperately seeking and they have got to be stopped. They are the number one state sponsor of terror. I'd cut off their money.\par \par \uc2 And if they keep firing missiles at Israel, it's time to take out their refineries, take out their nuclear sites, and the world will be a better and safer place in my humble opinion.\par \par \uc2 Congratulations, Governor. I guess I should say ambassador. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, Judge Merchan delaying the ruling in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's criminal case in New York.\par \par \uc2 And Alina Habba reportedly emerging as a candidate for Trump's White House press secretary. She will join us with reaction. That's straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And now, tonight, the left wing's weaponization of justice against President-elect Trump continues to crumble. Earlier today, the judge in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's falsified business document case, Judge Juan Merchan paused all court deadlines, including the November 26 sentencing date to consider the effect of his victory in last week's election.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, attorney for President Trump and his spokesman, legal spokesperson, Alina Habba, has according to reports emerged as a front runner for the role of White House press secretary.\par \par \uc2 Alina joins us now with reaction.\par \par \uc2 First, it was -- it was your legal team that in fact requested this -- this delay, indefinite delay. Finally, Judge Merchan agreed to something. But for all intent and purposes, isn't this case really dead?\par \par \uc2 ALINA HABBA, SENIOR ADVISOR TO PRESIDENT TRUMP: It was dead upon arrival, Sean. We know that. This case was never supposed to be brought. We also know that the DOJ had appointed people, Pomerantz included that were supposed to go in an investigate Trump before he decided to run for office and then when he decided to run for office, they brought charges.\par \par \uc2 We know what this has been. We've been talking about it for years. This was a sham trial that was brought to keep President Trump in the New York court as all these cases were, and they failed.\par \par \uc2 So, now, we have a judge who frankly should have dismissed it today. Hopefully, he will he should, and the Supreme Court has spoken on this. You know, it's exhausting to the American people at this point. I think I think they spoke loudly on November 5th about why they're tired of it and the direction the American people want to go