f the weaponization of Biden's DOJ is their third highest ranking official came in to help \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nobody is going to give up that spot to go work for \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  in New York City when they're the third highest official in the DOJ, but they did that anyway.\par \par \uc2 HABBA: Sean, I one up you on that. Take a look at the White House logs, take a look at the DAs and the \uc2 AGs\uc2  that have come in and coordinated with the president of the United States. That's a Harris administration. That's the woman that just ran against President Trump and lost in a major way.\par \par \uc2 America is done with this. We see it for what it is. It was lawfare. There is nothing he did wrong. They put his legal -- the judges, this -- they tried all the way up to the Supreme Court and lost, and there's a reason for that. The American people are speaking loudly. You cannot attack political opponents who have done nothing wrong.\par \par \uc2 You cannot put people from the DOJ. You cannot put \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 's law firm in charge of prosecuting political opponents. It's un-American.\par \par \uc2 I hope that the American people never have to speak about this again. I really do and I believe President Trump will make sure of that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's talk about the possibility and reports that you might be the president's press secretary. Any truth to it?\par \par \uc2 HABBA: I leave it to the president and three people that are on my board directors. That's Luke, Chloe and Parker, my children. Everybody will know in time.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Now, I got to go in a little harder. Have -- have there been any discussions about it?\par \par \uc2 HABBA: Sean, you know me better than that. You would never have me on prime time if I answered questions like that. Look, President Trump has put together an amazing cabinet. I'm really proud of the work that him and his transition team have done.\par \par \uc2 I think when we look at everybody, they are killing it on all fronts. America's excited for -- frankly -- sorry to use Mrs. Walz's term, but turn a page. It's time to turn the page. It's time to have advocacy for America first.\par \par \uc2 And whatever that looks like for president Trump and his team, I trust it. It's a decision for all of them to make not me.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Serious question, if you were asked to serve in that role or any other role, would you?\par \par \uc2 HABBA: I -- I am very loyal to President Trump. I would think about it, very seriously.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay. We appreciate it. Alina Habba, thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, Trump derangement syndrome has spread like wildfire since the election. Okay, some women, they're now reconsidering having children. Others are stockpiling abortion pills. Some women are divorcing their husbands and refusing to have sex with their partners, can't make it up.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Drew Pinsky will help settle their minds, that is next. It's important, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Election night was exactly one week ago and the left is still not taking the laws well at all. In fact some are resorting to pretty extreme measures.\par \par \uc2 According to reports, some liberal women they are now embracing something called the 4B movement where they are swearing off physical, romantic relationships with men. They're shaving their head. They are stockpiling abortion pills. They are vowing to never have children.\par \par \uc2 Some liberal women are planning to wear blue bracelets to signal to each other that they are liberal. Other women that are on the left are slamming the idea saying it is only -- well, performative virtue signaling.\par \par \uc2 And now, the media mob is getting in on the action by playing to the worst fears of their liberal audience. "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " is now offering a guide on how Americans can flee to other countries. Don't let the door hit you on the ass on the way out. That's my advice. If you don't want to be here you don't have to be here. I believe in freedom.\par \par \uc2 The co-hosts of that hard-hitting news show "The View" say it's okay to boycott Thanksgiving gatherings hosted by relatives that are Trump supporters. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I completely understand her point because I really do feel that this candidate, you know, President-elect Trump, is just a different type of candidate, from the things he's said and the things he's done and the things he will do, it's more of a moral issue for me. And so I think when people feel that someone voted not only against their families but against them and against people that they loved, I think it's okay to take a beat.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Here with reaction, he is the chief patient officer at the Wellness Company, Dr. Drew Pinsky is with us.\par \par \uc2 All right. So women are shaving their heads. They're pledging to either divorce their husbands or partners or don't have sex with them. They're stockpiling abortion pills. They're getting advice from "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " on how to leave the country.\par \par \uc2 Maybe they believed their own lies or the lies that were told during and the hyperbole and the hype and the misinformation during the campaign because there's no reason to leave. I will be the first person to stand up for their right to say stupid things if they want.\par \par \uc2 DR. DREW PINSKY MD, CHIEF PATIENT OFFICER AT THE WELLNESS COMPANY: Yep, yep. Well, I'm just glad to see that they move from the blue talisman over their face and nose to a blue talisman bracelet on their wrist, because it's the same damn thing. And the whole headline here, Sean, is hysteria. Hysteria and delusion and the source of this has been mainstream media.\par \par \uc2 The American public has been propagandized to the point that they literally become mentally ill and the thing about delusionality is it can't be be reasoned with. We have literally been through a stage of delusion that started with the first Trump presidency it was put into absolute orbit with COVID.\par \par \uc2 We now have the new \uc2 HHS\uc2  document that showed how the propaganda was done. How many hundreds of millions of dollars were spent, and vulnerable people were affected by this. And I would say the way to deal with your family are like members that are like this, A, compassionate, firmness, firmness. Not rationality, not discourse because argumentation will not work, they are delusional.\par \par \uc2 But firmness because the reality is this is like a cult. What do cults do? They separate families. They separate the cult member from the family, and this is how they get their way we must fight against that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. If you look at the nine years and every major newspaper in the country, three broadcast channels in the country, every liberal news channel in the country, it was almost 24/7, I hate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is bad, he's evil, he's this, he's that.\par \par \uc2 PINSKY: Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The amazing thing to me, the outcome of this election, all the celebrity endorsements didn't matter, all the musicians playing concerts that didn't matter, all of the legacy media attacking Trump didn't matter, and the American people didn't listen to them. And I've been making the statement that legacy media in America is dead.\par \par \uc2 Am I wrong because if they had any influence at all -- this would not have been the blowout election it became?\par \par \uc2 PINSKY: As my old friend Adam Carolla said to me just yesterday, he said it's like they had a magic wand and the batteries worn out. They're shaking the wand but there's the batteries aren't working anymore.\par \par \uc2 And so, the reality is and this is the way I've been thinking about it, it's that this is old timey stuff. These celebrities are celebrities from the `70s and `80s who used to have sway over our culture and the people that are advocating these old timey strategies -- look, Joe Rogan has the influence, not Julia Roberts and people cannot get that into their heads.\par \par \uc2 There are people -- I was talking to a 40-year-old today, didn't really know who Johnny Carson was, didn't really understand who Valerie Bertinelli was who was attacking me and Adam Carolla during the COVID epidemic. They never heard of these people and if they had heard of them they have no real relevance in their life.\par \par \uc2 It's old, timey, old-fashioned. It is time to move on to the new era. The late night is gone, so many things are over. Gutfeld is the king of late night, he still has sway but this is a new way of doing things.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I would argue in terms of late night comedy shows, I mean, the countdown to cancellation is on. I don't think those shows will survive and that means Kimmel, that means Colbert, that means Fallon because they're not funny and Greg Gutfeld is funny.\par \par \uc2 You got to laugh. You mentioned Julia Roberts. It might have been the funniest political ad in some ways but the saddest in another way where she is telling people narrating a video of a wife going into a voting booth, you -- you don't have to tell that evil husband of yours that you're not voting for Trump. Your vote is private.\par \par \uc2 Or \uc2 George Clooney\uc2  doing the same thing on the other end. You can still be your bro and act like you're voting for Trump. What is that?\par \par \uc2 PINSKY: I got to tell you, if that's actually -- listen, if that was act -- I'm a mandated reporter in my state. If that is actually going on, I have to fill out a bunch of paperwork to report these people for domestic abuse and that leads to domestic violence. Are they implying that all marriages in this country are just on the verge of domestic violence? Is that the implication?\par \par \uc2 It -- and by the way, I would say there are many more men keeping their mouth shut about what they doing in the voting booth.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They're saying lie to your husband and lie to your best friends instead of are you -- are you -- are you that?\par \par \uc2 PINSKY: It's so sick.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Are you -- but they lack pride in their candidate. They have to hide their vote and not admit what they really believe?\par \par \uc2 First of all, is that real marriage? Is that a real friendship? I don't think so.\par \par \uc2 PINSKY: We have -- we have a saying in my field is you're as sick as your secrets. How about the fact that we couldn't express ourselves? I don't know if you experienced this but I noticed that after the election when the American people made a pretty substantial statement, you kind of felt like speech was back, like you could start to talk you could have an opinion and you could have some affect with that opinion.\par \par \uc2 Sunny Hostin, who I've had nothing but affection for whenever I've dealt with her, she's talking about a moral issue as it pertains to a somebody voting for somebody, exactly what is the moral issue? What is she talking about? We are throwing things around.\par \par \uc2 What -- where's the morality? Adam Smith was a moral philosopher, how would he interpret exactly what the moral issue is for going in and issuing a vote? It's wild.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thanksgiving dinner, wham, throw the turkey leg, throw the mashed potatoes.\par \par \uc2 Let me ask you one last thing --\par \par \uc2 PINSKY: No, no, no, don't, don't. Either be stay quiet or just be really firm and direct and be compassionate and feel sorry for people that are in a delusional state.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm not advocating. I'm joking.\par \par \uc2 All right. So when you tell people like \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  did, and she lies to old people, seniors, and says he's going to take away your Social Security and Medicare, and it's completely a lie. When she said in her closing speech in D.C. that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will sign a national abortion ban, limit access to contraception and stop IVF, all lies, do people believe the lie? How much of -- how much responsibility does she bear?\par \par \uc2 PINSKY: Well, I -- you know, it's hard for me to direct it at her because she was so much a part of a general chorus of waving their magic wand without the batteries working.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Those words came out of her mouth, man.\par \par \uc2 PINSKY: But -- but listen -- but listen, the whole thing about women creating being fearful about abortions or being able to get pregnant because they might not be able to get an abortion, if their life is endangered, I looked up the data on that by the \uc2 Kaiser Family Foundation\uc2  today. Guess what the exception rate is for among states that have rest restricted abortion? A hundred percent exception if the mother's life is in danger.\par \par \uc2 Why -- it's misogynistic. It's disgusting to whip people into a frenzy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But you know what? Those words came out of her mouth. So I think she bears responsibility for that.\par \par \uc2 PINSKY: Fair enough.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Dr. Drew, we might need you back on regular basis. The country -- half the country is in -- well, 45 percent of the country is melting down. We appreciate your time.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, the trial of marine vet Daniel Penny underway in New York City. Gregg Jarrett, \uc2 Alan Dershowitz\uc2  weigh in, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. A huge case now underway in New York City, marine veteran Daniel Penny is now on trial for manslaughter after placing a homeless man Jordan Neely in a chokehold on the subway in May of 2023 after Neely issued violent threats to his fellow passengers. Nelly was pronounced dead following the incident.\par \par \uc2 Keep in mind, Nelly had a whopping 42 prior arrests including multiple alleged assaults, for prosecutors are attempting to make this case about racial bias criticizing Penny's indifference towards Nelly in their opening statement. But as the defenses argued, Penny sprung into action to protect those around him, citing that Neely was seething and psychotic when he got on the train saying, quote, I'm going to kill everybody and I could go to prison forever and I don't care.\par \par \uc2 One witness telling the jury that she thought she was going to die when Neely got on the subway and felt a sense of relief when Penny restrained him while other witnesses have recounted the incident in a similar fashion.\par \par \uc2 And in a bombshell testimony from the man who helped Penny hold Neely down the witness said that Penny wasn't holding tight enough and that Neely still had a pulse when they released him as they were waiting for police to arrive at the scene, which raised us another question, why aren't police there? Why did it take them so long to get there?\par \par \uc2 Here now with reaction, FOX News legal analyst Gregg Jarrett, along with Harvard law professor \uc2 Alan Dershowitz\uc2  is with us.\par \par \uc2 All right. So we have one woman and others saying that they thought they were going to die. Here's a guy that says I'm going to kill everybody. I could go to prison forever and I don't care, 42 prior arrests and now this former marine faces 19 years in prison, Professor? Tell me why this trial has even taken place?\par \par \uc2 ALAN DERSHOWITZ\uc2 , HARVARD LAW PROFESSOR: It shouldn't take place. This is Bragg at its worst. The only reason this trial has occurred is because the racial components are such that there was pressure on him to bring the case. It never ever should have been brought.\par \par \uc2 First of all, you know the jury is not going to know about his 42 priors, the jury however is going to see the videotape and any reasonable person seeing the videotape would say, look, this is too close a case, this is not a criminal case.\par \par \uc2 A criminal case should involve overwhelming evidence. It shouldn't involve a plausible theory of guilt, a plausible theory of innocent. That's what prosecutors are supposed to be trained to avoid. So this is a case that never ever should have been brought. I don't believe it's going to result in a conviction.\par \par \uc2 People who want to the go on the subways when they hear somebody yell, I'm going to kill you. I don't care if I go to jail, are in fear of their lives. And when you're in fear of your life, what you hope for is a Good Samaritan who's going to jump in and protect you and we ought to always err on the side of protecting Good Samaritans to encourage them, even if in a given case maybe, maybe in retrospect he held him in the chokehold a little too long. We should always resolve doubts in favor of the Good Samaritan.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm going to kill everybody. I could go to prison forever, and then all the witnesses saying that they thought they were going to die, Gregg Jarrett, it bothers me that the jury cannot know the full story of this man and his history of criminal activity because they need to know.\par \par \uc2 GREGG JARRETT, FOX NEWS LEGAL ANALYST: Well, but that's the law, Sean, because the passengers and Penny didn't know that. But I agree this prosecution should never have been brought. It's a classic case of defense of another. If Penny believed that passengers were in imminent danger of death or serious bodily injury, he is entitled under the law to act as he did, even a mistaken belief is justified under the law.\par \par \uc2 But he wasn't mistaken, Sean. A parade of witnesses as you point out testified they feared for their lives. One woman said, you know, I thought I truly was going to die. They told the jury how relieved they were that Penny saved them, came to their rescue, intervened to protect them.\par \par \uc2 These jurors well know just how perilous the subway is in New York because for too long, liberal mayors and prosecutors like \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  have allowed criminals to victimize writers with impunity. Used to be a safe place but now it is a death trap.\par \par \uc2 I tell my daughters, do not go there. So I do not see a jury fed up with crime in New York city handing back a guilty verdict.\par \par \uc2 And the other component is race you have to ask this. Was it brought because Penny is white and Nelly is black? The lead prosecutor answered that question when she hinted to the jury that the accused is a racist and then another prosecutor allowed a witness to repeatedly call Penny a white man.\par \par \uc2 That is outrageous. It is unethical, if this case had anything to do with race, Penny would have been charged with a hate crime. He was not.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: If this man is put in jail, nobody -- there will never be a Good Samaritan ever to step forward again. And people will be injured and people may likely die.\par \par \uc2 I hope the jury does the right thing.\par \par \uc2 Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 More "Hannity" straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Unfortunately that is all the time we have left this evening. As always, thank you for being with us, and making this show possible.\par \par \uc2 Please set your DVRs so you never, ever miss an episode of Hannity. For news anytime, every time, all the time, foxnews.com, hannity.com.\par \par \uc2 And in the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Greg Gutfeld standing by to put a smile on your face. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. All materials  herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be  reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020241113ekbc00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; International\par \b \uc2 Trump Prepares For Second Term After Sweep Of All Seven Battlegrounds; Biden Preps For Final Stretch Of His Administration; Interview With Rep. Byron Donalds (R-FL); Rep. Phillips on his Early Warnings About Biden's Re-Election and the Future of Democratic Party; Fight For Control Of The House; Blame Game Begins For Democrats; Future Of Trump Legal Cases; The Lessons from the 2024 Election\b0\par\par\uc2 Shannon Bream, Howard Kurtz, Mollie Hemingway, Marie Harf, Lucas  Tomlinson, Rich Edson, Howard Kurtz \par \uc2 10,083 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 November 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Fox News Sunday\par \uc2 FOXN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREAM, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: I'm Shannon Bream.\par \par \uc2 President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  begins preparing his new administration with an historic pick for chief of staff after a sweep of all seven battleground states with a late Saturday call for Arizona.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , PRESIDENT-ELECT OF THE UNITED STATES: Together, we're going to unlock America's glorious destiny.\par \par \uc2 BREAM (voice-over): \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  goes from former to future president, declaring an unprecedented mandate.\par \par \uc2 Now, the guessing game in full swing over who will get plum positions in his next administration, as Republicans retake control of the Senate and hold a narrow edge in the fight for the House.\par \par \uc2 Congressman Byron Donalds joins us exclusively to discuss the GOP's road map with the potentially unified government.\par \par \uc2 Then --\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 RITCHIE TORRES\uc2  (D-NY): I have a concern that the far left is pressuring the party to take policy positions that are deeply unpopular.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Deja vu, Democrats taking stock of what went wrong and what comes next.\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  who challenged Biden in the Democratic primary on the debate over the party's path forward.\par \par \uc2 And, where do Trump's legal cases stand ahead of his second term?\par \par \uc2 Our Sunday panel on what his political comeback could mean for his challenges in courts.\par \par \uc2 All, right now, on "FOX News Sunday".\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 BREAM (on camera): Hello from FOX News in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Here's a quick look at your headlines:\par \par \uc2 A firefighter has been killed battling wildfires about 50 miles from New York City. Severe drought has created dangerously dry conditions in the Northeast and the resulting fires have led to an air quality alert for the Big \uc2 Apple\uc2  and surrounding areas.\par \par \uc2 Republicans need just five more House seats out of the remaining undecided races in order to maintain control of the House. Democrats need to win 16 to get to the majority,\par \par \uc2 And Arizona becomes the last battleground state it's been called for President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , giving him a total of 312 electoral votes. That's compared to 226 for Vice President Harris.\par \par \uc2 Trump leads in a popular vote by more than four and a half million votes.\par \par \uc2 In a moment, we'll talk with Republican Congressman Byron Donalds on the new era for the GOP.\par \par \uc2 And also, former Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  who mounted a primary challenge against President Biden after repeated warning Democrats that Biden's decision to run for reelection could be disastrous.\par \par \uc2 But, first, we turn to team coverage. Rich Edson at the White House on President Biden's final months in office, but we begin with Lucas Tomlinson in West Palm Beach, near President-elect Trump's Mar-a-Lago estates.\par \par \uc2 Hello, Lucas.\par \par \uc2 LUCAS TOMLINSON, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Shannon, President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will return to the White House Wednesday to meet with President Biden to cap what some say is the greatest political comeback since \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It was a historic realignment, uniting citizens of all backgrounds around a common core of common sense.\par \par \uc2 TOMLINSON: Trump is the first candidate in 40 years to sweep the key swing states voters firmly rejecting the Biden-Harris agenda. Here are the front runners to join key cabinet positions in diplomacy, national and homeland security, law enforcement and energy to carry out Trump's mandate.\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE WALTZ (R-FL): I'm a soldier. If the president of the United States calls you to serve, then you have to take that very -- very seriously.\par \par \uc2 CHAD WOLF\uc2 , FORMER ACTING DHS SECRETARY: He is a reformer. He is a disruptor. So if asked, I would certainly be willing to serve again. I think it would be an honor of a lifetime.\par \par \uc2 SEN. MARCO RUBIO (R-FL): I'm going to work with the Trump administration at whatever capacity they feel is best. I'm not presumptuous to say they're going to pick me.\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 DOUG BURGUM\uc2  (R), NORTH DAKOTA: Every position he has, there's qualified people banging on the door.\par \par \uc2 TOMLINSON: Helping Trump vet the candidates will be his newly appointed White House chief of staff Susie Wiles, the first female to hold the job.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats perhaps with an eye on 2028 appear willing to work with Trump.\par \par \uc2 GOV. GAVIN NEWSOM (D), CALIFORNIA: I want our president to succeed and our job -- my job is not to wake up every single day and get a crowbar and try to put it in the spokes of the wheel of the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 TOMLINSON (on camera): This week, expect more candidates being vetted for cabinet positions to come to Palm Beach. Two who will not be coming, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 . President-elect Trump says he has not invited them to join his administration -- Shannon.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: All right. Lucas Tomlinson in Florida -- Lucas, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now from the White House, Rich Edson.\par \par \uc2 Hello, Rich.\par \par \uc2 RICH EDSON, FOX NEWS SENIOR NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Hello, Shannon.\par \par \uc2 Well, with 71 days left in this administration, officials here say President Biden has plenty left to do before Democrats turn control of the White House and the Senate over to Republicans. Officials say the president is focused on keeping the government open, approving hurricane relief money, passing national defense policy, confirming judges and overseeing an orderly transition.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: We want to have an effective, efficient transition of power. And so, we are ready -- ready to provide that. As you know, the president invited the president-elect, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , to come to the White House.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EDSON: Well, before Trump moves in, the Biden administration's trying to send more weapon shipments to Ukraine. Officials are also working to approve pending environmental regulations, though Republican Congress could overturn many of the more recent rules.\par \par \uc2 A source with knowledge of the Trump transition 