ly. That's why his victory was overwhelming.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Okay. Let's talk about his critics who have now ominous warnings now that he is once again president-elect.\par \par \uc2 David French\uc2  writing at "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 ": If Trump was telling the truth about his intentions, then he will attempt a campaign of retribution and mass deportation that will fracture families, create chaos in American communities and potentially even result in active duty troops being deployed to our cities.\par \par \uc2 Here's what your House colleague and Democratic Congressman \uc2 Ritchie Torres\uc2  had to say.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 RITCHIE TORRES\uc2  (D-NY): One of the fundamental differences between his first presidency and his subsequent presidency is the fact that he now enjoys absolute immunity, and he seems to be intent on exacting revenge against his political enemies.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: How do you respond to Americans who say they now are fearful about a second Trump presidency?\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: For the American people who've been listening to these lies from the Democratic left, I would tell you, this is not something that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has ever spoken to or he's committed to whatsoever. There's no enemies list.\par \par \uc2 I mean, yeah, there are people who've been opposed to him but he is focused on the American people.\par \par \uc2 Job number one is securing our border, and beginning the process of deporting illegal immigrants out of our country. Job number two is getting our economy thriving again, get -- becoming energy dominant again. That's his focus.\par \par \uc2 His focus is the American people, not some enemies list that only gets talked about in "The Daily Kos" or Salon.com or any other place like that. He's focused on making our country great.\par \par \uc2 And what will happen in our country is success is going to be the measurement that he will use 