 the Trump campaign efforts, which is younger men. So, when you look at the group of voters, 18 to 44, in 2020, they went for Biden by 52 percent, Trump, 45 percent. How successful do you think that that effort will be? And what are you learning in the early turnout to see whether or not that really focused effort will actually pay off tonight for your team?\par \par \uc2 ALINA HABBA, TRUMP 2024 SENIOR ADVISER: So, for early voting, it was definitely -- we didn't have as much male turnout. And that's not just for our party. That's for any party in terms of voting. But after today, we're seeing a change and we're seeing such optimism in terms of our camp. If you look -- you know, I listened to Senator Kelly. I don't know what state he thinks he's in. I know he's an astronaut, but maybe he's on a different planet, but we're leading in the polls right now, but we need to keep everybody out there to vote, including men.\par \par \uc2 And I think that, Martha, we've done something strategically different this time, which is that social media podcast and that different media outlets that do hit that age group, frankly, my age group, and I know that he's just -- he's the kind of guy that could speak to anybody, unlike Kamala, which is why we are doing so well, and we're seeing such a good turnout.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, let's play a little bit of the sound from Senator Kelly just a moment ago and give you a chance to respond to it, the part of the Trump team. Let's watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KELLY: he has said he will punish women and he will -- and doctors should go to jail and women know that here in Arizona. They've heard that and they've seen themselves bounce back and forth between one really bad ban and another, and they get that. And I think that's why they're turning out at high rates.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Alina?\par \par \uc2 HABBA: First of all, we're almost double in Maricopa County, if you look