wood or Malibu or, you know, what have you, Sun Valley endorses \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . They're like, big reveal \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . No kidding. Raymond, we'll see you on --\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Down with democracy.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah. That was fun. And we had fun at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 . That was a good time. All right, Raymond, thank you.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Indeed.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's it for us tonight. Be sure to tune in Sunday, 7 P.M. We're going to have a special edition of the Ingraham Angle. That's going to be fun. It's America Now and Forever. Jesse is next.\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020241101ekav00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Exclusive Interview With Former President Trump\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity \par \uc2 8,460 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 October 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And in just one week, official election results will be pouring in from across the country. We are in the final stretch.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, I sat down with the 45th president of the United States for what will be my last interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as a candidate. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So you have this big event at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 , it went on for hours. I don't even know if you were there for the whole thing. I don't know what time you got there. I was told and made aware that you had no idea about this comedian who made comments.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT & 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I still have. I have no idea who he is. Somebody said there was a comedian that joked about Puerto Rico or something, and I have no idea who he was, never saw him, never heard of him and don't want to hear of him. But I have no idea. They put a comedian in which everybody does. You throw comedians in, you don't vet them and go crazy. It's nobody's fault.\par \par \uc2 But somebody said some bad things now what they've done is taken somebody that has nothing to do with the party has nothing to do with us, said something. And they try and make a big deal, but I don't know who it is. I don't even know who put them in, and I can't imagine it's a big deal.\par \par \uc2 I've done more for Puerto Rico than any president I think that's ever -- that's ever been president.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We'll have more on that issue and much more. Part one of my exclusive interview moments away.\par \par \uc2 But, first, we do have a message for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's opponent tonight. Now, earlier, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  -- well, she's not campaigning in Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, Michigan, Georgia or any other battleground state. Instead she is spending time in a place near and dear to her heart, a city filled of lobbyists, government workers, bureaucrats, politicians, far-left fake news journalists, a city that Biden carried by more than 92 percent of the vote, and a city where comma fields were right at home.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, we are talking about the Washington swamp. And just moments ago, the anointed Democratic candidate made her so-called closing argument at a rally near the White House and just a few metro stops away -- well, violent crime is raging through Washington, D.C. It is one of the most dangerous cities in America but Kamala didn't talk about crime in tonight's speech.\par \par \uc2 The nation's capital is also struggling with rising homelessness and a record high cost of living, Kamala didn't say much about inflation or the high housing crisis. She didn't deal with for four years. Meanwhile, Washington, D.C. is also suffering from a massive influx of Harris-Biden unvetted illegal immigrants but according to Kamala, this is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's fault, of course.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES & 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I will work with Democrats and Republicans to sign into law the border security bill that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  killed.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Kamala told a lot of lies tonight and that was the amnesty bill that would allow millions of illegal immigrants into the country every single year. That was not a border security bill by any stretch of the imagination and that wasn't the only lie from tonight's speech.\par \par \uc2 So let's expose these smears one by one. Here's Kamala lying about abortion, birth control and IVF. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Trump's not done. He would ban abortion nationwide, restrict access to birth control and put IVF treatments at risk and force states to monitor women's pregnancies. Just \uc2 Google\uc2  Project 2025, and read the plans for yourself.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's like a triple lie in one paragraph. Here's a headline from \uc2 CBS\uc2 , quote, Trump says he would v to a federal abortion ban. He's never -- he supports IVF, and by the way does not call for restrictions on birth control, the opposite of what Harris claimed tonight. He is also totally opposed to limiting any of this in any way has called on the federal government to help fund IVF as a matter of fact.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, it is not Trump's project 2025, he's not affiliated with it in anyway, knows nothing about. It has never even read the so-called project. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is a liar and her next lie was about Social Security and Medicare, let's scare the old people as per usual. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a different approach. He tried to cut Medicare and Social Security every year he was president.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, here's the truth. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he will, quote, never do anything to cut benefits. In fact, benefits went up under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in his first term. She's lying again.\par \par \uc2 She also blatantly lied when she mentioned unity and bringing the country together. In reality, she and her surrogates are spending almost all their time, all their energy, smearing, slandering her political rivals and playing political games. In fact, just seconds before promising to bring the country together, here's what she had to say about her political opponent. Wow. This is really unity if I've ever heard it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: America this is not a candidate for president who is thinking about how to make your life better. This is someone who is unstable, obsessed with revenge, consumed with grievance, and out for unchecked power. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has spent a decade trying to keep the American people divided and afraid of each other. That is who he is.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That was like 10 lies in one paragraph. Amid all the smears and the slander and besmirchment and lying, this was a robotic, uninspiring, meaningless speech. She claimed she will represent all Americans even those who don't vote for her days after she and her acolytes were out there calling everyone supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  a Nazi and a fascist.\par \par \uc2 She promised to always tell the truth, even when it's difficult but she lied over and over again didn't she about inflation being transitory, the border being secure, about how comfortable she was with the Afghanistan withdrawal and about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's cognitive state. She says she will never denigrate or dishonor those in the military. She called the Afghan withdrawal a success and when she has asked -- if she would have done anything differently or had any regrets from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , she couldn't -- you know, she could not say that she regretted any decision including the decision to allow our enemies to take over the security outside that air base in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Her inability to admit to her mistakes and failures that led to deaths and it dishonors the service of so many, what we are witnessing is a failing campaign and an attempt to try and regain the post-DNC bump a week before the election as they see more and more states falling out of reach the desperation and panic is palpable. Still, this election, I always warn everybody, assume that your vote will decide the outcome of this election and it's very close on paper, but the Harris campaign is clearly running scared.\par \par \uc2 Today, we did learn that the campaign is now pulling millions of dollars in ad spending from North Carolina amid a, quote, surge of Republican early voters. There has been a similar surge across all the battleground states and Trump is also outperforming expectations in national polling and according to the most accurate pollster of 2020, Atlas Intel, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now up by nearly two points. Now, the same poll shows Trump ahead in all but one battleground state.\par \par \uc2 And again, this will all mean nothing if you don't bank your vote. I voted Sunday but you can still take joy in knowing that these polls are causing epic meltdowns on the left. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Here's the warning you all have set it up, but let me take it a step further please if I may. This is called normalization. Yes, this is the descent into fascism if we so choose.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They think, okay, we've already seen that movie, I can live with it for four more years, but it's not the same movie. You know, it's the sequel to "Scream" where it's just that much bloodier. And you know there are people -- I mean, you're a journalist. You and I might be sharing a cell in, you know, six months from now.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The stakes literally are life and death for every woman in America.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: And he wants to start interment camps and that's what we are busy talking to every voter. He's telling you what he's going to do, believe him.\par \par \uc2 JAKE TAPPER, CNN HOST: Interment camps?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, he's talking internment camps. You know what, Jake, you may have to visit me in one I get worried enough when he talks about what he's going to do to his political enemies.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And it gets worse. Remember, irredeemable, deplorables and bitter Americans clinging to their God, guns, bibles religion from Obama? Yeah, well, now, President Biden, well, he couldn't stay out of the fray. He referred to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's supporters as, quote, garbage. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Puerto Rico, where I'm in my home state of Delaware, they're good, decent, honorable people. The only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Only garbage I see out there just Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 Now, remember, according to Kamala, it's Donald who he's the one that's flaming -- fanning the flames of division. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INTERVIEWER: I talked with Governor Walz yesterday. He compared Trump's rally on Sunday to that of one of the Nazi rallies in the `30s at Madison Square Gardens. Do you compare that? Do you find that a similar comparison?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Listen, this election is in seven days, and I think the American people have a very clear choice, and on the one hand, you have \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who is constantly fanning the flames of division and hate, who is trying to have the American people point their fingers at each other, or my leadership which is founded on a lived and experience that the vast majority of us have more in common than what separate us.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, let's double down on Nazi, Nazi, racist, racist, fascist, fascist. It might be the clearest example of gaslighting and hypocrisy that we'll ever see. At the end of the day, only one question really matters, are you better off than you were under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And so, tonight, while Kamala is spending time with her friends in the Washington swamp, the former president -- oh, look, right there. He's in Allentown, Pennsylvania, in front of another massive crowd.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, former 2024 GOP presidential candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You know, I just want to go to this \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  clip for a second here because if you remember, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  said irredeemable, deplorables. Obama said bitter Americans that cling to their god, guns, bibles, religion to that effect. The only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters.\par \par \uc2 You know what's interesting, aren't they really calling Trump supporters Nazis when they call him a Nazi and a -- and aren't they saying that his supporters are fascists when they say that as well?\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2 , FORMER 2024 GOP PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Look, here's the October surprise that just arrived. This is the basket of deplorables moment. That's what Hillary Clinton said in '16 that tanked her campaign. Well, that's the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 -\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  moment right now.\par \par \uc2 I am a little bit more cynical about this one, Sean, in the following way. It might look like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's usual cognitive deficits kicked in, but the reality is we know his family is secretly probably rooting for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  not \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to win because they feel really vengeful about how they were treated. So if you're in their shoes, you know that kind of comment is actually going to tank \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . So we're going to put those kinds of motivations to one side.\par \par \uc2 But regardless, it is a welcome October surprise because let's take a big step back what's going on here, the wheels are coming off the car they're spiraling and now you see the accusations of the other side being Hitler or piles of garbage you're going to hear a lot about threats to democracy in the next week. They are flailing, Sean, they understand Americans are not falling for their trick anymore.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a record that he's running on. They're frustrated by it and I think it's in some ways a beautiful thing for our side to watch to watch this completely come undone and turn the page on this ugly chapter of our history.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: To watch Kamala tonight just flat out lie about abortion, about IVF, about limiting birth control, about blaming Trump for the border, not addressing the issues of law and order and safety and security, not addressing her own failures, I kept thinking to myself, wow, is this all you've got? I mean, is it not one thing you can point to that you feel as an accomplishment in your years as the second in charge of our country?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: I think the answer to that question is no. There is nothing that she can point to as an accomplishment while she ran the country, and I think that's been evident in the case she's been making to voters it has nothing to do with her own vision for the future, nothing to do with her own policy record, and everything to do with really made-up allegations against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She's trying to attribute views to Trump on issues like abortion and IVF that aren't actually \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's views. This is actually something that's really frustrating Democrats this cycle, Sean, is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has actually staked out positions on let's just say marriage equality, abortion some of the issues where Democrats have historically accused Republicans of being extreme through the 2000s. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has not adopted those so-called in the 2000s extreme positions and that's frustrating Democrats deeply.\par \par \uc2 And that's why they're resorting to threats of democracy or he effectively threats on his own character that have resulted in some ways in this charged national environment. I mean, think about this election we've got two assassination attempts that have occurred in a matter of months and yet they're still shamelessly comparing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to Hitler and his supporters to Nazis. I think that they should at least in this final seven days when they know they're going to lose apologize for that tone that down so we can at least be united on the other side after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins this election. That's what I want to see.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It is -- it is really remarkable to me and I predicted it would happen and it's one of the reasons maybe I was a little repetitive in pointing out she co-sponsored with \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , the green new deal, promised she'd eliminate the filibuster. She co-sponsored government health care for all, Medicare for all, elimination of private health insurance, gun confiscation or mandatory gun buyback, highlighting over and over, saying banning fracking, no offshore drilling, pointing out what she tweeted out after a police precinct burn to the ground in the summer of 2020, a bail fund, and then saying on \uc2 CBS\uc2  that the rioters won't stop, they shouldn't stop, and she wouldn't stop supporting them.\par \par \uc2 Or her radical record on defund, dismantle, no bail, reimagine. Her radical record of decriminalizing illegal immigration, offering free food, housing, health care, education, legal driver's licenses, sex change operations and amnesty for illegals. And I'm -- it's just the tip of the iceberg.\par \par \uc2 The media never asked those questions. Those were her stated positions. How do you grade the media in this whole election?\par \par \uc2 RAMASWAMY: I'll give him an F, maybe a D minus if you include some that have at least gone the distance of actually at least highlighting some of her flip-flops. The reality is on all of those issues, Sean, those are areas where she has purported to change her mind. Here's one where she hasn't, she has still sticking to this one on a tax on unrealized capital gains.\par \par \uc2 Remember, the economy is the number one issue on the minds of American voters on the left and on the right. This is the single greatest way to trigger a second great depression and a stock market crash by forcing people to sell assets when they don't have enough money to pay taxes that the government is going to assess on them even when they don't have the cash to pay it. That's a tax on unrealized gains when the government tells you that your property is worth something when it may not even be worth that where you have to write a check out of your bank account to pay it.\par \par \uc2 That's something that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  still stands by. Who knows? Seven days left, maybe she'll reverse her stance on that, too.\par \par \uc2 But the beautiful part about this is people aren't falling for it. I was at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  at that rally. I would have never imagined that in the year 2024, even just a few years ago, that a Republican candidate for U.S. president would not only fill that \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  but have 200,000 people lined up to get in and that's because we're not just running to lead red states this time around, we're running to lead the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 And that's what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's going to do they're frustrated by it, but in seven days, we ultimately get the verdict from the people of this country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I hope the verdict is the right one, and I'm telling everybody assume that your vote especially in Georgia, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, Michigan, Arizona, Nevada, that your vote will be the deciding vote in this election.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, part one of my exclusive interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I asked him about the state of this race, the left's vile rhetoric against him, their closing arguments and much more, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We are just seven days away from election night, although every day is Election Day, until then because if there's voting in America, it's Election Day.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, I sat down with former President Trump for an exclusive interview. Here's part one of that interview.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mr. President, great.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT & 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: This will be -- one week from today is Election Day, the last interview I will ever have with you as a candidate. I'm sure you're probably not thinking about that yet.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, not really, but it's a little bit sad. We've been together long time as a candidate. Now, we can be together maybe toward making America great again because we have to do that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, it is amazing. With one week to go, how are you feeling about the race?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I think we're leading in every state, every swing state. I think we're even picking up maybe some states that traditionally don't go Republican. People want to see change. They don't want to have borders where murderers are being released into our country and many others, drug dealers, where jails are being emptied out into our country.\par \par \uc2 I happen to think it's the biggest issue. I think inflation would be second, the horrible inflation and the economy. I mean, the economy went bad because of inflation. We had no inflation whatsoever. We had a great economy, maybe the best ever. I think the best economy anyone's ever had.\par \par \uc2 And when you see what's happened to our country, it's very sad. But when you see what they're allowing to come into our country and kill people, just randomly just kill so many people, young girls are dying left and right, we can't let this happen. I think it's the most important issue.\par \par \uc2 And we're talking about by the thousands. They're coming in by the hundreds of thousands and even the millions.\par \par \uc2 And so, they have 21 million people released into our country through a ridiculous open border policy of Kamala. You have to blame her because she was put in charge of the border by Biden who went to sleep at 4:00. And she's done a horrible job.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, I think it's very important for your listeners to know that the Border Patrol endorsed me powerfully, and said she was horrible. They said I was the best ever and that she is the worst ever. So it shouldn't be that much of a choice.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, she in her own words, and this has frustrated me in the campaign, the media has covered for her, you know? They're an extension of her press office.\par \par \uc2 She has said in her own words, she wants to decriminalize illegal immigration, free food, housing, health care, education. Her -- the running mate, legal driver's licenses for illegals, free taxpayer-funded college, free sex change surgeries.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Correct.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And amnesty.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And defund the police -- and defund the police.\par \par \uc2 Don't forget, she was one of the leaders of defund the police. That means it's in her psyche, defunding the police.\par \par \uc2 We have to do the opposite. We have to let the police do their job. We can't take away their house and their pension and their family and everything else if they are a little bit more aggressive.\par \par \uc2 We have -- our country is a crime-ridden country. When they go into department stores and they strip the store, they strip the store, and our police are standing out. They're wanting to do their job but they're told, stand down, don't touch anybody.\par \par \uc2 And they're walking out with refrigerators and they're walking out with air conditioners, and there's hundreds of --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, they let them walk away, as long as it's under $1,000.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah, yeah. Well, that was her policy, under -- anything under $950, you don't prosecute. But really it's much worse. They don't prosecute anyway.\par \par \uc2 The only ones they go after is me, people like me. They go after Catholics. They go after -- and evangelicals will be next.\par \par \uc2 This is a horrible group of people. These are very dangerous people.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Uh-huh, or they -- they use limited resources to look into moms and dads at school board meetings as potential domestic terrorist.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We're now -- with the final week of this campaign, we have two very, very different closing arguments that have emerged. Kamala's closing argument, her -- her surrogates, Nazi, fascist, racist, Stalin, Hitler, Mussolini.\par \par \uc2 And -- and I thought this was supposed to be the campaign of joy. Doesn't seem very joyful to me.\par \par \uc2 What's your reaction when you hear that?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, first of all, they have no joy. They took it away from a man. I'm not a fan of Biden, obviously, but he got 14 million votes, she got no votes.\par \par \uc2 She was the last in -- 22 people ran, she was last. She came in last. Never made it to Iowa.\par \par \uc2 They went in and they said, you're not running anymore. We're taking it away. They took it away and he gave up much more easily than I would have thought he would have.\par \par \uc2 But this is not a campaign of joy for them. It's a campaign of hatred.\par \par \uc2 You know, my father -- and I mentioned this for the first time. Yesterday, I was in Pennsylvania, and I mentioned it. I said my father when I was young never mentioned the name Hitler ever. He was tough on it.\par \par \uc2 Somebody would say Hitler, never mention that name. Nazi, never mention -- never mention that name, and he meant it, too. And it was a word that you never use.\par \par \uc2 You know, you never use those words and now --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's the embodiment of evil.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : -- they accuse me of being a Nazi. They accuse me of being a Hitler type guy, or a Hitler lover, and I'm not. I'm the opposite.\par \par \uc2 They're the ones that are doing -- they're oppressive. This is like an oppressive machine and you know, they also happen to have the press for whatever reason.\par \par \uc2 But think of their -- think of what they're fighting for. They're fighting for open borders where millions of people can pour into our country. Think of it, millions -- who would -- who can get elected with that. They're thinking of having men playing in women's sports.\par \par \uc2 You know, it's interesting. I've been a politician now for nine years. I can't -- I hate to say I'm a politician, I guess I'm a politician.\par \par \uc2 Nobody's ever come to me and say, sir, it's really important that we let men play in women's sports. Sir, transgender operations all over the place are really important. Nobody ever brought this stuff up.\par \par \uc2 They bring -- could you lower taxes, could you do this, could you do that, could you help me here, my businesses, you know, et cetera, et cetera. They bring up a lot of things.\par \par \uc2 But nobody ever came to me and said it's really important that we do this. Men should play in women's sports. I think it's got a constituency of about -- about almost nothing and yet they do it. Maybe it's because they want to destroy the country. I don't know.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Or gender-affirming care for minors.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Sure.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Care without parental consent.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So, a young man leaves for school and goes to school, and the authority takes him over without parental consent, and they do things to him that you don't want to know about? I mean, is this supposed to be America? I don't think so.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It doesn't sound like --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : These people are radical people and let me tell you -- she's not a smart person. She's a low IQ individual. I've said it for a long time.\par \par \uc2 She speaks so slowly. Everything's so slow. She thinks of answers. They ask her a question, she talks about she was grown up with a lawn growing on her front yard. Everything is like crazy.\par \par \uc2 "60 Minutes" protects her. "60 Minutes" takes out her answer and puts a new answer in because her answer was so bad.\par \par \uc2 Could you imagine them doing -- now, I would love to have them do it for me. Think of it, Sean, "60 Minutes", \uc2 CBS\uc2 , they should lose their license. This isn't just editing. They took out her whole answer every word, and they put a total, totally different answer, and so that she looked better, because she looked like a very stupid person if they would have left the original answer.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I've never even heard of a thing like that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You mentioned your father and you did have -- I know the media would like to focus on the comments of one general, but you had about a week or so ago, 200 former generals, admirals all come out and support you.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Nobody wants to talk about.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Over 300 people --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Three hundred.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : -- from the administration, the most respected people. I see even Bill Barr's name was mentioned. I said, well, that's nice, because he understood -- look, he understood I did a hell of a good job. And so did everyone.\par \par \uc2 They signed a document, over 300 people. The press will not put it out. I'm so glad you guys -- thank you for asking this question, but I had over 300 of the top people from intelligence, generals, everybody, from the administration, saying Trump was a great president.\par \par \uc2 But the press won't put that out. They just don't. Look, we have a very, very corrupt and dishonest press. And I think with time, it gets better because they're all doing pretty badly.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you this: you -- you mentioned your father said never say the word Nazi, and you even have NBC News showing -- comparing \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  to the Nazi rally and I'll get to MSG in a second, and I'll get to your closing arguments.\par \par \uc2 But what's interesting is if you want to talk about the embodiment of evil, you talk about Stalin, Hitler, Mussolini --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- and they are they are pounding this. It is their closing argument. This is the environment we're in.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But it's the only thing they can do, Sean, because look, I had --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Because they can't --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : -- the best economy in history. I had the strongest border and the border wall. I built 500 miles of wall and without that wall, nobody could do anything. You couldn't -- they -- remember they used to say you don't need a wall. What are you going to do? Send some drones up to look?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: She called it a vanity project.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah, but now they have to do it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Medieval vanity project.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Now, they have -- in the meantime, they put in for funding to do a wall.\par \par \uc2 Look, I had the best economy ever. We cut more regulations than ever cut. I had no wars.\par \par \uc2 Think of it, no wars except I finished off a war that they couldn't finish. They wouldn't have finished it off in 10 years. I did it in a few weeks.\par \par \uc2 ISIS\uc2 , I knocked out \uc2 ISIS\uc2 . I rebuilt our military. I gave you the largest tax cuts in the history of our country.\par \par \uc2 We had the greatest economy in the history of our country. We were lapping -- think of it -- we were lapping China. I took out hundreds of billions of dollars from China in the form of taxes and tariffs. Nobody thought it was even possible.\par \par \uc2 And China respected us and everybody respected us. \uc2 Viktor Orban\uc2  said he was the most respected leader. And now, we have these clowns that -- that look so bad, they make us look so bad. Nobody can believe what's happened to our country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me -- if they -- if their closing argument and their surrogates are -- doubled down and tripled down and quadrupled down on Nazi, Nazi, fascist, fascist, think of the environment we're in.\par \par \uc2 In Butler, Pennsylvania, you came within a millimeter of being murdered, assassinated.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We had Trump International. You had a would-be assassin in -- in the bushes, with an AK-47 with a scope on it. This is the environment we're in.\par \par \uc2 I am told -- you can confirm if you want or not, Iranian hit squads are in this country that want to assassinate you. And you have the -- an entire establishment that the Democratic Party, Kamala's not telling them no. She's -- she herself is using the some of these words. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is using these Nazi analogies.\par \par \uc2 And in light of the environment and what has happened and assassination squads being here -- I mean, what is your reaction to the fact that they won't stand up morally and say, stop with the Nazi, fascist garbage, and let's argue on the issues of the day and whoever wins, wins?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : They only go after consequential presidents. I'm very consequential. I make China pay.\par \par \uc2 I had Iran ready to make a deal. They would have done anything. Now, they - - they have $350 billion. They were broke with me.\par \par \uc2 And I would have been very good to Iran. They had have one thing, no nuclear weapons, you can't have nuclear weapon. Nuclear weapons are the greatest danger to our country going forward, to the world going forward. It's not global warming.\par \par \uc2 I'm an environmentalist. I do great things. We had the cleanest air, we had the cleanest water. But if the ocean rises 1/8 of an inch over the next 500 years, we'll handle that.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : What -- what we don't want is global warming of the nuclear variety, and that could happen tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And coming up, more of my exclusive interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I asked him about the comedian's controversial jokes at his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally. That's straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And now, more of my exclusive interview with \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  from earlier today.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You've created a broad coalition I believe the Republican Party is now the party of hardworking men and women, and the Democratic Party is the party of Hollywood, New York and D.C. coastal elites as I call them.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: If that, if that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: If that.\par \par \uc2 So you have built a very broad diverse coalition, including Hispanic Americans, African-Americans. And by the way, I'll put the numbers up on the screen, and we can -- and show people where they were in those first three years of your presidency, the best growth rate in 60 years, and the people that did best were minorities in America.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right. That's right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They did you and you have built this coalition.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, so you have this big event at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 , went on for hours. I don't even know if you were there for the whole thing. I don't know what time you got there. I was told and made aware that you had no idea about this comedian who made comments.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I still have -- I have no idea who he is. Somebody said there was a comedian that joked about Puerto Rico or something, and I have no idea who he was, never saw him, never heard of him, and don't want to hear of him.\par \par \uc2 But I have no idea. They put a comedian in, which everybody does. You throw comedians in, you don't vet them and go crazy. It's nobody's fault.\par \par \uc2 But somebody said some bad things.\par \par \uc2 Now, what they've done is taken somebody that has nothing to with the party, has nothing to do with us, said something, and they try and make a big deal. But I don't know who it is. I don't even know who put them in, and I can't imagine. It's a big deal.\par \par \uc2 I've done more for Puerto Rico than any president I think that's ever -- that's ever been president. I -- when the hurricanes came, I rebuilt -- I helped them rebuild their electrical system. I helped them rebuild dams and everything else.\par \par \uc2 That place was hit by so many hurricanes. It's almost like hurricane -- hurricane alley. I've never seen anything like it. And Puerto Ricans love me because I was the president that stood up for them, more than any president. I've had great relationships with Hispanics but I've had really great relationship with Puerto Rico and people from Puerto Rico.\par \par \uc2 They love -- every time I go outside, I see somebody from Puerto Rico. They give me a hug and a kiss.\par \par \uc2 I gave them more money. I sent a hospital ship when they had one of the big hurricanes. They had no hospitals. Their hospitals were wiped out.\par \par \uc2 I sent the big Mercy ship. I sent it to Puerto Rico, fully equipped. It took care of things.\par \par \uc2 I mean, they love me in Puerto Rico, and I love them. I was -- I was there handing out food. I got in trouble for that too because we were having fun. We had a lot of people and I was throwing paper towels to the back, they were all having fun, every -- and the fake news came, oh, that was very disrespectful to be throwing tunnels.\par \par \uc2 No, I have unbelievable good relationship with Puerto Rico and the Puerto Rican people.\par \par \uc2 Who this comedian was, I have no idea.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You wish he wasn't there?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah. I mean, I don't know if it's a big deal or not, but I don't want anybody making nasty jokes or stupid jokes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Probably, he shouldn't have been there, yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me -- let me ask this it seems to as we come down I as --- look, as just an American citizen, I've never been more concerned about the country, the state of the world, especially we got war in Europe. We got war in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 We have a presidential candidate that talks about mandatory gun buybacks and no fracking and no drilling and --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, talks actually about confiscation of your guns.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's correct.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Not a buyback.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's what it is.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : They're going to confiscate your guns.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : If she wins, they will confiscate your guns.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Then, the new green deal, $93 trillion, eliminate the filibuster, eliminate private health insurance, sex change operations and amnesty for illegals, all of this -- it didn't get covered by the press.\par \par \uc2 However, at the end of the day, if you win, this is going to be about an -- the borders, energy --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Going to be --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- the economy --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Going to be about --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- law and order, safety and security.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Healthcare -- it's going to be about healthcare, taking care of people. It's going to be about things other than what you would typically think coming from me. We're going to take care of our borders immediately, day one. We're going to drill, baby, drill. We have more liquid gold than anybody else including Saudi Arabia.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Bigger than last time? Because you made us energy independent for the first time in 75 years.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You were energy independent, we would have been energy dominant -- well, I'll tell you, ANWR in Alaska. I got it approved. Reagan couldn't do it. This is the biggest find anywhere in the world. It's a size of Saudi Arabia. Some people say it might even be bigger.\par \par \uc2 Think of it, Saudi Arabia in our country. Alaska, they were already -- I got it approved. They got everything done. Biden cames in -- comes in, the first thing he does is end it.\par \par \uc2 We would have been supplied oil and gas to China, to all of Asia, it's Alaska, to Japan. We would -- it would have been unbelievable. We would have been paying down debt.\par \par \uc2 He comes in and he rejects it because the environmentalist -- oh, reject it. It has nothing to do with the environment. It's good for the environment.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When you say energy dominant would you be able to -- to ratchet up production, natural gas, oil coal --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Very quickly.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- where we could provide all the energy needs to, say, Western Europe.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And that means \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  would be cut off.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We would have taken over Western Europe. Oil prices will go down and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  wouldn't be able to prosecute the war.\par \par \uc2 Look, when they came in. They screwed up my energy program and the prices went through the roof, and Putin went in. If I were president, that would have -- number one, we wouldn't have had inflation, oil wouldn't have gone up like it did. But it got close to $100 a barrel. He made a lot of money during the war, at $100 a barrel, he makes money, at $40 and $50 a barrel, he wouldn't have even thought about doing it.\par \par \uc2 Biden forced him, he said -- he said we're going to raise the price of oil. Oil went up to $100 -- almost $100 a barrel, would have gone up even more. You know what they did, they went back to my policy and got it down a little bit, but only a little bit because it wasn't really my policy.\par \par \uc2 Right now, we would be -- we would have three to four times more than what we're doing. But if they didn't go back to my policy, you would have been paying -- you would have been paying literally $20 a gallon for gasoline for your car. They want to get rid of all gas.\par \par \uc2 I will end that immediately, by the way. You're going to be able to get a gas-powered car. You're going to be able to get a hybrid. You're going to be able to get an electric car, but they have -- they want to --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, the freedom, they're free -- the choice to what they want.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Of course, they want to force -- and nothing wrong with electric, but they want to force everybody to electric. Everybody doesn't want an electric.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What -- what would your role for Elon be? \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So, Elon has a lot of roles he could take because he's a very exceptional guy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But he has a thing -- he feels there's such waste, fraud and abuse in our budgets and he's right. And he's a great cost cutter and he'll cut cost without anybody even knowing it. Nobody's going to know it. Nobody's going to feel it.\par \par \uc2 He will cut costs and he feels he can save $2 trillion. If he does that, our budget is more than balanced.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We'll have part two of my interview coming up tomorrow night. We do have breaking news tonight. Moments ago, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  responding to the kind of repulsive Biden comment, calling \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters garbage.\par \par \uc2 We'll play you the tape. We'll get reaction from the great Victor Davis Hanson, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now as breaking earlier tonight at Trump's rally in Pennsylvania, Florida Senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  broke the news that Biden referred to Trump supporters as garbage, eliciting a very strong reaction from Trump and the crowd. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. MARCO RUBIO (R-FL): I wasn't going to say anything, but I have breaking news for you. Mr. President, you may not have heard this. Just moments ago, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  stated that our supporters are garbage.\par \par \uc2 (BOOS)\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: Are garbage. He's talking about the Border Patrol. He's talking about nurses. He's talking about teachers. He's talking about everyday Americans who love their country and want to dream big again and support you, Mr. President.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Remember Hillary, she said deplorable, and then she said irredeemable, right? But she said deplorable, that didn't work out. Garbage I think is worse, right?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wow.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now senior fellow at the \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2 , Victor Davis Hanson.\par \par \uc2 Wow. So I mean -- how do you respond to that, the only garbage I see floating out there is Trump supporters? Calling \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  a Nazi and a fascist and a racist, aren't they really also saying that his supporters are too? Are they really thinking -- isn't that what they really think of anybody that disagrees with them in spite of Kamala's, you know, new speech right -- written speech -- her speech tonight which I'm sure was you know gone over with a fine toothed comb?\par \par \uc2 VICTOR DAVIS HANSON, SENIOR FELLOW AT THE HOOVER INSTITUTION: Well, that's what ex -- that's exactly what they mean when they talk about rallies because the -- rallies are people, and that's what they're calling Nazis. But you know, this wasn't a mediocre comedian that went off script and gave a poor joke that was kind of repulsive that Trump disowned didn't know who he was. This wasn't a third party.\par \par \uc2 This was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  himself, the former Democratic nominee, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's boss and the president of the United States. And this came on the same day when she was telling the nation that she's a unity candidate and she's not going to be divisive. And this comes from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as was pointed out who had used the term chumps, and if you remember, he went to Pennsylvania in 2020, Sean, and he called the people of Pennsylvania that supported Trump chumps, he called them another time in another occasion, dregs.\par \par \uc2 And this follows Pennsylvania voters who were also called clingers by \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . So, there's a pattern here of looking down at the middle class. And you know, it's very ironic because we're seeing the same iteration this campaign, we got the same actors. We got Biden who's used the term chumps and dregs, now he goes to garbage.\par \par \uc2 We've had Hillary, she's used deplorables and irredeemables. Now she's talking about Nazis and fascists. And then we have the Obamas who've used the term clingers, now they're back again and they're talking down to African-American men as if they have false consciousness and they're not able to formulate their own independent thoughts.\par \par \uc2 So there's a pattern here of this elite left who talks down and denigrates people of the working class, and that they -- they should ask \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tonight, what is your relationship with that comment? That's your president, that's your boss, you disown it, you said you were a unifying candidate, what are you going to do about that?\par \par \uc2 And I think she's been very careful --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANSON: They should put her on the spot and ask her flat out are these the Nazi -- is this -- is this in accordance with your use of Nazi and fascist? Is this the logical result of your rhetoric that your boss would now call and go beyond you and call them garbage?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But she herself has said called Trump a fascist. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has used the Nazi analogy. So we know how they feel. She has allowed her surrogates to use these analogies of pure evil over and over again, especially in light of two would-be assassins, millimeter and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's assassinated, and it is reckless, irresponsible and repulsive.\par \par \uc2 And wow, it's -- it really exposes this elitist side to them.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: Yeah, I think it's going to be turning point this last week. I think they're going to regret it dearly because they've offended half the country and they're not going to get over -- they're not going to forget it. They're not going to forget it. And so --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: I'm a -- I'm a supporter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I don't feel like a piece of garbage.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't feel like one either and I'm not a fascist and I'm not a Nazi, and I resent being called it and I'm not a racist. And I find, you know, it -- that offensive.\par \par \uc2 What does it say that this is their closing argument? We don't have a lot of time.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: They don't have any policy. They've tried to -- she's tried to avoid the press and then that didn't work, then she went out and that was even worse.\par \par \uc2 She has these issues that didn't resonate because they don't have 51 percent, then she appropriated the Trump agenda. Nothing's working. So, now, it's -- I'm going to unite you all by calling half the country fascist. I don't think it's going to work.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't think that's a particularly inspiring or unifying. I mean the speech was supposed to be about unifying after a week of fascist, Nazi, racist, now, we're all pieces of garbage? Good luck with that strategy. We'll see, a week from tonight, we start counting votes.\par \par \uc2 Victor Davis Hanson, thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, more "Hannity" straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. More of my exclusive interview with \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  tomorrow night. More on Joe thinking you're garbage and Kamala calling Trump a fascist, Walz calling him a Nazi.\par \par \uc2 That's all the time we have left this evening. Thank you for being with us. Thank you for making the show possible. Please set your DVR so you never, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Greg Gutfeld standing by to put a smile on your face. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. All materials  herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be  reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020241030ekat00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Puerto Rico's Shadow U.S. Senator Endorse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ; Time To Move On From Failures Of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  And \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ; Veteran Versus Veteran In Closely Contested VA-7 Race; Anderson Takes On Vindman In Key House Race; Republican Tom Barrett Vying To Flip Michigan House Seat; Now, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Delivers Final Pitch To Voters\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham \par \uc2 7,868 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 October 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 VIQ Solutions, Inc. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Remember, if you can't catch us live, set your DVR, 06:00 p.m. in the East, 03:00 p.m. on the West Coast. You can follow me on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  @bretbaier. We're going to take you behind the scenes and all our travels, also behind the big set in New York for election night. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight and every night. That's it for this Special Report. Fair, balanced, and still unafraid. The Ingraham Angle starts right now.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. As always, thank you for joining us. Now, Democrats have been trying to dine out on that anti- Puerto Rican joke at the \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally, hoping they're really going to capitalize on that, thinking Trump is going to take a big hit among Puerto Rican voters. Well, this was Puerto Rico's shadow Senator speaking today.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ZORAIDA BUXO (R), U.S. SHADOW SENATOR FOR PUERTO RICO: I strongly and fully support and endorse \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  to be our 47th President to make America great again. And of course, to make Puerto Rico shine again.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, I loved it. I mean they thought all these indictments and the lawfare was going to crush Trump, and it didn't. But a joke told by a comedian was going to get -- these people can't be taught.\par \par \uc2 But another narrative being trampled on, but certainly that won't stop Kamala from telling lies tonight in a desperate attempt to reignite what is clearly waning enthusiasm for her campaign, exactly one week before the election, Harris is going to speak to a very large crowd gathered on the ellipse across from the South Lawn of the White House. We're going to bring it to you live.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he's rallying in Allentown, Pennsylvania, which we'll also cover. But first, return to rage, that's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 Now think about the contrast here. Trump packs the Garden to the rafters. He goes to a liberal city to do so, but for her closing pitch, she heads to the most pro-Democrat place in the United States, here in Washington, D.C. How brave is she? Well, tonight, she'll tell us that it's time to turn the page.\par \par \uc2 Finally, I agree with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , it is time to turn the page from the Biden era of decline and demonization that she will continue, and to an era of prosperity and peace, from their agenda of division and hate to a new time of unity and optimism. With her, it's not turning the page, it's a return to rage.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT AND 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: She's running on a campaign of demoralization, and really a campaign of destruction. But really, perhaps more than anything else, it's a campaign of hate, campaign of absolute hate.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Of course, Harris is also going to go after Trump on abortion, because Democrats think so little of women, they reduce them to one issue. So, all you women out there tonight, forget the nightmare cost of living, what you pay at the pump, what you pay at groceries, insurance, all of that that Harris helped create, forget the open border that the girls and women have been brutalized under. Forget all that. Just focus on that one issue.\par \par \uc2 Now, for the party that claims to cherish democracy, they sure don't like it when it comes to abortion. Now, all the Supreme Court did was return the issue to the states, and reportedly, there are more abortions happening now than they happened before the Dobbs decision was even handed down. So, how does any of this make sense?\par \par \uc2 The truth is, she doesn't trust the people to make their own decisions on this or any issue. Beyond abortion, her party wants the federal government to dictate the outcome on every major issue, from boys playing on girls sports teams to the type of car that you get to drive. They don't trust you, really, they don't even like you. So, don't buy the abortion hustle. It's lame.\par \par \uc2 And of course, they're going to be more dire warnings tonight about how Trump will try to jail his political enemies. Hello, they have been trying to put Trump in prison since he came down the golden escalator nine years ago. They hoped the lawfare, by the way, would be an insurance policy to prevent Trump from running again. And of course, she is accusing Trump of wanting revenge and retribution.\par \par \uc2 And let's not forget Biden and Harris's flunkies actually did put Trump's former aides in jail. \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , he just released today. \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  was only released in July. Who out there thinks that they would have been prosecuted had they not worked for Trump. And if you think that, then I have some sand to sell you in the Mojave Desert.\par \par \uc2 Now, let me say this. I want to say this as clearly as possible tonight, we got one week out to this election. Everything Kamala is saying tonight is a lie. All of it. It is a classic case of psychological projection.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was President of the United States for four years. I've known him for about 25 years. I spoke to him at least once a month during that time he was President, and at no time did he ever try to weaponize the DOJ against his opponents, and he didn't use the military or the \uc2 FBI\uc2  against his opponents either, never did it.\par \par \uc2 So, this speech of Kamala's will basically be a replay of Biden's Independence Hall speech. Remember that? With the creepy red lights. Biden, ultra-MAGA is coming for you, kids. No, it was nasty. It was hate filled, was laughed at. It convinced no one. Talk about divisive. But of course, no more so than the Hitler-Nazi fascist card that Kamala and company are desperately playing now.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Kamala intends to conflict and keep this misery going, and she's going to keep it going as long as she can, because that's the only way she can get elected. She's going out and only criticizing, talking about Hitler and Nazi, because her record's horrible. Her borders are the worst in the history of the world.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's an understatement, I think, if it's possible in the history of the world to be an understatement. Now, perhaps my favorite part of Kamala's speech tonight is her promising to bring Republicans to the table and even to give them positions in her administration.\par \par \uc2 OK, as if a single Trump supporter thinks that \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  or \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  count. They're worse than liberals. They're liberals who want perpetual war. So tonight is simply \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's latest attempt to answer the Trump juggernaut. But his rise is based on his record, the economy, the border, his foreign policy, and he promises a return to peace and prosperity, which is pretty credible because he's done it before.\par \par \uc2 But the animating theme of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's campaign is hating on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and throw in a little abortion for good measure, it's toxic fear- mongering and her economic plan, if you can even call it a plan, it's a joke, price controls and tired cliches. The fact is, she's been trying to play catch up with Trump for several weeks now.\par \par \uc2 Trump's dominating the mail vote because he treats them like actual human beings. He offers them real solutions to their top concerns, but Kamala is either sending the Obama's out to lecture men, pay attention to women's health, or you're a sexist, or she's trying to pander to them with stupid stage moments like this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE U.S., (D) PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: We need to move ground among men. Oh, we have microphones in here just listening to everything. I didn't realize that. OK, well, now you tell us. We just told all the family secrets, (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Two empty pant suits having a beer, they're going to need shots after Tuesday night. All right. Meanwhile, Trump seemed totally at ease, remember when he went on Joe Rogan show for three hours or at the \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's drive-thru. It just seemed like classic Trump.\par \par \uc2 But you knew Harris was in trouble when she even tried to co-op Trump's positions on everything from degree requirements for federal workers to no taxes on tips. Copycat. Now, even the rally at the ellipse when you think about it. Oh yes, that was Trump's January 6th rally. But I have expected to wear a red tie in a navy Brioni suit. It's almost as pathetic as her freedom message tonight.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are the true guarantors of liberty. Really? Was that -- what it was all about, and the Biden administration was pressuring tech companies to censor certain types of speech, was that freedom? The only freedom that Kamala will protect involves maybe pot, porn, and abortion, and the only Democratic outcome they'll accept is when it's an outcome they like.\par \par \uc2 Just a few short months ago, they were suing to kick Trump off the ballot in states, and they would have done so, had the Supreme Court not slapped him down nine to zero. Again, the guarantors of democracy. They tried to sue him and kick him off the ballot. Come on, that's it.\par \par \uc2 Harris's closing argument is just another cynical, tired retread of the same lies that we've been hearing for years. They haven't worked so far. And if President Trump wins next week, the Democrats will have to throw away this entire shameful playbook and maybe start listening to the American people instead of constantly attacking them. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Florida Congressman, Byron Donalds. Congressman. The real agenda of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , she's going to tell us tonight is unity and love and freedom and turning the page. What do you expect?\par \par \uc2 REP. BYRON DONALDS (R-FL): I expect nothing, but fear-mongering from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , because that's all she has. She can't talk about the border. She broke it. She can't talk about the economy, she wrecked it. She can't talk about foreign policy, it's a mess. And she can't even talk about her job with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over the last three and a half years, because he's not even allowed at this rally, which is 200 yards away from the White House, so all she can do is fear-monger against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But it's not going to work, because when -- as I travel the country, people are looking for solutions. They're looking for answers, All she has is word salad, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the person who will fix America and make America great again. So expect the fear-mongering, expect the projection. That's all you're going to get.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think that she's really trying to reclaim the narrative, Congressman, tonight, that she's the change agent, and here's what her camp campaign co-chair said when she was asked about how she will differentiate herself from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Watch. I think we have it in just a moment with Sarah Snyder asking the question.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JEN O'MALLEY DILLON\uc2 , HARRIS CAMPAIGN CHAIR: We feel very good about where we are. As you say, we're one week out, and we're closing this election strong. We feel very good about what we're seeing in early vote, and that is, you know, our voters turning out to vote, people that are lower propensity voters, they don't always vote. We're seeing on our side, supporters for the Vice President turning out in higher numbers, exactly as we'd like to see to win a close race.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is that, is that convincing to you? That's how it's going to work.\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: That's not convincing to me at all. And you could tell it's not convincing with how they've acted in this campaign. They were joy and vibes three weeks ago. Now, everything is attack \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Call him Hitler, call his supporters fascist. We were at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 , Laura, it was great to see you there. It was a fantastic night. You had people like myself, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , Harry-O, the founder of Death Row Records. We spoke at that rally. Do you think the Nazis would let three -- two black guys and a guy of Hindu descent speak at a rally at one of theirs? Absolutely not. But that's all they have.\par \par \uc2 The constant fear-monger -- fear-mongering and gaslighting is enough. People are sick of it. They are done. They're done with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and they're done with this version of the Democrat Party.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, I just ask you, because I think it was my favorite part of the excerpts that came out from the speech is when she's going to talk about, she's going to invite Republicans not to just sit at the table, but to be part of her administration. Does \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  as Secretary of Defense sound good to you? Want another war, Congressman? Because the Ukraine thing is working out really well.\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: No, it would not sound good to any of us. It would be a disaster. It will be a return to massive military spending all over the globe, which is not what our country needs right now. We need peace through strength. We need common sense. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the candidate to bring that. He will fix everything that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  have broken.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, it was great to see you Sunday night. Thank you very much. All right, coming up, why do Democrats want women to lie to their husbands or their boyfriends. Former NASCAR driver Danica Patrick has an idea. That's next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Democrats have a really cool new strategy to win over women when it comes to time to vote, lie to your husbands and your boyfriends.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: In the one place in America where women still have a right to choose, you can vote any way you want.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Did you make the right choice?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Sure did, honey.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Someone actually got paid to write that script for Julia Roberts. Is it any wonder that male voters can't stand Kamala with messaging like this, that men are somehow bullying or threatening the women in their lives who vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ? Now, I don't get offended by much anymore. I've been in Washington for too long, but that even offends me.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Danica Patrick, former NASCAR driver. Danica, it's wonderful to see you tonight. So, pitting women --\par \par \uc2 DANICA PATRICK, FORMER NASCAR DRIVER: Good to see you, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- against the men in their lives, your reaction to that?\par \par \uc2 PATRICK: You know, obviously, that's about lying. And I'd love to say that they have been lying about so many of the things that they said, but they barely said anything when they're interviewed, you don't really even barely know what their policies are or what their plan is. It's just a bunch of words. So, I think this is disappointing. You know, on the other side, J.D. Vance said something beautiful. He said, you shouldn't be losing close relationships with people based on who you vote for and this election.\par \par \uc2 So I think that really, if this is the truth about how you feel and that you can't tell your significant other about how you voted, it might reflect a little bit more on the depth of your relationship, because this is a core -- this is a core value. Voting is a core value that really builds relationships, and I think it's really disappointing that they're encouraging lying.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And also the implicit message is that men are going to, like, beat you up. Men are going to beat you up or somehow abuse you emotionally if you don't agree with them. And again, they wonder why there's such a big gender gap with men for the Democrats, but I want to play something for you, Danica. This was J.D. Vance being interviewed on \uc2 CBS\uc2  about the gender gap itself and kind of trying to pull in female votes for Republicans. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: 56 percent of women say the Trump campaign is paying too little attention to women's concerns. You say one of your top advisors is your wife, Usha.\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R-OH), 2024 VICE PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Yes, the top advisor.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: So what is she telling you? Because the data says you do have a women problem.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, what she's telling me is we got to make the case to women as well as we can, and ultimately, trust in the wisdom of those women to make a determination about what's in the best interest of their family.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Danica, it sounds like he almost believes in democracy, and he's not worried about women being threatened by men, just like make the best decision for you. Isn't that what we all want?\par \par \uc2 PATRICK: Well, of course, speaking of democracy, I think it's always interesting how Kamala and the Democrats talk about democracy when the least democratic thing that's happened is that she's in the position she's in without being elected into that position. I think that's a sad reality.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Well, there is a joke going around the internet, Danica, and they're calling her Coupmala, C-O-U-P-Mala, because it's always another iteration of you don't get any votes, but somehow you get elevated. You don't actually have the merit, but you get this job. And so, now she's in line to get the biggest job in the world, the most important job in the world. And today, she was asked, you know, what will you do for laid off autoworkers, essentially, if this EV mandate goes through? And her answer was, once again, well, you know, I was raised in the middle class. She actually answered a question with that as the response.\par \par \uc2 PATRICK: Well, I hope she was trying to be funny, because we find that funny. But you know, look, the women vote is definitely something that's very important. And I know that women can be very triggered by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's personality to some degree, but I also think that the propaganda and the fake news that has come out time and time again about him has painted a bad picture, and I think it really leads to the fact that we as Americans need to, as human beings, need to think for ourselves, do our own research and realize that so many of these things are just not true.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Danica, thank you so much for joining us tonight, and I know you voted. Yes, good. All right. Kamala likes to exaggerate her record of taking on the drug cartels. We've heard that countless times. But remember, during her tenure as borders are of course, the cartels have gotten richer and even more powerful, and of course, she has no policies to combat that.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : For the first time, under my administration, we will be seizing the assets of the criminal gangs and drug cartels, and we will use those assets to create a compensation fund to provide restitution for the victims of migrant crime.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, so Trump offering policies, she's talking about her old tenure years ago as A.G. of California. Now, a stark contrast to everything \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is proposing. Alabama Senator Katie Britt joins us now. Senator, thanks for joining us. So, immigration is one of the top issues for voters, top three issues. Migrant crime --\par \par \uc2 SEN. KATIE BRITT (R-AL): Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- has been horrific and hurt women the most and girls the most of any group in America, anything she is proposing that would impact migrant crime.\par \par \uc2 BRITT: Well, Laura, first thank you for letting me come on and thank you for letting us dig in on this important issue. I mean, as a mom, I look at this, and I think I want to make sure that we are keeping our children safe. You look at what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did versus what \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  did. And there could not be a more stark contrast. Here you have \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  coming in, undoing what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did, undoing the progress he made with 94 executive orders on the first 100 days.\par \par \uc2 I mean, let's not forget that she came in and said, let's halt deportations, let's stop building of the border wall, and then she said, I'm going to give mass amnesty to people who came here illegally.\par \par \uc2 Laura, we continue to see that, even today. You saw earlier, President Trump post the billboard that was put out that said using taxpayer dollars to talk about services for people who came here illegally. They've got their priorities all wrong and unfortunately too, we heard today about an attempted rape on a woman from someone who came here illegally. We continue to hear these stories after stories after stories, and they're a direct result of the failed policies of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . And at the end of the day, Laura, listen, Kamala broke it, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will fix it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, we have the video of that attempted rape, which I think our viewers have to see. This is what women in the United States are facing under \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's tenure as border czar. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Hey.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: He's trying to rape me.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Get off her now.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Can you help me?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Get off right now.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Give us a channel.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Thank God.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Don't you (inaudible) move.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: There's another case today that was tweeted out of two Louisiana girls, rape of them that a migrant actually videotaped. The \uc2 RNC\uc2  research \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account sent that out. Another disturbing case. Is that, is that supposed to be good for women, Senator? Is that pro-women \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  policy?\par \par \uc2 BRITT: Thank you and thank you for bringing light to this, because obviously the mainstream media is not. You think about this, this is, unfortunately, yet another story in a long line of heartbreaking stories where women have been raped, women have been brutally murdered. Women have been taken too soon. I mean, I was just in Texas last night campaigning with Senator Ted Cruz. We were talking about justice for Jocelyn, you know, talking about a 12 year old that was taken from us, raped and brutally murdered.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: These are sick people.\par \par \uc2 BRITT: You know, it is absolutely sick. And then you hear \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a CNN town hall said, I think we did everything right when it came to the border, she did everything wrong, and fortunately, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is going to come back in and put us back on the right track and I'm looking forward to that.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Senator, yes or no, is the rhetoric about Trump being a so-called fascist and his supporters being fascist, which the -- of course, her vice presidential nominee has said is that putting former President Trump's life in danger. That type of rhetoric, yes or no,\par \par \uc2 BRITT: It is absolutely reckless, absolutely Laura, and we've seen this rhetoric, and they continue to dial it up. It is -- it has no place in American politics. No one should be talked to or called things like that. And they know it, and they know exactly what they're doing, Laura, and it's despicable.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Two assassination attempts, and they're fanning the flames, or some wacko to take -- to act like a hero again, Senator, great to have you on the show. Thank you so much. All right. Up next, we take a look at some of the most critical congressional races that you might not have heard of, but that could help expand the GOP majority. You got to be on this, and we'll help you, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This is a Fox News alert. I know you're highly anticipating this, but \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is about to make her closing argument to the country. Her speech is expected to be filled with false claims of unity after she and her team spent a week claiming Trump is fascist and would not walk back those comments today. We'll bring you more as we get it.\par \par \uc2 But first to Virginia, two vets are vying to win the state's very important 7th Congressional District. Democrat Eugene Vindman, who is all about war, is facing off against Republican Derrick Anderson. Now, the priorities for these candidates could not be clearer.\par \par \uc2 And Vindman has spent much of his campaign talking about abortion and more funding for Ukraine because $200 billion's not enough, while Anderson focuses on the American economy and the cost of living. Well, wait, to be fair, Vindman did talk about higher grocery prices, but he claimed it's a result of Russia's illegal war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Derrick Anderson joins me now. All right, Derrick, this race is very important to me personally. The Seventh District is near and dear to my heart. Democrats poured a lot of cash into this race. Only three candidates have raised more than Vindman. The war machine wants this man to win. How do you combat that?\par \par \uc2 DERRICK ANDERSON (R-VA), U.S. CONGRESSIONAL CANDIDATE: Yeah, Laura, so I'm running against Vindman, a guy who is so focused on his past. You know, he's focused on his revenge tour with President Trump and doubling down on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's failed policies that got us into this mess in the first place.\par \par \uc2 But like you said, Laura, we're focused on the future. We're focused on making it more affordable for people here in central Virginia, making our communities safe by making sure our borders are secure and taking care of veterans.\par \par \uc2 But what's interesting about this, Laura, is my opponent, he's not only lied about me with millions of dollars' worth of ads, he's outspent me about 10 to 1 right now. But the polls show that we're absolutely tied despite the fact that he's lied about his military record, you know. He's lied about his rank. He's lied about his time overseas saying that he used weapons of war in combat when in fact he didn't.\par \par \uc2 Look, I'm a former Green Beret with six deployments overseas including Iraq and Afghanistan. He's not going to out army me, Laura. So, I get -- this all roads to the majority House are going to come -- yeah, are going to come through Virginia's seventh congressional district.\par \par \uc2 So, I encourage all of your viewers out there, if they want to help get a green beret back Congress, I encourage them to go to my website, derrickanderson.com, that's derrickanderson.com, because we have a shot to not only make sure we build that majority and keep that majority, but we build it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What I would say about this race is to women out there in the 7th District of Virginia, if your goal is to get closer to this idea of bringing back the draft, and perhaps your son or daughter getting drafted to fight in Ukraine, then Vindman is definitely your guy. I mean, I'm sorry, but -- I mean, he would restart the draft tomorrow if it would, he thinks, give a little bit of an edge to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 That is not what Virginia wants. I know the very pro and proud military tradition in Virginia, the great Commonwealth of Virginia, but the voters want America handled first, Congressman. And they respect enormously your incredible service to this nation.\par \par \uc2 But the peace and prosperity is what they want, and Trump and you will help get us there. The peacemaker. I think that is very important for you to use to counter Vindman's warmonger background.\par \par \uc2 ANDERSON: Yeah, absolutely, Laura. And we look at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's track record, right? Three to four years ago, we didn't have wars across the world. We didn't see what happened in Israel, where \uc2 Hamas\uc2  came across the border and attacked our biggest ally in the Middle East. We didn't see Russia come over into Ukraine. We didn't see China continuously -- yeah.\par \par \uc2 So, this is what you get at the hand of weak leadership. My opponent would be a rubber stamp for that weak leadership, Laura. And that's why it's so important. Folks need to help me get over this finish line. Go to derrickanderson.com because, again, as a former Green Beret, I've done it all. I've been all over the place. I've been shot at. I've had five of my guys lost in Afghanistan. So, we don't want war. We're ready to get things back to normal, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Bring back common sense. Derrick, always great to see you and good luck on Tuesday. We're watching this very closely. Now to Michigan's seventh district. The race to replace Democrat Congresswoman Alyssa Slotkin. It's Democrat as Curtis Hurtell versus Republican Tom Barrett in a district that relies heavily on the youth vote.\par \par \uc2 Now, according to study from \uc2 Tufts University\uc2 , this is the top race in the country in the House, and that's where college students would have the greatest impact. Tom Barrett joins me now.\par \par \uc2 All right, Tom, we all think college kids are all liberal. I was just at Texas A&M, and I can tell you they're not liberal there, but it's a different kettle of fish where you are. So, how do you capture the youth vote in your district, my friend?\par \par \uc2 TOM BARRETT(R-MI), U.S. CONGRESSIONAL CANDIDATE: Well, thank you, Laura, so much for having me on. And you're right. You know, the youth vote is so important. It's important across the country, but really here in the seventh congressional district in Michigan, we have \uc2 Michigan State University\uc2  right here in the center of this district.\par \par \uc2 I just did a rally there on Friday with Governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 . There's been a number of outreach events. We hired a campus coordinator. I've been on campus quite a bit. And I will tell you that young people, when you ask them, do you want to graduate into a Trump economy or a \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  economy?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We've got a -- sorry about that, Tom, but Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has just walked out to the stage to deliver what we're told is her closing message. So, take a breath and watch.\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: Thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you, everyone. So, listen, one week from today, you will have the chance to make a decision that directly impacts your life, the life of your family, and the future of this country we love.\par \par \uc2 And it will probably be the most important vote you ever cast. And this election is more than just a choice between two parties and two different candidates. It is a choice about whether we have a country rooted in freedom for every American or ruled by chaos and division.\par \par \uc2 Many of you watching have probably already cast your ballots. But I know many others are still considering who to vote for or whether you'll vote at all. So tonight, I will speak to everyone about the choice and the stakes in this election.\par \par \uc2 Look, we know who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is. He is the person who stood at this very spot nearly four years ago and sent an armed mob to the United States Capitol to overturn the will of the people in a free and fair election. An election that he knew he lost. Americans died as a result of that attack. One hundred and forty law enforcement officers were injured because of that attack.\par \par \uc2 And while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sat in the White House watching as the violence unfolded on television, he was told by his staff that the mob wanted to kill his own vice president. And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  responded with two words, so what? America, that's who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is. And that's who is asking you to give him another four years in the Oval Office. Not to focus on your problems, but to focus on his.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has told us his priorities for a second term. He has an enemies list of people he intends to prosecute. He says that one of his highest priorities is to set free the violent extremists who insulted those law enforcement officers on January 6th. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  intends to use the United States military against American citizens who simply disagree with him. People he calls, quote, "the enemy from within."\par \par \uc2 America, this is not a candidate for president who is thinking about how to make your life better. This is someone who is unstable, obsessed with revenge, consumed with grievance, and out for unchecked power. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has spent a decade trying to keep the American people divided and afraid of each other. That is who he is.\par \par \uc2 But America, I am here tonight to say that is not who we are. That is not who we are. That is not who we are. You see, what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has never understood is that e pluribus unum, out of many, one, isn't just a phrase on a dollar bill. It is a living truth about the heart of our nation. Our democracy doesn't require us to agree on everything. In fact, we like good arguments from time to time. Just think of your own family, right?\par \par \uc2 It's not the American way to not have disagreements. We don't shy away from robust debate. Robust debate. In fact, we like a good debate, don't we? We like a good debate. And the fact that someone disagrees with us does not make them the enemy within. They are family, neighbors, classmates, co- workers. They are fellow Americans. And as Americans, we rise and fall together.\par \par \uc2 America, for too long we have been consumed with too much division, chaos, and mutual distrust. And it can be easy then to forget a simple truth, it doesn't have to be this way. It doesn't have to be this way. It is time to stop pointing fingers. We have to stop pointing fingers and start locking arms. It is time to turn the page on the drama and the conflict, the fear and division. It is time for a new generation of leadership in America.\par \par \uc2 And I am ready to offer that leadership as the next president of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Now, look, let me say, let me say, I recognize this has not been a typical campaign. Even though I've had the honor of serving as your Vice President for the last four years, I know -- but I know that many of you are still getting to know who I am.\par \par \uc2 Well, let me tell you, I am someone who has spent most of my career outside of Washington, D.C. So, I know that not all the good ideas come from here. I am not afraid of tough fights against bad actors and powerful interests.\par \par \uc2 Because for decades, as a prosecutor and a top law enforcement officer of our biggest state, I won fights against big banks that ripped off homeowners, against for-profit colleges that scammed veterans and students, against predators who abused women and children, and cartels that trafficked in guns, drugs, and human beings.\par \par \uc2 And I did this work because for as long as I can remember, I have always had an instinct to protect. There's something about people being treated unfairly or overlooked that frankly just gets to me. I don't like it. It's what my mother instilled in me. A drive to hold accountable those who use their wealth or power to take advantage of other people.\par \par \uc2 The drive to protect hardworking Americans who aren't always seen or heard and deserve a voice, and I will tell you that is the kind of president I will be.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: And look, I'll be honest with you, I'm not perfect, I make mistakes, but here's what I promise you. I will always listen to you, even if you don't vote for me. I will always tell you the truth, even if it is difficult to hear. I will work every day to build consensus and reach compromise to get things done. And if you give me the chance to fight on your behalf, there is nothing in the world that will stand in my way.\par \par \uc2 So, look, in less than 90 days, either \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or I will be in the Oval Office. Ok. On day one -- and on day one, if elected. On day one if elected, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would walk into that office with an enemies list. When elected, I will walk in with a to-do list. Full of priorities of what I will get done for the American people.\par \par \uc2 And I will work with everyone, Democrats, Republicans, and independents to help Americans who are working hard and still struggling to get ahead. I have been honored to serve as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's vice president. But I will bring my own experiences and ideas to the Oval Office. My presidency will be different because the challenges we face are different.\par \par \uc2 Our top priority as a nation four years ago was to end the pandemic and rescue the economy. Now our biggest challenge is to lower costs, costs that were rising even before the pandemic and that are still too high. I get it.\par \par \uc2 I still remember our mother sitting at that yellow Formica table late at night, cup of tea in hand, a pile of bills in front of her, trying to make it all work. And I've heard from so many of you who are facing even greater financial pressures.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's answer to you is the same as it was the last time. Another trillion dollars in tax cuts for billionaires and big corporations. This time, he will pay for it with a 20 percent national sales tax on everything you buy that is imported. Think about it. Clothes, food, toys, cell phones. A Trump sales tax that would cost the average family nearly $4,000 more a year.\par \par \uc2 And on top of that, you will pay even more if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  finally gets his way and repeals the Affordable Care Act, which would throw millions of Americans off their health insurance and take us back to when insurance companies had the power to deny people with pre-existing conditions. Well, we are not going back. We are not going back.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: We are not going back. Because we also know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would deliver tax cuts to his billionaire donors. I will deliver tax cuts to working people and the middle class. I will make sure you have a chance, not just to get by, but to get ahead. Because I believe in honoring the dignity of work.\par \par \uc2 I will enact the first ever federal ban on price gouging on groceries. Cap the price of insulin and limit out-of-pocket prescription costs for all Americans. I will fight to make sure that hardworking Americans can actually afford a place to live.\par \par \uc2 I will never forget how our mother saved up and how excited she was when she could finally afford to buy our first home. I remember how excited she was. And I know that owning a home is not only a measure of financial security, it's about the pride of your hard work. And as president, I will fight to help first-time home buyers with your down payment, take on the companies that are jacking up rents and bills, millions of new homes.\par \par \uc2 For years we've heard excuses about why America can't build enough housing, enough with the excuses. I'm going to cut the red tape and work with the private sector and local governments to speed up building and get it done.\par \par \uc2 And the cost of housing isn't the only financial pressure on middle class families. I have met so many young people who have a natural desire to parent their children well, but not always the resources to do it. So, I'll fight for a child tax credit to save them some money, which will also lift American children out of poverty.\par \par \uc2 I'll work to lower the cost of childcare, which is out of reach for too many working families today. And for too many people in the sandwich generation who are raising young children and taking care of a parent, juggling all of it is extremely difficult.\par \par \uc2 You know, I took care of my mother when she got sick, cooking food that she had a taste for, finding clothes that would not irritate her skin. And understand, as I do, that caregiving is about dignity. It is about dignity. And currently, if you need home care and you don't have some money to hire someone, you and your family need to deplete your savings to qualify for help. That's just not right. So, we're going to change the approach and allow Medicare to cover the cost of home care, so seniors can get the help and care they need in their own homes.\par \par \uc2 Now \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a different approach. He tried to cut Medicare and Social Security every year he was president. Look, I believe that when people have worked hard their entire life, they deserve to retire with the benefits they have earned. And I believe in the fundamental freedom of Americans to make decisions about their own bodies and not have their government tell them what to do.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: I will fight to restore what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his hand-selected Supreme Court justices took away from the women of America. Today, one in three women in America, think about it, one in three women in America lives in a state with a Trump abortion ban. Many with no exceptions even for rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 The idea that a woman who survives a crime of a violation to her body should not have the authority to make a decision about what happens to her body next, that is immoral. That is immoral. And Trump's not done. He would ban abortion nationwide, restrict access to birth control and put IVF treatments at risk, and force states to monitor women's pregnancies. Just \uc2 Google\uc2  Project 2025 and read the plans for yourself.\par \par \uc2 And look, I think we all know one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to simply agree the government should not be telling her what to do with her body. Not the government. And when Congress passes a bill to restore reproductive freedom nationwide, as president of the United States I will proudly sign it into law. Proudly.\par \par \uc2 And look, on another subject, politicians have got to stop treating immigration as an issue to scare up votes in an election, and instead treat it as the serious challenge that it is that we must finally come together to solve. I will work with Democrats and Republicans to sign into law the border security bill that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  killed.\par \par \uc2 When I was Attorney General of a border state, I saw the chaos and violence caused by transnational criminal organizations that I took on. And when I am president, we will quickly remove those who arrive here unlawfully, prosecute the cartels, and give Border Patrol the support they so desperately need.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, we must acknowledge we are a nation of immigrants. And I will work with Congress to pass immigration reform, including an earned path to citizenship for hardworking immigrants like farm workers and our dreamers. As Commander-in-Chief, I will make sure America has the strongest, most lethal fighting force in the world.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , on the other hand, has shown his contempt for our nation's heroes, calls them suckers and losers. Called a four-star Marine general a, quote, "low life." I will always honor, never denigrate the service and sacrifice of our troops and their families, and fulfill our sacred obligation to care for them. I will strengthen, not surrender, America's global leadership. And I will stand with our friends because I know that our alliances keep American people safe and make America stronger and more secure.\par \par \uc2 Look, world leaders think that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is an easy mark, easy to manipulate with flattery or favor. And you can believe that autocrats like Putin and Kim Jong-un are rooting for him in this election.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020241030ekat00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Electrifies The Garden; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 : Dream Big, Save America; \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  And Kamala Harris Barnstorm Key Swing States; Kamala's final pitch to women, abortion; Democrats final pitch, they're Nazi and more abortions; \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  tries to shame men into Kamala vote; Harris and Walz try and fail to win over male voters; The left links Trump rally to 1939 Nazi rally; Absolutely despicable, Trump rallygoers rip \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 's Nazi comparison; Kamala caught on hot mic with Governor Whitmer at Michigan bar\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Laura Ingraham, Ari Fleischer, Katie Pavlich, Raymond  Arroyo \par \uc2 7,614 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 October 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 VIQ Solutions, Inc. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: -- with former South Carolina Governor, U.S. Ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  and Presidential Candidate, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  live on set. The final days of this election. Remember, if you can't catch us live, set your DVR, 06:00 p.m. in the East, 03:00 p.m. on the West Coast. You can follow me on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  at Bret Baier. We're going to take you behind the scenes as we close down on this Election Day. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this Special Report. Fair, balanced, and unafraid. Here's Laura.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. An unstoppable force. That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 Well-respected polling analyst tonight, Nate Silver, has Trump now with a 55 percent chance of winning the election, Harris is now down to 44.6 percent. I want to be clear, this is still anyone's race, but if the Trump momentum holds and he wins the presidency a week from tomorrow, there are four events that I believe will be remembered as pivotal. First, the VP debate, where Vance trounced Walz.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R-OH), 2024 VICE PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: You yourself just said Iran is as close to a nuclear weapon today as they have ever been. And Governor Walz, you blame \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Who has been the Vice President for the last three and a half years? And the answer is, your running mate, not mine.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Second, Trump's return to Butler,\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT AND 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: A very big thank you to Pennsylvania. We love Pennsylvania. And as I was saying.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Third, Trump working at \uc2 McDonald's\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Keep it tight. We've got the salt (ph) on. Never touches the human hand. I made it myself. I have worked at \uc2 McDonald's\uc2 . I now worked for 15 minutes more than Kamala, requires great expertise actually.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And fourth, the capper, the packed show at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: For the past nine years, we have been fighting against the most sinister and corrupt forces on Earth. With your vote in this election, you can show them once and for all, that this nation does not belong to them. This nation belongs to you. It belongs to you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I was there, and the message was hopeful, optimistic and Reagan-esque. Thousands and thousands waited in line for 12 hours to get in. The crowd was patriotic. It was happy, diverse, young, old, independents, Republicans, of course, different races and ethnicities. They shared a faith that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can deliver on bringing a new golden age to the country they all love.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We will have the strongest economy, the most secure borders, the safest cities, the most powerful military, the best trade deals, and we will dominate the frontiers of science, medicine, business, technology and space. And I'm asking you to be excited about the future of our country again, I'm asking you to dream big again. This will be America's new golden age.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I love that line, the new golden age. Yes, we need that in America. Now, I've been covering these types of rallies since 2015, and the coalition has grown, the people that the MAGA movement gained along the way, these are significant people, and it tells us a lot about why this matters, why it's working.\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr., \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and countless regular folks who have given Trump's pragmatic populism another look, because they all came to see what we've known for years, that the old Washington establishment has failed us in every way. It's failed us at home. It's failed us abroad, in politics, and the culture. But voters are recognizing that just because they failed, it doesn't mean America has to fail, because America can be renewed. We're for everyone, if you're an American.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We're building the biggest, broadest, most diverse coalition in American history, including union workers and border patrol agents. We're seeing historic levels of support among our black population, Hispanic population, and our Asian population, Jews and Muslims and Catholics and evangelicals and Mormons, and they're all joining our cores in large numbers, larger than anyone has ever seen in this country before, and the Republican Party has really become the party of inclusion.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The party of inclusion. Take their language, recapture it as your own, because that's the truth. They're exclusionary. They're intolerant. We want everyone to be better, stronger, more prosperous and safer. It doesn't matter where you came from. It doesn't matter what color your skin is, that's what we believe. So the atmosphere in that arena was electric. It was on fire, and it was overwhelmingly optimistic. I kept thinking, and I was watching what other politician in America could gather such a crowd.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  was packed. People waited hours to get in. They sat through hour after hour of this rally. They were fervent in their devotion to all things Trump. Trump has created a movement. There is no doubt. I cannot think of another Republican figure of my lifetime who could have come into a Democratic city like New York and put together anything like that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, they've been trashing him all day for saying that. That's true, that's obvious. Everyone who is honest today would be saying the same thing. There is no one else who could have done it. They wouldn't even try to do it. And the night was a celebration of American freedom, probably above all else. But there, of course, there are others who truly believe that you can't be a good person or a moral person if you believe that we need to take care of American needs and American problems first.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP