ver answered that question and no one really asked them.\par \par \uc2 So, instead he directs his attention to an unnamed, unknown mass of generic men that he can assume is dumb, uninformed, and gullible. That is his escape hatch from reality, a way to avoid this glaring blind spot. Why are there rich, smart, industrious, intelligent well-read people supporting Trump? They cannot answer that question. So, instead he says no, they're just this easily persuadable group. I don't even know who they are. Oh, they're so stupid I got my little hat on the flag in the back. But he's got superhero delusion disorder. Just because you play one doesn't make you one.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And finally, Dana, you know, men are being told that they're the problem especially white men by the Dems. You know that -- you know, check your privilege at the door. I mean, all of this stemmed from the Democrats hating men.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes. So, I want to make two points in two parts. So, in a more recent thing of the last several years, right, you've had people like James Carville and Ruy Teixeira, these moderate Democrats, maybe they call them establishment Democrats now who have been sending these flashing warning signs. Like, guys, we have a problem with men. We have a problem with boys. We got to pay attention to this. Nobody wanted to pay attention to it and they continued on the path that they went on.\par \par \uc2 So, then Politico does this whole piece about the flat -- the frat guys that saved the American flag, and they said it was all for Trump. No, that was because the pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  people took the flag down. That's why they got -- it wasn't that. And they're mad -- well, they're mad at the Democrats. The Republican Party ID is at its highest level in decades. And some Hispanic and Black men are saying, wait, we just don't like the policies but maybe we don't want to wear a red hat, but we are not going to stand for this anymore.\par \par \uc2 Then the second part I wanted to say, there is a bigger issue and I was kind of the product, maybe Jessica you are too, in a -- in a way, Judge, you are. One of the people that helped figure out a way to say I'll be the first woman to do that. I'll do that, right? So, we're paving ways. And we were told -- I had a yellow T-shirt when I was -- as a kid, I was 6 years old. I wore this t-shirt for three years. It was yellow and it had the ugliest black lettering. And my dad bought it for me. And it said, anything boys can do, girls can do better.\par \par \uc2 And there was this push to try to tell girls you can do it. You are going to be OK. You can do math. You can do science. You can lead too. Don't let anybody tell you that you can't. And now what do we have? Laura Bush in 2002 said we've got a problem. We're -- great that we're focusing on girls, but you guys, we have to focus on boys. Look at how they're falling behind in school. 20 years later this is what happened. And the only person giving them an option for how they could improve their lives is Trump.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK. I agree. Ahead, trip wires and booby traps, campaign yard signs are no joke this year.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yard signs are no joke this year. One guy in Virginia got so tired of people messing with his anti-Kamala sign that he set up cameras, trip wires, and alarms on his property.\par \par \uc2 No one has a yard sign here.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I do.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Do you? You have a yard? You guys have yards?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I mean, if you have an American flag, everybody knows you're a Trump voter, so --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes. I have a sign. I have -- I have a Jill Stein sign in my yard.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: In your window?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Good idea.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Because it drives Democrats crazier than a Trump sign. I got like all these Jill Stein signs.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Wasted vote.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Flag kills them. OK, so here's the deal. So, the neighbors get very upset. And so, they call the police and because they worried that there's trip wires. The truth is they could be arrested for trespassing, criminal mischief. There ain't no trip wires. There was no danger. And they're the ones who literally put themselves in in harm's way.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: I love when she studies for the E block. Dana?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I did not study for the E block.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: It's OK.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And I really don't have anything. Sorry. I never take a pass. I don't have a sign. I have a flag. I have a flag.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You're not -- you're allowed to pass? You can't pass.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You can't pass.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No, you can't.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I have a flag.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You're not Kamala.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Here's what I think they should do.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, and I have a flag.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: He should put fishhooks all over it so if they touch it, it'll cut their fingers off.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: There you go.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, that's it.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: How about that?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well, they've been f like young kids, like high school kids with tons of them. Like --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Kamala signs?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No, pulling ---\par \par \uc2 PERINO: They're not old enough to vote.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No. So, who cares about you?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: That's their vote.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: OK. This was awesome. "ONE MORE THING" is up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's time now for "ONE MORE THING." Talk about being stuck between a rock and a hard place. A woman in Australia was on a hike and she dropped her phone between two boulders.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, boy.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And she tried to reach down and get it, and she slipped, and got herself stuck upside down.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, but did she get to the phone?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Upside down?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: For seven hours.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Upside down?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I'm telling you, women, you guys get it together.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: What? Is she upside down --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Tonight, "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME," Johnny went to Detroit to see what people are thinking about the election. Here's a sneak peek.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHNNY BELISARIO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL PRODUCER: What have the Democrats done for you?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: How long do the cameras roll for because we going to be rolling for a long time until I can think of something.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: All right, you're up, Greg.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I think we figured out why women are voting for Kamala. Tonight --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: What?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Kat Timpf, \uc2 Kevin O'Leary\uc2 , Emily Austin, Tyrus. Let's do this. Greg's Have You Ever Wondered What It's Like To Be A Cat News. Well, live the life of Max. They app -- they put some kind of camera on his collar and this is what it's like to be a cat, chasing another cat through a car park as they say in England.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: It's kind of cute.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, this is what it's like. Just get really close to the TV if you're home and you will find out what it's like to be a cat. Look how busy it is.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: That's so fun.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Everything is low. You're running around. This is exactly how it feels when you're going for a walk, Dana.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, you got -- you know what I mean?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It makes you tired just watching.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I know. Isn't it great?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: He got his zips in. I'll say that.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It goes for four hours.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Dana?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Well, there's been a little bit of a heat wave here in New York. It's been a glorious weather. I want to show you Hugo. He's taking advantage of this at Central Park. This is how he, you know, cleans himself at the park. They've having to water because there's so -- been so dry we haven't had any rain.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Damn. I'm going to bring dogs.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: That's Hugo. That's Percy's friend.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: No one ate the dog, Greg.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: They're eating cats.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: We don't have that problem here.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us. Have a good night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FOXFIV0020241025ekao00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Democrats May Be Running Out Of Cards To Play; Left Tries To Scare You Into Voting Against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ; \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Loses Male Voters, Scares Women Voters; Out-Of-Touch Celebrities For Harris; Obama's Bad Rap With Bad Accent; The Real Slim Shady Reads A Script; Mega-Rich Celebrities Insults Working Class Fans; Black Voters In Philadelphia Pick Trump Over Harris; Black Voters Offended By Obama Shaming Them; Kamala Says If President Carter Can Vote Early, You Can Too; Obama Gives Smug And Ageist Warning To Young Voters; Walz's Ironic Critique Of Musk's Stage Presence; Harris Campaign Gives Coach Walz Bit Another Try.\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Laura Ingraham, Raymond Arroyo \par \uc2 7,626 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 October 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 VIQ Solutions, Inc. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: I mean think about that, \uc2 Steve Jobs\uc2 , 23 years ago. and how much has changed since then. Amazing. Tomorrow on Special Report, Vice President Harris turns to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and the boss to campaign in Atlanta. Former President Trump hits the trail as well. We've got them all covered. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for the Special Report. Fair, balanced and still unafraid. The Ingraham Angle is now.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. As always, thank you for spending some time with us. 13 days out, and while top polls show the race is extremely tight and very difficult to predict, there are some undeniable trend lines in Trump's favor.\par \par \uc2 Now, even as Harris has a massive money advantage, we see this from the economist. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes the lead as polls swing away from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Now Harris has dropped 10 points in the survey from just a week ago, and Trump, he surged by 10 on the other side, and Harris is only up in two swing states, Michigan and Nevada, according to Bloomberg. Trump leads in Pennsylvania, in Wisconsin, Arizona and North Carolina. And last night, for a moment, it seemed even Obama was feeling it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BARACK OBAMA (D) 44TH U.S. PRESIDENT: I notice my palms are sweating, knees weak, arms are heavy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Heavy. I'm not sure what heavy means, whatever. Of course, like I said, conservatives shouldn't count their chickens. This is still anyone's race. Remember what happened in 2022, a lot of people were disappointed. But that doesn't stop Republicans from having a little fun in their minds, from dreaming of what they saw eight years ago.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  is now President of the United States.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Can we find her? I'd like to interview her tonight, if possible. Now, as close as things are, Democrats may be running out of cards to play. The best they can hope for is that maybe they can juice the female turnout enough to overcome their deficit with other demographic groups, like male voters, Hispanics, black men and young people. And to that I say, Kamala's bad for women. That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 Well, none of it really seems to be sticking. They tried Trump's a dictator in waiting. They even compared him to Adolf Hitler, didn't really work. He's going to unleash the Pentagon on us.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE U.S., (D) PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: He is out for unchecked power. That's what he's looking for. He wants to send the military after American citizens.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The audience was like, what? None of its landing. But they keep going negative.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is increasingly unstable and unhinged and will stop at nothing to claim unchecked power for himself.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And yet, the lower she sunk with her attacks, well, the lower she sunk in the polls. So now what? Well, now she's turning the page on joy and love to a new chapter of fear and loathing.\par \par \uc2 So from now until Election Day, Kamala's crew will spend their time and a lot of money scaring and lying to women in order to increase turnout. Now, although this strategy may be your only hope, given some of the trends I mentioned earlier, it's not in the least inspiring, nor is it optimistic. It's not what we thought we were getting with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . It's just plain cynical and coming from Governor googly eyes, it's plain comical.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. TIM WALZ (D-MN), VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE: Think about all of the women in your life who you love, daughters, wives, moms, cousins, your neighbors, whatever. This election is literally about their lives.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Literally, well, the media also got their marching orders. Women be afraid. Be very afraid.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: If there weren't men like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the world, women actually wouldn't require protection.\par \par \uc2 MITCH LANDRIEU, CO-CHAIR, HARRIS-WALZ CAMPAIGN: The difference could not be more stark relating to women's reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, Mitch, now the most bizarre aspect of their super charge fair campaign targeting women voters is Kamala's decision to involve a former Congresswoman with zero following.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: I was just with one of the leaders, and I think, opinion leaders in the Republican Party. \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 . She is pro-life, but she also understands the pain and the tragedy that has happened since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  allowed Roe v Wade to be overturned.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What tragedy is she talking about? And she is not an opinion leader of the Republican Party. Thank you very much. Look, the tragedy of more babies being born in states like Alabama, Mississippi, Louisiana, this is what the Democrat Party has become, where the right to abort one's offspring until birth is now their central defining sacrosanct organizing tenant, their dogma. But women don't fall for it, regardless of where you are on that issue, because Harris herself is responsible for bringing the tragedy to America, economic suffering with inflation, meaning young families, young women struggle to buy homes and afford basic necessities.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The cost of groceries and gas, everything going so high. We live in a fairly rural area, it's the prices that get us.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I could not afford day care. I tried applying for any kind of assistance and was denied.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Like, are you going to eat this week or are you going to save money to pay rent?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's a heartbreak. And then there's the tragedy of Kamala's open borders, vicious, brutal crimes committed by illegals against women and girls, primarily human trafficking, child sex trafficking. We're never going to know the actual number of victims involved, but their cries go unanswered in the Harris campaign, which is why \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 's words are just not believable.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WALZ: She has had one client, the people. She stood up for women and children against predators and abusers. She stood up for families and communities against transnational gangs and traffickers.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Traffickers. There we are. What a joke. The cartels and the traffickers have been one of the few growth industries under Biden and Harris, and when pressed, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will not apologize for the suffering that her open border has wrought.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Jocelyn Nungaray, Rachel Morin, Laken Riley, they are young women who were brutally assaulted and killed by some of the men who were released at the beginning of the administration. Do you owe those families an apology?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Let me just say, first of all, those are tragic cases. There is no question about that. There is no question about that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You know what I call that, tragic cases. You know the feigned, feigned, you know, concern, that's camera ready compassion. It's totally phony. And women voters are also mothers, and no mother wants to see her son, or her daughter get needlessly killed because of an administration's incompetence. Afghanistan was another Biden-Harris tragedy. And with \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  said to be Secretary of Defense in a Harris administration, moms should prepare for more of their sons and daughters to go off to war, because that will be on the agenda, and maybe even a draft if things get really bad.\par \par \uc2 And how is this any of this good for women again? Women across America, none of the people you're seeing on TV, you're listening to on podcasts really believe that Trump is dangerous. You saw \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  hanging out at the Al Smith dinner with Trump. He thinks Trump's Hitler. I don't think so. And if Trump wins on January 20, 2025, and he goes into the White House. Well, every single member of MSNBC will be back on the air to attack him.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will be at the inaugural, if he can find it. So, will \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . No high profile celebrities, I'm sorry, will be selling their belongings and moving to Europe. Liberals will not go into hiding. It is all a lie, and they know it, and smart and savvy women are too cool and too with it to fall for any of this. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is \uc2 Dana Loesch\uc2 , Nationally Syndicated Radio Host and Brianna Lyman, a correspondent at The Federalist. Dana, now, despite all of this, a new \uc2 UMass Amherst\uc2  poll has Kamala leading Trump among women by seven points, but I've seen other polls as high as 10 perhaps this is a trend into tightening even of this demographic. Are you surprised that they are going with the abortion narrative and the fear and smear campaign in these closing days?\par \par \uc2 DANA LOESCH, NATIONALLY SYNDICATED RADIO HOST: I'm not, Laura, and I think you hit the nail on the head. I'm not surprised at all. And it's just, I mean this, they've been doing this since I was a