 \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. Wait, wait, wait, wait a second. What about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  assuring us, Mr. President, that they've tightened up the border in recent months.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : They're going to have open borders 100 percent, just like they tried to trick everybody. They said they tried to tighten it up a little bit, just to make -- because they have an election coming up.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And of course, from watching the Angle and the reporting of our own Bill Melugin, voters are learning the truth, aren't they? Hundreds of thousands of migrants are right now being fast tracked into the country by other means, through humanitarian parole, through special immigrant visas and via the CBP app. And all communities are being swamped by this influx.\par \par \uc2 Local budgets, they are under strain by migrants who need schooling, they need housing, they need health care, and for all the women out there who are all in for Kamala, perhaps just for a moment, consider what her border policies are doing to young women and girls.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Fox confirming that the suspects arrested in Florida in connection with the sex trafficking of a 15 year old girl were in the United States illegally.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: These people should have never been in this country. This should have never happened. And we see this all the time. We've had four incidences of Palm Beach County involved in illegals that came across the border. Should have never been in this country and committed crimes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The great interview by Martha McCallum and Harris has let him in and hope for the best approach to the border that has facilitated the largest child sex trafficking operation the world has ever seen. How is that for girl power? And of course, Hispanic girls are often the victims here, and Hispanic voters know this, but rather than focus on ending this madness, protecting our own people and protecting the migrants, Democrats try to make Trump out to be the villain here.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE OBAMA\uc2 , FORMER FIRST LADY: It's his same old con, his same old con, doubling down on ugly, misogynistic, racist, lies as a substitute for real ideas and solutions.\par \par \uc2 REP. PRAMILA JAYAPAL (D-WA): Welcome to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 's America, where the federal government tries to coerce state and local governments to adopt the most anti-immigrant policies.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (D), PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We rejected xenophobia of my predecessor and leaders like him around the world.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, gramps (ph). But despite the blow back from the blowhards, Trump kept going, because we all know this, a country without a border, at some point, is not a country at all.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: How millions of people are arriving so quickly, so efficiently. So now, this is the first group that's going to go to the border, and then you're going to come back and pick up more people.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This SUV pulls up, and the migrants are loaded in one by one. Every inch of space taken.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Every week, you get like 200 300.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Of course, the Democrats knew that an open border would end up with situations like that. The cartels cashing in, and Americans and migrants alike would be brutalized as a result. But the thing that really gets me and a lot of this really gets to me, as you know, for 20 years, I've been covering this issue, our border czarina and Alejandro Mayorkas, they didn't give a rip. Remember, they're all about compassion. They don't care because they're fanatics. But Hispanics are not, they're pragmatic and they're patriotic.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BOB UNANUE, CEO, \uc2 GOYA FOODS\uc2 : You're a builder, you're a uniter, you're courageous, you love, and you create. The other side of you know loving and building and creating is hating and destroying and dividing. We have become from the land of opportunity to land of exploitation, and the exploiter-in- chief is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and this administration.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, the Democrats answer to all this is just more of the same, smears and fears. So, no matter what happens two weeks ago, two weeks from today, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the man the D.C. establishment excoriated for being anti-Latino and anti-immigrant, will likely win the largest share of the Latino vote of any Republican in American history. And if he wins the presidency, the GOP, going forward, will have a fighting chance in states like California and Colorado, because success breeds more success, Si Se Puede. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Alfredo Ortiz, CEO of Job Creators Network, and Abraham Enriquez, Founder and President of Bienvenido, both were at Trump's Round Table event today. Alfredo, let's start with you. I know Job Creators Network, \uc2 Bernie Marcus\uc2 , one of the greatest Americans alive have devoted so much time and money to getting the message out to Latino voters across the country. Why is Trump's message resonating more today than it did even four years ago?\par \par \uc2 ALFREDO ORTIZ, CEO, JOB CREATORS NETWORK: Well, Laura, you were absolutely right. President Trump was absolutely right. Bernie was absolutely right, and had the vision to actually understand that Latinos were actually and Hispanics were a reachable community if you hit the right message, and President Trump has hit that right message from an open border perspective, immigrants, Hispanic immigrants do not want an open border because the criminality that comes through that porous border lands in their communities, and so the crime issues that are small business owners. There are 5 million small business owners that are Hispanic out of 33 million.\par \par \uc2 So that's a big chunk of small business owners. The criminality that's coming to their doorsteps and to their businesses is real, and it's also landing in the schools. It's landing in their streets, and that's what Hispanics want to stop. And so they want that border to be closed, the porous border to be closed to address that. And by the way, Laura, they also care about things that you care about, right? We care about the same things. We care about education. We care about faith, family, entrepreneurship, right? Inflation has been horrendous for our small business owners.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Horrible.\par \par \uc2 ORTIZ: It's never been worse, actually, and quite frankly, it's never was better than under President Trump. Hispanics did about --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 ORTIZ: -- $6,500 in real wages, better under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  than they are today, and --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: $6,500 --\par \par \uc2 ORTIZ: -- small businesses are closing down. 6,500.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wow. Real --\par \par \uc2 ORTIZ: And so --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- that's real numbers. That's real wages.\par \par \uc2 ORTIZ: It really is --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I want to move -- move on to Abraham, because Abraham, you're saying that Hispanic voters now second and third generation Americans and that -- and that they're not buying into the old clap trap from the Left, the pandering tactics from the Left. Why is that?\par \par \uc2 ABRAHAM ENRIQUEZ, FOUNDER AND PRESIDENT, BIENVENIDO: Yes, well, first and foremost, Laura, I've got to give you some credit for that Spanish at the top line.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 ENRIQUEZ: The blonde hair and the green eyes might fool some people, but I think when you start calling you Laura Ingraham, first and foremost, Laura, it's great to be with you, but I think your audience needs to understand a few things. One, the average age of Hispanics in America are 29 years old were the youngest racial demographic in the country. And yes, two-thirds of Hispanics on the voter rolls are second and third generation Americans. What does this mean? This means we're assimilating to American culture better.\par \par \uc2 Most of us, you know, have a college degree, and English is predominantly our first language. So, Democrats haven't changed from this idea that they believe all Hispanics care about is immigration, amnesty for all and weak borders. You know what young Hispanics are talking about today, Laura, how can I start a family? How can I buy a home, and how can I start a business? The policies that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has put out on us makes all of those things close to impossible. So, it's no surprise that when \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  shows that young Hispanics under the age of 30 actually acknowledge that they were better off under the Trump policies, which is why he's on record to receive some of the highest approval ratings and votes for a Republican presidential candidate among Hispanic voters.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think it's going to be huge. And Alfredo. When we really look back on this election, we look back at everything that was said about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He's a xenophobe, he's anti-immigrant, he's anti-Latino. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is saying that now, she's giving an interview to Telemundo. You know, we'll read the transcript, but I mean, it's the same old thing, will any of that land? Will that land, especially with Hispanic women, because there is a gender gap?\par \par \uc2 ORTIZ: No, it really won't, Laura. And you should have felt the energy in that room from the Hispanics that were there, and Abraham was there as well. And you could feel that energy. And I have to tell you, one of the most impressive moments and emotional moments is actually when we all laid hands on President Trump --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I saw it.\par \par \uc2 ORTIZ: And praying over him. I mean, faith is such an important part of the Hispanic culture, and the Democrats have completely gotten this wrong, talking about abortion. I mean, they are targeting abortion ads to Hispanic men. I mean, they are so far in this and so far off. It's just ridiculous.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. We got to roll. Alfredo and Abraham, we're going to have you both back before election night. So, thank you very much for joining us tonight, both of you. All right. Kamala flails a brand new interview. She took all day to prepare for this, but what did she really say? That's next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, two weeks from tonight, election returns are going to start trickling in. But today, the supposedly exhausted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  didn't just do the Hispanic forum in Miami. He returned to the swing state of North Carolina for other events. And as for Kamala, well, she's clearly the energizer money of campaigning, because all day long, she was hunkered down in D.C. So much for multitasking on the trail. Hunker down in D.C. She needed the entire day to prep for NBC News, an interview there, and for Telemundo tomorrow, where she was pressed on her economic pitch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Do you think that's not landing with voters? It's the opposite. Former President Trump leads you on this issue.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Well, when I'm out, this is why I'm going out to Wisconsin, Pennsylvania and\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: And Michigan.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Michigan, excuse me, just got in late this morning, actually, but going to three states yesterday, and I'm going to continue being on the road, I have to earn the vote.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And thus you can see why this modern woman needs a man to save her.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BARACK OBAMA (D) 44TH U.S. PRESIDENT: Disruptions from the pandemic caused price hikes. It put a strain on family budgets, and people started feeling like no matter how hard they worked, they were just treading water. So, I understand why folks are looking to shake things up. What I cannot understand is why anybody would think that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will shake things up in a way that's good for you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That seems to fall flat. I mean, I don't know. Charlie Hurt, Fox News Contributor, Washington Times Opinion Editor. Charlie, does Obama even seem to believe what he's saying? I mean, it seems like the expiration date is long since passed with hope and change that didn't seem to work at all.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, OPINION EDITOR, WASHINGTON TIMES: Yes, of course. And let's not forget, of course, you know, probably the single person in Washington who is more responsible than anybody else for giving us \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  himself.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HURT: So, I think you and I owe him a bit of a debt of gratitude. But you know, you look back, remember, throughout his entire career, he could get himself elected, he could not transfer any of that good will to anybody else all of the midterms. What was it? Over 1000 Democrats lost their offices, all the while \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was pursuing his agenda. It got himself re-elected once. But man, he is not good at passing the love around, and we see it, I think, in the failure -- the failings, the obvious failings of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's campaign right now.\par \par \uc2 You know, the reason she's so terrible at this stuff is because she doesn't know what she thinks. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has able to do 50 interviews in a day and wheel through them because