nybody else's problem.\par \par \uc2 You know, it's really interesting though that she's unable to answer that simple question. And if the Biden campaign and then later the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaign had been a smart campaign, months ago, they would have announced, we're -- no matter what happens if we get elected, we're going to pardon \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on everything. It would have been a very smart move months ago, months ago, it would have taken some of the wind out of the sails. But there -- both of them are so stingy, they're so angry, they're so full of nothing but hatred for this guy that they weren't able to recognize how smart that was. And here she is now, sounding like a salty school mom who just sucked on a lemon and can't come up with any sort of visionary -- vision that make -- that brings voters together and can't even come up with a kind of a neat tactic that actually might be somewhat effective.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Charlie, I found it all so inspirational. And just when I think of girl power, I think of those types of answers from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . I mean, that's what our girls are aspiring --\par \par \uc2 HURT: And bringing out a man to save you. I love that.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, no, damsel in distress, come on. We're back to the early 1900s. Charlie, who's taking us back? I think that's taking us back, Charlie, thank you. It's always wonderful to see you. All right, the blue wall you've heard is cracking. NBC News is reporting that North Carolina is now slipping away from Democrats, and there are signs that Wisconsin, Michigan and Pennsylvania, remember they paved the path to the White House for the last two Democrat presidents. That could be gone too, which is 14 days until the election. There are concerns within \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's campaign about whether the VP can claim all three states.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, someone who knows this all too well. Matt Towery, political analyst and pollster. Matt,