 than the other way around. And that's a vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  this time this year.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Vivek, I can't wait to have you back right before the election. This is going to be fun. Thank you, as always, for joining us. All right, up next, Kamala wants to keep you in the dark, literally. I'll tell you how, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Democrats are in the dark about pretty much every issue, the economy, the border, and their crazy climate policies will literally put us all in the dark. Now over the weekend, we saw what happens when lunatics are in charge of energy policy, as they are in Cuba.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: You've got a country of 11 million people, and really for the past five days, most of them have been in the dark unless you have a generator if you're a fancy hotel or if you're in a hospital. It's been incredibly challenging for families, especially for those with small children.\par \par \uc2 Those Cuban power stations were built by the Soviet Union and most of them are almost 50 years old.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, that can't happen here, right? Joining me now, Ray Washburne, chairman and CEO of Charter Holdings, former OPIC head in the Trump administration. Ray, great to see you. Now, could this kind of total meltdown of an aging electrical grid happen in the U.S. under these crazy greeniac policies of Harris?\par \par \uc2 RAY WASHBURNE, CHAIRMAN AND CEO, CHARTER HOLDINGS: Yeah, well, I think what's happening in Cuba could be indicative of what's happening in the United States right now. Under the Harris-Biden energy policy, we haven't increased our base load in the United States for electrical generation power. In the last four years, AI and data centers have come along and we're seeing absorption going up the next 10 years, over 150 percent, and we're doing nothing other than trying to do these renewable