as.\par \par \uc2 This country is blessed with the greatest natural resources the world's ever known, and we need to use those.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How much of a hit has our economy, Ray, and you're an incredibly successful businessman in Texas. You know, restaurants, real estate, all these stuff that you invested in over the years. How much has the energy costs in our country affected our economy overall?\par \par \uc2 WASHBURNE: Well, not only to businesses, just to people, the normal person in the street. Look at what -- look at your electrical bill today versus five years ago when Trump was president. It's skyrocketed. And that has just affected us in the worst way.\par \par \uc2 And now when we're building new restaurants and you're sitting there, fortunately, we're in Texas, but if we're going to other states like California, how can you afford to do that when you think they're going to go all electric on you?\par \par \uc2 I mean, these mandates they're putting in place are just a massive, massive tamp down on our economy.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And the regular folks are the ones who always get hurt the most in this insane greeniac vision, which is a nightmare for most people. Ray, thanks for educating us. I never knew what baseload was before until tonight. Now I know. All right, thanks Ray.\par \par \uc2 Americans are over the MAGA-shaming of the left. What does that mean? I'll tell you next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Why you vote for Trump?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Because I want to be able to afford my lifestyle and just make America better.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I'm voting for Trump because as a woman in America, I don't currently feel safe with the amount of illegal people here, and I'm ready for those borders to be closed.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: If Kamala's elected president, I don't think we'll be American in the next three years.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I was formerly a Democrat, but I'm a Jewish student here. And after October 7th, I sort of switched over.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I know you're tired of paying for high gas prices, high rent, high everything. Dude, how are you affording your groceries?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I'm voting for Trump.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Trump.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Trump.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Trump.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Trump.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Trump.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Trump.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Trump.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Trump.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, the era of the silent Trump voter, done. MAGA's populist wave's sweeping the nation, especially among younger voters. Even Hollywood movie stars are getting involved.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: My cry to all of you out there, you closeted conservatives, closeted Trump voters, you all, it's now or never. If you need to come out publicly and say it, if you feel like you still can't, then don't. You know, I would never pressure you to that. But know that if what you're afraid of is somehow the backlash of an industry that's not going to exist very soon, then don't let that, don't let that hold you back.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Joining me now, Jobob Taeleifi, and Alex Clark, both contributors with Turning Point USA. All right, I love this story. I'm heading to Texas A&M this weekend, and I know there are a lot of Trump supporters there in College Station, Texas. But Alex, what has caused this new boldness in support of Trump?\par \par \uc2 ALEX CLARK, TURNING POINT USA CONTRIBUTOR: Well, I believe Trump's October surprise was becoming more likeable than ever before, Laura. He's on another level with his charm, his empathy, his authenticity, his sense of humor. Don't forget he's also going on podcasts that everybody loves, like Theo Vonn and Joe Rogan now. We learned this Friday he's going to go on Rogan.\