of a downsized American dream, you know, because they can't reach it, so just like redefine it. The American dream ought to be the Cadillac of aspirations, but in an age of tight money, it's just time to, you know, readjust their scope a bit. Enter the townhouse. It's the American dream, but with a smaller backyard.\par \par \uc2 Alex, that is their solution, OK? Give up the idea of owning your own home. Give up the idea of owning a car. Rent, you know, you know, do a, you know, daily rental of a car, and forget the idea of raising a family and a home. That's what they're doing.\par \par \uc2 CLARK: Yeah. So, the main demographic, the main age group that's going to pertain to are the younger millennials. So, we are the ones who are now at the age where we are starting to have families, raise kids and think about buying a home. Gen Z still a little bit too young. They're probably, definitely, still doing the apartment thing. And millennials have been living this life, right? So, we've already been dealing with this for the last four years.\par \par \uc2 So, selling us, I'm like, hey, you know what? Downsize everybody. Just do your fair share. We've already been living this. We do not enjoy it. And the Democrats are not thinking about this same age group are the ones who are very, very enthused and excited about this RFK Jr. endorsement and all of the health stuff. This is the most popular issue with millennial moms.\par \par \uc2 I know that the Democrats are banking on abortion with women. And I am telling you, my audience, I have one of the biggest conservative female audiences, 25 to 35. They are so obsessed with the Maha movement. This is going to be neck and neck with the women voting for abortion. Do not underestimate it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I love it. Jobob, I want to just briefly talk about dating in your world, because according to Axios, 43 percent of people between the ages of 18 and 34 say that have a more negative view of a date if they were told they voted for Trump, 19 percent they said they'd have a negative view of a date who voted for VP Harris.\par \par \uc2 Jobob, so much for the tolerant left. You vote for Trump? Some of the young feminazi types and they're not interested in you. Is that a big loss?\par \par \uc2 TAELEIFI: Well, you know, it's a loss for them. I would say it's a pretty easy interview if that's going to be the only question that matters. So, good luck out there in the dating world. But also, maybe if they're not going to date you because you voted for Trump, you got out in the early part of that relationship. That's a good thing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Early detection, Alex and Jobob. That's actually a good thing in health and it's a good thing in dating. Both of you, we'll have you back before the election night. This is going to be a lot of fun. Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 That is it for us tonight. This was a jam-packed show. It was fun. Make sure to follow me on social media. Thank you for watching. Remember, it is America now and forever. Two weeks from tonight, we'll all be up in New York, prime time on the same panel. A lot of fun. Jesse will be there. And he's here in about three seconds.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020241023ekam00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Serves Up Working Class Cred; Pro-Weed Measure In Florida Backed By Dollar; A Kamala loss would blame racism and sexism; Harris downplay black voters drift; The left's ant-Christian rhetoric; Chr