ike Trump had turnover in his first couple of years in the administration, because he just got there. She was a Senator for years before that, you should have very little turnover in her office --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He didn't have 90 percent turnover --\par \par \uc2 DUFFY: Not at all.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: -- Sean. No way, not close to that.\par \par \uc2 DUFFY: No, no, I know, but -- no, no, I know, but there was turnover, Laura. This is massive turnover. And you know what, in Washington, D.C., people love to be near power. The vice presidency is a great place to be. It has to be that bad that 90 some percent of your staff leaves, or you fire them. That says a lot about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . And by the way, she's made a mistake, and she's doubled down on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's policies. But also, this is a race of being authentic. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , put him in any venue, he's authentically --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 DUFFY: -- Donald -- \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  doesn't know who she is, and I think people read that and they don't trust her, and they don't like her because they don't know who she is.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Alex, I think it's hysterically funny, along with a lot of other things that he, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , can go into, you know, a setting in the Bronx, in this case, a barbershop and he just acts completely, let you know, everyone who knows him, that's just who he is. But if you put her in the same setting, she looks like she's always wondering where the teleprompter is. It never seems natural. I think that resonates poorly with many people. There's no authenticity there.\par \par \uc2 MARLOW: You're so right about this. Trump and Vance both look so comfortable with normal people, because they are comfortable with normal people. Trump had a great line last night, where he said that she probably brings a teleprompter to dinner with Doug. It's perfect. It's not just funny. It might be true. How do we know? We nev