 And what I think is so notable, Laura, is that when he talks about war, he talks about it the way any moral person should by saying the problem with war is actually that it kills huge number of people. It takes immense amounts of lives.\par \par \uc2 You will never hear \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  talk that way. You'll never hear her suggest a diplomatic solution, because in Democratic Party politics, suggesting that is taboo. It provokes accusation of being a Russian agent.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We're not even talking about the number of people who've been killed. Do you notice that's never even mentioned? I mean, it's astronomical. I don't even think we know the final or the current tally. These facts are heartbreaking.\par \par \uc2 I mean, you read them and you think, my god. I mean, this does have to stop.\par \par \uc2 GREENWALD: Well, I mean, we fight in a lot of wars. We participate in a lot of wars. We fund a lot of wars. And we almost never talk about the dead of the countries we don't care about. And this is what offended me so much was from the beginning, the claim of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was, we have to fund the war in Ukraine, because we have to protect Ukraine and Ukrainians, when in reality, what they were after was the destruction of Ukraine, killing huge numbers of Ukrainians to serve this broader geopolitical goal that I don't really understand. I don't think anyone understands why we have, which is to weaken Russia.\par \par \uc2 And they've now explicitly been saying, oh, don't worry about this war. It's only young Ukrainians and increasingly middle-aged Ukrainians who don't actually want to fight, but who are forced to being used as cannon fodder. It's so grotesquely immoral, especially because it was inevitable all along that what is happening now is what was going to happen, which is Russia being a massively bigger country was always going to win this war.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah. Well, she's the border czarina 