 or you're just a person who thinks that we shouldn't throw our elderly folks into poverty, then join the Trump campaign, send the illegal aliens home before they bankrupt the programs that our people rely on.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: All right, we'll keep an eye on that. That is J.D. Vance, the vice presidential candidate. He is in Lycoming County, which is smack dab in the middle, a bit to the north in between Philadelphia and Pittsburgh. So, they're spending a ton of time in Pennsylvania for understandable reasons with 20 days to go.\par \par \uc2 And we're going to talk a little bit about the latest line of attack by Vice President Harris against former President Trump. She is talking a lot about the fact that she sees him as weak and unfit to serve, and we heard some of that here from one of her spokespeople yesterday.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , U.S. VICE PRESIDENT, DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE: He won't put out his medical records. And you have to ask, why is his staff doing that? And it may be because they think he's just not ready and unfit and unstable.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: All right. So, you get the idea there. Senior Trump campaign official \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2  snaps back, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, breaking just moments ago, Fulton County, Georgia D.A. Fani Willis reportedly now asking a court to reinstate six criminal charges against former President Trump and his co-defendants. That's according to the Atlanta Journal-Constitution. And you remember that the judge threw out some of these charges in March, saying that they were not specific enough.\par \par \uc2 The case is on hold right now while an appeals court considers whether Willis should step aside. The judge let her stay on after the former prosecutor, Nathan Wade, stepped down after there were revelations and questions about their romantic relationship and the ethics surrounding that case. And as I said, some of those charges were dropped, now she's trying to bring them back.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: All right. On that and other things, let's bring in \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2 , Trump 2024 senior official. Corey, good to have you with us today.\par \par \uc2 You know, I find it interesting that the efforts to bring these cases back do not seem to be central in any of the campaigning. And for a while it felt like all of this, lawfare or whatever you want to call it, was going to be one of the major centers of the thrust of the Harris campaign or the Democrats campaign. What do you think is going on there?\par \par \uc2 COREY LEWANDOWSKI\uc2 , TRUMP 2024 SENIOR OFFICIAL: Well, clearly the Biden- Harris administration wanted to use a two-tiered justice system to go after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , probably first to try and push him out of the race, probably try to intimidate him with the raid on his home at Mar-a-Lago. But what we've seen is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a fighter. He's fought back. This has been a political prosecution against him in the cases in Georgia, in the case in Florida with \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 , in the case in Washington, D.C., and obviously the case in New York. And it has only emboldened his supporters to support him more because he has said many times, and I believe it, that he's the only thing standing between the federal government coming after them is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, I guess what I was getting at is, do you think that voters didn't respond to that, you know, that, that they didn't really run with it, that it wasn't as successful, you know, all of this stuff gets poll tested with voters. Do you think that it didn't really work?\par \par \uc2 LEWANDOWSKI: Yes, the voters don't care about it, Martha. What they care about is the pocketbook issues. They ask the age old question, are you better off today than you were four years ago? And by every discernible metric, the answer is no. So, when you can't put gas in your car or food on your table, or as we come into the fall, home heating oil into your homes, they don't care about the political prosecutions as an issue that they want to vote against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for. They want to vote for themselves. They want to make sure that we've got a secure border so that their families are safe. But most importantly, and every polling data indicates it, it's the economy, stupid, as the old saying goes.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Well, we see that in all the polling. And I just find it fascinating when you consider all the time and effort that was put into all of those cases that you barely hear about them anymore, although there are sort of sputtering up here and there as they try to revive them.\par \par \uc2 You know, we mentioned in the tease, Corey, this question that Harris seems to be focusing on right now. She's got 20 days to go and she's calling the former president unhinged, unfit, all this stuff. I just want to remind people that \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  did something very similar at the end of the 2016 race. Let's remind people. Let's take a look at what she was doing.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HILLARY CLINTON\uc2 , FORMER DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE: His latest \uc2 Twitter\uc2  meltdown is unhinged.\par \par \uc2 Temperamentally unfit and totally unqualified to be president and commander-in-chief.\par \par \uc2 He has proven himself unfit.\par \par \uc2 We've never had someone so unqualified and unfit to be president and commander-in-chief.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So we know how that worked out. Did you find it curious that this is a thrust with 20 days to go here from the other side?\par \par \uc2 LEWANDOWSKI: Well, it's a desperate tactic because you've got a candidate in Vice President Harris who has no policies that are going to benefit the American people. So, you try and make the election, in her case, about \uc2