to neighboring Syria. These vulnerable people left with no place to live as the campaign continues.\par \par \uc2 With the fight ongoing against Iran's largest proxy, attention is shifting to Iran itself after it launched a ballistic missile attack against Israel last week. Israeli officials say there will be a response to the 180 missiles, and it will be severe, with Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  saying this overnight.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BENJAMIN NETANYAHU\uc2 , ISRAELI PRIME MINISTER (through translator): No country in the world would accept such an attack on its cities and citizens, nor would the state of Israel. Israel has both the duty and the right to defend itself and respond to these attacks, and that is what we will do.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 YINGST: Overnight, Israel ramped up airstrikes against the Gaza Strip, killing multiple Palestinians there, and this morning issuing new evacuation orders for residents of northern Gaza. Just moments ago, there were sirens sounding in southern Israel amid renewed rocket fire from \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shannon.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Trey Yingst reporting from Israel. We look forward to your special 10 p.m. Eastern on Fox News Channel tonight. Trey, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, House Speaker Mike Johnson. Speaker, welcome back to "Fox News Sunday."\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE JOHNSON, (R-LA) SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE: Hey Shannon, great to be with you as always.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: OK, so we're talking the Middle East as we now await to see what Israel's response is to the incoming attack by Iran. There's questions -- there are questions about whether or not Congress may need to come back for a supplemental for Israel.\par \par \uc2 Now, the same day that that attack was incoming from Iran, Secretary Blinken wrote this in Foreign Affairs. He said, "The Biden administration's strategy has been to put the United States in a much stronger geopolitical position today than it was four years ago." He says when the Harris and Biden administration -- Biden-Harris administration came in, our enemies saw a country that was in decline, that there was an undermining of norms and alliances. Now, the Secretary says he doesn't do politics, but what do you make of his statements?\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: The statement, it's nonsense. Of course, everything that they've done since day one, the Biden-Harris administration, is project weakness on the world stage and that has put us in the most dangerous situation that we have been in since World War II.\par \par \uc2 Our allies are nervous, our adversaries do not fear us, they don't respect us and that is why China, Russia, Iran, North Korea, terrorists and tyrants around the world are coordinating against us and that is why you're seeing the provocations of the war in Israel. Russia moved on Ukraine, China doing all the things they're doing and threatening Taiwan. None of this happened on President Trump's watch because he was a steady hand, a strong hand at the wheel. We have got to re-elect him so that we can restore the order in the world and project peace through strength again. That's what we have to get back to and it cannot happen soon enough.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: So, while you consider additional funding for Israel, obviously the main thought for most people is about Hurricane Helene and the victims left in the wake of that. Hundreds still missing, we don't even know their fate at this point. You've been to Georgia, Florida, you have plans to go to North Carolina as well. What are you seeing and what do you make of the local, state and fed responses?\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: Well, I would just tell you at the federal level, this has been a massive failure and you could just ask the people there on the ground. I have been there, I was in Georgia, I was in Florida where Hurricane Helene made landfall there on the coast and then we'll be going to the hardest hit parts of North Carolina on Wednesday of this week.\par \par \uc2 When you talk to the people who are directly affected, they will tell you that this has been an abject failure. FEMA has lost sight of its core mission, I think, in so many cases. And the administration has not shown that they were prepared for this eventuality, in this terrible disaster.\par \par \uc2 The thing about hurricane, Shannon, is that we know that they're coming well in advance you know they had more than a week's notice of this, and yet, we still have people who have not been served and even rescued in North Carolina. It is a heart-breaking tragic and infuriating situation to have the federal government fail as they have.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, and we've got now as the Storm Milton that's being tracked in the Florida gulf, may land there as a category three later this week.\par \par \uc2 So DHS Secretary Mayorkas has said, they don't have money to get through what they need for the rest of this hurricane season. We've heard similar statements from the Secretary of Transportation. President Biden has said more money is needed.\par \par \uc2 He actually sent a letter to congressional leaders on Friday night, including you. And he said specifically, the \uc2 Small Business Administration\uc2  is in real trouble. Here's what he says. I warned the Congress of this potential shortfall even before Hurricane Helene landed on America's shores. I requested more funding for SBA multiple times over these past several months, and most recently my administration underscored that request as you prepared a continuing resolution to fund the government.\par \par \uc2 Will you call Congress back before the election? Do you need to?\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: Look, we'll be back in session immediately after the election. That's 30 days from now. The thing about these hurricanes and disasters of this magnitude is that it takes a while to calculate the actual damages, and the states are going to need some time to do