mising not to fact check the candidates -- well, the moderators, why play by the rules? They constantly attempted to insert their own so-called facts after answers only from J.D. Vance.\par \par \uc2 In the end, it didn't matter. Vance was able to rise above it, call them out. On X, people even joked that \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  look ready to vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and J.D. Vance after last night's performance. I'd like to agree with Senator Vance on that which was pretty funny.\par \par \uc2 And following the debate when J.D. Vance head it to the spin room to answer more questions, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  while he scurried off to grab some pizza, need a little comfort food where he tried very hard to avoid any and all questions about his horrific debate performance. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Governor, you said you become friends with school shooters during the debate. Can you clarify what you meant on that?\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Can you clarify what you meant when you said you befriended school shooters? Why did you say you were in Hong Kong when reports say you weren't?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'll take the school -- shoe -- school shooter special, please. It's so bizarre.\par \par \uc2 Today in Pennsylvania, when asked again to clarify his comments about being friends with school shooters and his bizarre word salads about one of his many trips to China is outright lying, he still struggled to come up with a simple answer. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Do you want to clarify the comments that you made about school shooters?\par \par \uc2 WALZ: Yeah, and look, you got to see me these folks know me. I'm super passionate about this. The question come up about school shooting, we're talking about everything except school shootings. And I sat as a member of Congress with the Sandy Hook parents and it was a profound movement. David Hogg is a good friend of 