ame to this debate to land a bunch of punches and he did. He landed a lot of punches in between all the niceties and all of that, and the thing that that really stood out to me was that \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  did not seem prepared for it.\par \par \uc2 DANA BASH, CNN HOST: I think the lack of interviews that he has done with national media, with local media, it showed. He needed more rest.\par \par \uc2 JOHN KING, CNN CHIEF NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Two issues driving the campaign right now are Harris has a big deficit on the economy, Harris has a big deficit on immigration, and Republicans were happy tonight and Democrats a little bit nervous that on those two issues, Vance carried it.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I mean, it's pretty clear Vance outclassed Walz tonight. I mean, I was watching this and all I could think of was, man, Walz is so in over his head.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And while fake news CNN is grappling with reality, the far-left lunatics at MSDNC, well, was an absolute fit of hysteria. It was funny for all the wrong reasons on their part. They lost it. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It's the audacity. I agree with you that we're in year nine and no one knows how to cover the audacity. The audacity is it is it so much should have said stop it -- stop, stop. Are you effing kidding me? And they should have they should have dropped that F bomb, right? I mean, they should just -- are we -- this is a debate. This may be the only chance people have to see the difference.\par \par \uc2 And instead, I mean, I'll go back to my toothpicks, J.D. Vance, just put one little toothpick on top of the other and said I'm for this and I'm for this and I'm so sorry those women died they died because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: And so, I think that the people who want the fist fight are the base of the Democratic Party. Democrats want to see someone get up there and give a knuckle sandwich to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . That's what they want, but that is not the group of people who need this debate.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I think they might want to consider free Xanax or the host at MSDNC, and of course, MSDNC's liberal viewers could always, always count on America's number one tinfoil hack conspiracy theorist, Rachel Maddow to lie straight to their faces and protect them from any and all truth. And last night, she delivered big time once again proclaiming a great victory for \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , only one in the country that thought that but take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RACHEL MADDOW, MSNBC HOST: I think the big picture takeaway from this is that one of these candidates is much slicker than the other, is a much more practiced kind of professional debate style speaker, and the other candidate won.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: "Hillbilly Elegy", really? Anyway, that's almost as believable as a year and year long -- long obsession with the Russia hoax, the Russia hoax, the Russia hoax.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, "Politico" was also serving up some truly insane propaganda. They actually claimed that Walz's wide-eyed deer in the headlights look of sheer terror and panic was actually a sign of passion and intensity. Wow. They had to stretch to make that one up.\par \par \uc2 And the -- you know, the same time by the way, the same "Politico" reporting that J.D. Vance's beard is triggering to women in America, quote, conveying aggression and opposition to feminist ideals. I wonder who they're voting for.\par \par \uc2 But if you really need any more evidence that J.D. Vance crush \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  during last night's debate, take a look at this headline from "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 ", quote: Vance's dominant debate performance shows why he's Trump's running mate.\par \par \uc2 Mark my words, this will have an impact on what is a very close race, as Senator Vance pointed out competently last night, that leadership matters. And by the way, after nearly four years under Biden and Harris, so you better off than you were four years ago? Is the economy better off? Are the borders better off? Are you cit -- towns and cities safer?\par \par \uc2 How do you like paying a dollar plus more per gallon of gasoline? And how do you think we're doing on the world stage? How is that war in Europe going?\par \par \uc2 We're on the verge of a complete, you know, breakout of war in the Middle East. We know that Harris is incompetent, and it looks and it feels like nothing but incompetence. You're not better off than you were four years ago. Our country is far worse off. The world is a far more dangerous place.\par \par \uc2 And under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in spite of their predictions of the death of democracy -- well, everything was better. We didn't have war in Europe. We didn't have war in the Middle East. We didn't have Iranian mullahs and their proxies, you know, creating havoc and shooting off hundreds of ballistic missiles, their proxies, and Iran themselves were bankrupt.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held them in check. They were probably about on the verge of going under, but under Biden -- well, billions of dollars were unfrozen and deposited in the accounts of the Iranian mullahs. The Islamic Republic made billions and billions, thanks to Harris and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  after their sanctions were either eased or they just simply turned a blind eye to them and never enforced them.\par \par \uc2 Harris and Biden made Iran rich again, so that they can then foment murder and terrorism worldwide which we've been watching. In 2021, Biden Harris, they even lifted sanctions on two Iranian missile producers. And, of course, they brought back that idiotic Iranian deal which puts put them on a path to becoming a nuclear power.\par \par \uc2 And now, our closest ally in the Middle East, Israel, they are now, fighting a multi-front war while Iranian missiles rain down on Tel Aviv and all throughout Israel, and the idiotic Biden-Harris plan to appease the Iranian mullahs has been an abject failure. But to this day, they refuse to change tactics.\par \par \uc2 Here's Biden, you know, here they got attacked with nearly 200 ballistic missiles, a massive escalation, and what has been going on. They're not using their proxies, \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in the south, \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  in the north, the Houthi rebels. No, they're going with ballistic missiles straight at Israel.\par \par \uc2 But what's -- what's Joe's advice? What it's always been -- please show restraint, please show restraint. No, don't attack their nuclear facilities. I promise them they could -- they could pursue nuclear power.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Obviously, Iran has gone way out of -- I mean, is way off board. We're going to -- putting together a joint statement, hasn't been done yet. It'll be done before too long probably by the time we land and there's going to be some sanctions imposed on Iran.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Would you support an attack on Iran's nuclear sites by Israel?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: The answer is no.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The answer should be yes. You know, sanctions, what, like the ones you lifted you're going to put a couple of them back in place?\par \par \uc2 Here -- here's what the United States of America, if we had strong leaders, what their message would be. Now, Joe hasn't spoken to Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 . \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has. But the message should be clear, unambiguous, go win your war against those radical Islamic terrorists that attacked your country, murdered your citizens, kidnapped them, raped them, tortured them and beheaded them, even if Kamala doesn't ever want you to say the words radical Islamic terrorism or illegal alien.\par \par \uc2 Now, if Biden-Harris get their way, it's only a matter of time before the world's number one state sponsor of terror will start producing nuclear warheads and the odds I would bet are very high they would use them.\par \par \uc2 How does that benefit anybody in the world? How does that contribute to global peace? The Harris-Biden administration is actively putting our country in the entire world at risk with their appeasement policies that are at the very least naive, but far worst sinister in my view.\par \par \uc2 It's not too l late to reverse course. In 34 days and sooner for those of you that vote early, you can write the ship, you can get our country back on track, you can restore America's role as the leader of the free world.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, FOX news contributor, former speaker of the House Newt Gingrich.\par \par \uc2 Let's start with the debate last night, get your reaction.\par \par \uc2 NEWT GINGRICH, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, I think it was a great moment for J.D. Vance. I thought he was remarkable it's almost a case study that people could use to see this is how you do it, including taking on the \uc2 CBS\uc2  moderator when she clearly was wrong and you just going right at her. I mean, it was absolutely the right thing.\par \par \uc2 He was friendly. He was personable. When it was appropriate, he used things out of his own family, his own background. I thought it was remarkable.\par \par \uc2 And you watched Walz who really is not in the right league. I mean, Walz shouldn't be out there. He's not a national player. He's not fast enough. He doesn't know enough, he's not confident enough.\par \par \uc2 And I almost felt sorry for him because he'd been put in a position where as at one point, J.D. Vance said, you know, you have a problem because you have to play whack-a-mole because every time you turn around, something would come up where he'd have to somehow defend \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . And I thought that J.D. won by 