day with Melania Trump, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. With the election just 34 days away, it appears momentum is now beginning to build clearly for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . According to a new set of Insider Advantage polls, from the Sun Belt states, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is up in Arizona. He leads in the state of North Carolina as well. The race in Georgia right now he has as a tie but his numbers in -- but new numbers in the Quinnipiac poll -- well, they were even better. According to their polling, Trump holds a six-point lead in Georgia, one-point lead in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a new set of polls by Trafalgar show strong numbers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the Rust Belt. Their Pennsylvania poll released over the weekend shows \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ahead by more than two points, a brand new Michigan poll has him ahead by an identical margin and the new poll out of the state of Wisconsin showed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ahead by one point there.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here with reaction, pollsters Matt Towery, Robert Cahaly. And for the record, two of the most accurate posters in both 2020 and 2016.\par \par \uc2 Good to see you both.\par \par \uc2 Matt, let's -- let's -- let's go -- let's do a whip around the country. Georgia, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, Michigan, Arizona, Nevada. Where are we?\par \par \uc2 MATT TOWERY, POLLSTER: Well, I've got four points. I don't usually use my notes, Sean. We've been doing this a long time, but tonight, I'm going to go through some very quickly. And I'll cover that. First of all, President Trump will get credit and I think it'll help him in the polls that tremendous job by Vance because it shows he made a great pick.\par \par \uc2 Number two, beware of these polls that you're seeing right now that the media is rolling out to say, oh, Harris is gaining speed. They're rolling out polls. For example, Cook Political Report find pollsters who work for them that's September 19 through 25. We got to get to the fresh polls, and the fresh poll show exactly what you said in the Sun Belt states.\par \par \uc2 Georgia is a little iffy I think, and I'm from Georgia, know it well. I think I'm right about that, they need some work there. But I even have Nevada now going back to Trump and that's a big move.\par \par \uc2 Finally, I would also say that what you're seeing and causing this increase is an increase in his support among African-Americans, Hispanic voters, young voters, and some independent move as well. So when the momentum starts to shift, you can feel the momentum.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats are trying to stop it with throwing out the stuff, you know, the indictments and January 6th, and the like and that is not going to stop this. Something else will have to stop Trump's momentum because we see it, at least I do, and I know Robert does as well.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And, Robert, I mean, when you look at Atlas and Trafalgar and Insider Advantage, that's both your polls and Rasmussen, you're the top pollsters in 2020, Robert, let's get your take. Let's do a whip around the swing states and what are you seeing.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT CAHALY, POLLSTER: Well, I -- very much the same as Matt. I mean, we -- we're showing a separation. One of the things that Trump and actually J.D. Vance accomplished very well was they created the sense in the voters minds of this woman is telling me what she wants me to hear and if she believed all this, she'd have already done it.\par \par \uc2 And so, I think that explains why we're seeing an increase in Pennsylvania which I think is separating -- moving Trump's way strongly. I see the same thing in Michigan. It's getting stronger, and just a little bit less on Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Now, Matt did the other states and I'll kind of defer to him. I think Georgia is a little more of a challenge than other people think.\par \par \uc2 But one of the things that I don't think J.D. Vance got enough credit for last night was how well he answered the climate change question. He gave the most rational explanation I've seen on the environment, talking about if you really truly care about environment, you'd be on-shoring jobs, you've been using America's clean energy, and basically giving you a template of how Republicans should answer that question. And I think that's something that is really helping and will help with the young people.\par \par \uc2 He wasn't this meme and caricature, this boogeyman that he had been portrayed. He was -- delivered a rational arguments that made sense. And like he said, the sense of the common person.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, Matt, I -- when you get to this point in any campaign, I think the motto's got to be win every day or try to win every day, and I see this momentum shift as it relates to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and I would even trace it back to this network and appearance that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had with our own Greg Gutfeld, followed by Union Dale.\par \par \uc2 And people think, well, why -- why would he be campaigning in New York? Because a lot of congressional seats actually made a big difference back in 2022. But if it's about winning the day, I would say that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  now has put, you know, put together what is the equivalent of almost two straight weeks where he's winning every day, and I don't really see anything on the horizon -- again, there's always the possibility of an unforeseen event, of Democrats shifting momentum here.\par \par \uc2 I don't see \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  now going to do an interview that's going to you know blow Americans away or \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , if he's capable of even doing an interview. Do you agree with that idea about winning the day? Do you think the momentum has shifted in terms of, you know, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has an ability to make news when -- when they do not? Because they're not anywhere.\par \par \uc2 Well, I think -- I think -- I think momentum goes back and forth in campaigns. We know that. But right now, you've got the forces of unrest in the Middle East. You have a hurricane that been poorly addressed.\par \par \uc2 I know because I was in the middle of it and lost cars and the like to it and there are people in North Carolina still who don't have water --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They don't care about your cars --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TOWERY: Don't have electricity.\par \par \uc2 Don't say that, of course, I loved my cars, Hannity. And I -- it was a big pain in the rear end, the whole thing.\par \par \uc2 But let me just say this, I think the momentum has shifted towards Trump, I think it -- I think it will stay that way unless the Democrats try to manufacture something that we don't know about right now, and that could easily happen. It -- any moment, they can try to shift something.\par \par \uc2 But so far, they're the ones facing the strike among the longshore dockworkers and they're the ones who are not able to deal with the hurricane, and they're the ones who are dealing with the Middle East. And that's a big three-problem-prong the Democrats have to deal with.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, one thing, I -- you know with the storm being as damaging is it's been and the very poor response by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who sat on the beach and Kamala hanging out with her friends in Hollywood, a lot of the areas affected in North Carolina and Georgia, Robert Cahaly, are heavily red areas. Is that going to be a problem for people voting down the line as they're dealing with rebuilding their lives? We'll talk to \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  later.\par \par \uc2 CAHALY: I don't know that it's necessarily -- I don't know this going to necessarily affect whether they vote, but they're going to vote with some anger because they see plenty of money for everybody else and they're going to be frustrated when this, you know, it's taking weeks to get the power back on, and the federal response is so slow and they're going to see real, you know, they've seen real more real leadership out of \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2  than they've seen out of the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, it was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  calling \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , and thanks to Elon, Starlink now is up. And after a week with no communication, now, people are finally being able to communicate for the first time. Tip of the hat to \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . I mean, that was -- that was very generous of Elon and very smart of Trump to call him.\par \par \uc2 Appreciate both of you.\par \par \uc2 All right. We'll watch closely. When we come back, I spoke with the former First Lady Melania Trump about her new book and about this upcoming election. She's next and then we'll check in with North Carolina Senator \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2 , straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, yesterday, I sat down with former First Lady Melania Trump to discuss her new memoir called "Melania". We spoke about the upcoming election, the importance of this race and the lawfare that is being used against her husband, her family.\par \par \uc2 Here's part one of that interview. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Madam First Lady, it's great to see you again.\par \par \uc2 MELANIA TRUMP, FORMER FIRST LADY: Nice to see you, too.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you for doing this.\par \par \uc2 You don't love media interviews and I don't blame you because I watch a lot of media too and I've been part of it for 35 years. We are grateful that you're here. Thank you for doing this.\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So we're 34 days away from an election, it is -- I've covered politics my whole life -- it is a long, hard, tough, grueling process as you know. What's this process like for you?\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: As you said, it's a long process and you just need to be in it and enjoy it as much as you can, also you need to be very focused and take it day by day. Some surprises come as well. So, it is very important that you prepare for those surprises.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What's election day and election night like for you? I'm sure -- if I was on the ballot, I would imagine I'd probably be a wreck.\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: Well, as I explained in my book, I'm -- I'm very calm. That's maybe my personality and -- because I know on the Election Day, it's all in the people's hands.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: People decide what they want for this country and it will be again this year on November 5th.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. here we go again, your third run.\par \par \uc2 You know, one of the most interesting stories to me is when -- and I've known your husband for many years, long before he ever got into politics and then when he was thinking about it, we had a lot of late night conversations about issues and we would kind of go back and forth and debate. And what's so fascinating is that he was going up against 16 of the top governors and senators in our country and when he brought the issue to you that he was thinking of running, you're quoted as saying, well, you know, if you -- you run, you're going to win. True story?\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: True story.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How did you know?\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: I saw how people reacts to him and he's a passion for this country. And we travel all around the world, and he was making speeches at that time, and I saw what the people want.\par \par \uc2 And I think the country was ready for change. They wanted to have somebody who was not in politics all the time. And I saw it. I saw in him as well that he really wants to do it that time.\par \par \uc2 He was talking for many, many years but he really felt 2016 was the right time.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What if anything is different this time around?\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: I would think that the world and especially United States, it's more divided than ever before. We -- we are dealing with what much, much more danger and especially we see what's going on -- on the world and the threats that we get, and my husband -- what he went through in the last few months.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, I'm going to get to the issue of the assassination, and there are new threats as you know, and we'll talk about that. Let's talk about the divided country. How -- and you often talk about you want the country united, I like the country united. Some people wouldn't believe it, but I have very strong political beliefs about what the right thing to do is to get the country on the right track, putting politics aside.\par \par \uc2 How do you reconcile those that want open borders and those that want secure borders those that want high taxes and those that want tax cuts and free market economy? How do you reconcile those that want to defund and dismantle the police and those that believe in law and order? Or those that believe in energy independence and those that don't? Or those that believe in peace through strength and those that, for example, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  doesn't think we should use the words "radical Islamic terrorism"? How do you reconcile such differing views in your view and be united as you want like you talk about?\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: I think we need to listen each other. I think we need to have -- we have different perspectives. We have different beliefs. We -- we need to respect our freedom of speech, our individuality.\par \par \uc2 I think it's very important that ideas are heard that we have a very -- very straightforward communications and we share the idea with debate, because I think with that, we could have innovation and success in this country. I feel it's a troubling trade in this country that we are cancelling people that they don't agree on certain issues.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I want to talk to you about you've been a victim of cancel culture in ways that I never knew about, and I want to get to that too in the course of this interview. Politics though has gotten pretty rough and tumble and again having done this for three -- over three decades, look at what you and your family have had to go through. I covered the Russia -- as your -- as the president would say, the Russia hoax, Russia, Russia, Russia, right? Three years, it was all based on a lie, and it was debunked.\par \par \uc2 I watched him not through -- go through not one but two impeachments. We'll get to the assassination attempts. He has been through so much but so have you. And what stunned me is when you actually said that when they first impeached him, oh, I'm surprised it took so long. Wow, you were expecting it all?\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: I did because I saw how they treat -- treat him. How the media was against him. I think they are afraid of his strength and he was leading this country with peace through strength.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 M. TRUMP: So as soon he announced that he's running for the president, everything really changed and I saw it and I said, you know, this will not be very pleasant but I knew what he's in -- into it, what he will need to deal with.\par \par \uc2 And as soon he announced presidency and then when he won, they start already talking about the impeachment, the opposition newspaper had the front page story, impeachment is starting. So I always said to him, what is next?\par \par \uc2 So it's in one way, you're not surprised and every event that it happened, I'm thinking what is next? What they are trying to do? And you always feared the worst and that it happened.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, we have part two of my interview with Melania Trump, that's coming up tomorrow night. And by the way, you can get your copy of her new book. You go to MelaniaTrump.com.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, Sara Carter in the devastated area of Asheville, North Carolina, today, speaking with residents about the devastation, the lack of support and help from Kamala and Joe. We'll show you what they said. We'll get reaction from North Carolina Senator \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2 , and he said North Carolinians are frustrated, rightly so, about the federal government's non- response, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We now have over 180 people that are now dead in the horrific aftermath of Hurricane Helene, which flooded entire portions of western North Carolina, on top of all the damage in Florida, in Tennessee, in Georgia. And we saw in North Carolina, entire roads have been washed away, homes have been washed away, forcing people to cling to anything for dear life.\par \par \uc2 Our very own Sara Carter was in the Tar Heel State today. She spoke to local residents, many of them are mad, rightly so. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SARA CARTER, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Tell me what it was like?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It was -- it was actually pretty scary. I didn't really think it was going to be anything just like a normal storm or something, and all of a sudden, it just got crazy.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Well, after it got started then -- I mean, it was on the roofs, it covered a lot of the buildings like the building over there, it was on the rooftops.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The biggest thing is we were worried for family outside of the area that didn't know we were safe and not being able to let them know we were safe.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Any support that we needed here, you know, there's a lot of people that have absolutely nothing, have lost their families and stuff and -- I mean, you know, we need anything and everything that they you know are willing to do or give.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I got out immediately and I got out into the storm to see what was going on and I saw all that and we went in the other end of the house, and we've been living in the kitchen actually and sleeping on the floor in the kitchen since this happened and --\par \par \uc2 CARTER: Absolutely --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Thank God \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2  got here.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: What's been incredible to me is how the community has pulled together. \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2 , this \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2 , \uc2 Billy Graham\uc2 , this is your home.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, it is. \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2  is headquartered in Boone, North Carolina, and all of the staff live in the surrounding areas, the mountain towns, and so we're used to deploying supplies internationally, in different parts of the United States where disasters at this level are so common. For it to hit home made it much more personal, but the mission stays the same.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Finally, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  got off the beach and visited North Carolina today. He was briefed on the recovery effort in Raleigh after flying over some of the worst damage further west, which remember two days after Katrina, \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2  got vilified for. He continues to maintain that the federal government is doing all it can to support the victims, federal troops and helicopters finally now are being deployed to help the victims, it's nearly a week later.\par \par \uc2 According to North Carolina Senator \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2 , quote, every North Carolinian I have talked to is frustrated by the government's horrific response.\par \par \uc2 Now, thanks to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's good friend \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , thankfully, Starlink is finally available in impacted areas that have not had communications for over a week. Now, where was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  when the crisis began? On the beach. Where was \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ? In Hollywood, you know raising money from a friends there.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina Senator \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  is with us.\par \par \uc2 Senator, first, our condolences to the people of the great state of North Carolina. You know what's amazing to me, Senator, as I look at all of this and you say that you're frustrated and everybody you talk to is frustrated by the slow response, and then I look at, you know, you went on to say it's clear and has been clear from the beginning that federal resources were needed to access communities now.\par \par \uc2 But, first, \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2 , \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  calling \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and Starlink, you know, I don't know if there would have been any help at all and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  today's talking about climate change. How about we talk about saving lives, getting communication, water and supplies to people?\par \par \uc2 SEN. TED BUDD (R-NC): Sean, that just shows how out of touch he is. But before we get into that, and you don't -- this is not a time for political grandstanding. This is a time, first of all, to let the people of North Carolina know how much we love them, how much I love them, how much we're doing to work for them to bring --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Amen.\par \par \uc2 BUDD: -- as many resources as fast as we can, and absolutely.\par \par \uc2 So, I've been on the ground at Katrina. I was -- I was doing relief work at Hurricane Floyd 25 years ago. I've never seen anything like this. So, this is a 500 -- a thousand-year incident, we pray it never happens again.\par \par \uc2 But this -- these are resilient people in western North Carolina and yes, there are other states, too, and we pray for them as well. I'm talking to my colleagues in those other states and this is the worst disaster I have ever seen.\par \par \uc2 But God bless groups like Samaritan's purse, \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2 , his son Ed Graham, others that are stepping up bringing in the military discipline, and the speed and the generosity and serving in the name of Jesus to make things better for people in western North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 So I would say, let's reach out to these private groups. If people want to come and help, go through the \uc2 American Red Cross\uc2 , volunteer through \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2 , come through a -- go through a local church or organization, it's the private citizens that are stepping up right now.\par \par \uc2 I saw a group the other day, Operation Airdrop, private citizens with small airplanes. People who spent their life savings to make the dream come true and be able to fly a small helicopter, are risking themselves bringing their own personal equipment here and doing rescues and they're taking these Starlinks that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has generously donated. They're flying them into isolated volunteer -- volunteer fire departments that are connecting neighborhoods and communities that are otherwise cut off.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I'm -- I'm -- I'm not asking people to do something -- I myself did. I sent a donation to \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2 . It's samaritanspurse.org.\par \par \uc2 We'll continue to follow the story, Senator, and our prayers are with the people of North Carolina. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right. More "Hannity" straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left this evening. As always, thank you for being with us. Thank you for making this show possible.\par \par \uc2 Please set your DVR so you never, ever, ever, ever miss an episode of "Hannity". For news anytime, every time, all the time, Hannity.com and FOXNews.com.\par \par \uc2 But in the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Greg Gutfeld, he's next, to put a smile on your face. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020241003eka200001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 J.D. Vance Showed America He's Ready To Lead; J.D. Vance VP Pick Was Blasted By The Media; Post-Debate Loss, Democrats Run Back To January 6 Lawfare; Chutkan And Smith Desperate To Influence Election; Biden-Harris Administration Ignoring Major Crises; More Pain On The Way To U.S. Consumers; Democrats And Their Media Allies Clean Up For Walz; Montana Election Could Decide Fate Of The Senate\b0\par\par\uc2 Harris Faulkner, Bret Baier, Laura Ingraham, Charlie Hurt, Raymond  Arroyo \par \uc2 7,899 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 HARRIS FAULKNER, THE FAULKNER FOCUS ANCHOR: Right on abortion and I thought for sure that that would be an area that he would fight, I thought that J.D. Vance did a good job of being transparent, that there needs to be growth within the GOP party, among women and family and so on and so forth.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: Great to have you guys.\par \par \uc2 FAULKNER: Thanks for having us.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Fair, balanced, and unafraid. Laura's up next.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. It's great to have you with us. Another desperate move by desperate people. Judge Chutkan unseals a motion, and the libs go absolutely nuts. It's more proof that the DOJ has been weaponized. We're going to expose it all in moments. But first, the right man for the job. That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 Just as we saw during COVID, the people who are called experts are often wrong. Cloth masks work, social distancing, it's based in science, the vaccine that stops infection and transmission. Well, they couldn't have been more wrong. Then after January 6th, they were confident that Trump was finished.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Do Democrats have the votes to mark the end of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's political career?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: That could mean the definitive end of his political career.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Trial alone, even without a conviction, will be enough to end \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's political career.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And now in their assessment of J.D. Vance as his VP pick, they were again spectacularly wrong.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: J.D. Vance here, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's running mate, having some people wondering whether he should be replaced.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This J.D. Vance parade is not going to move on. I don't know if Vance is here in the end, we'll see.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Yes, it's hard for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to make -- admit making a mistake, but certainly a lot of Republicans very unhappy right now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And the anti-populist Republicans also embarrassed themselves anonymously telling the Hill that Vance's selection by Trump was the worst choice of all the options, so bad, he didn't even think it was possible one congressman said. Another Republican said, nine out of 10 on our side would say Trump's wrong on the J.D. pick. My personal favorite from this June story was another congressman claiming that Vance is the only person who could do serious damage to Trump.\par \par \uc2 But they were even preemptively blaming Vance if Trump fell short in November, what else? Well, who fell short last night? Not this guy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R-OH), 2024 VICE PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I knew a lot of young women who had unplanned pregnancies and decided to terminate those pregnancies because they feel like they didn't have any other options. One of them is actually very dear to me. She told me something a couple years ago that she felt like if she hadn't had that abortion, that it would have destroyed her life because she was in an abusive relationship.\par \par \uc2 I want us as a Republican Party to be pro-family in the fullest sense of the word. I want us to support fertility treatments. I want us to make it easier for moms to afford to have babies.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: From beginning to end, Vance not only showed his mastery of the issues, but his artful ability to navigate the smug bias of those \uc2 CBS\uc2  moderators, that was perhaps the most impressive thing of all last night. I thought -- I think that one of J.D.'s best moments was his debunking of the Biden-Harris claim that they're letting in migrants under just a normal legal process.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Thank you, Senator. We have so much to get to.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Margaret, I think it's important because --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We're going to turn now to the economy.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Margaret, the rules were that you guys wouldn't do a fact check, and since you're fact checking me, I think it's important to say what's actually going on. So there's an application called the CBP One app where you can go on as an illegal migrant, apply for asylum or apply for parole and be granted legal status at the wave of a \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  open border wand.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: 100 percent right then they mute the mic. Literally, the only way \uc2 CBS\uc2  could save face was to cut his mic. It's pathetic. Now maybe do this next time. Maybe listen and learn something. Then maybe you'll finally understand Trump's growing working class appeal. Try that on for size.\par \par \uc2 But again, I think that's expecting too much of these people who apparently don't have much contact with the real world, because outside the Beltway corridor, Vance has been connecting, and not just intellectually, but on a human level.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He's very battle tested, very ready, and you can just see that he went to Yale, and he's very intelligent, and he reassured a lot of people, I think.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Somebody else needs strong control of the facts, he ran the show.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He remained steady during the whole performance, and I was very impressed with him being very sincere and authentic.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He humanized himself, and actually looked like a regular guy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, if it were a fight last night, some boxing match, the ref would have called it for Vance early on. But perhaps the most important takeaway from the VP showdown is how Trump's judgment in picking him in the first place was totally vindicated.\par \par \uc2 Now let's be clear, no one but Trump would have picked Vance, who was most definitely not the choice of the Senate leadership, even though, when pressed by a Huffington Post reporter at the DNC, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  did call Vance a great choice. Well, I don't say this too often, but Senator McConnell was right now, but this was a hard choice. It was controversial. It was a controversial decision at the time, but Trump was willing to take the slings and arrows in order to name Vance as his number two, because it was someone who actually believed in the America first agenda, and Trump understood that Vance could persuasively advocate for it and then defend Trump's record before a hostile press.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Honestly. Tim, I think you got a tough job here, because you've got to play whack a mole. You've got to pretend that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  didn't deliver rising take home pay, which, of course he did. You've got to pretend that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  didn't 