ston\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 BROOKE TAYLOR, FOX NEWS CHANNEL NATIONAL NEWS CORRESPONDENT (voice over): With negotiations stalled, dock workers are not letting up on the picket line.\par \par \uc2 AMERICAN CROWD: Make the deal! Make the deal!\par \par \uc2 TAYLOR (voice over): The port strike is costing the economy up to $4.5 billion a day, according to economists. 36 major U.S. ports stretching from Maine to Texas are currently shut down. And because of this, many of the cargo ships that usually deliver goods to East Coast and Gulf Coast ports are now stuck offshore.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Association of Wholesaler-Distributors\uc2 , along with 300 other trade groups, are calling on President Biden to take action.\par \par \uc2 ERIC HOPLIN, PRESIDENT, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION OF WHOLESALER-DISTRIBUTORS: He's got the authority to shut down this strike, and we think he needs to do that.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Mr. President!\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Mr. President!\par \par \uc2 TAYLOR: While President Biden still refuses to do so, he had this to say today.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: It's time for them to sit at the table and get this strike done.\par \par \uc2 TAYLOR (voice over): The union has two major demands; a 77 percent wage increase over six years, along with a ban on automation.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. maritime alliance group made an offer, including a 50 percent wage increase, claiming it exceeds every other recent union settlement.\par \par \uc2 But the ILA rejected it.\par \par \uc2 JACK DACOSTA, JR., STRIKE CAPTAIN, INTERNATIONAL LONGSHOREMEN ASSOCIATION: We worked tirelessly through this pandemic. We had to come to work to get paid. Everybody else stayed home while they got paid.\par \par \uc2 TAYLOR (voice over): On average, ILA union members start with about an $81,000 annual salary, but can pull in over $200,000 annually with overtime.\par \par \uc2 DAVID HELLERMAN,