th actor Matthew Perry's death has pleaded guilty to conspire to contribute -- distribute ketamine. Prosecutors offered lesser charges to Dr. Mark Chavez and two others who have admitted guilt in this case, in exchange for their cooperation and going after two targets they deem more responsible for Perry's death.\par \par \uc2 Fox 46 in Charlotte, North Carolina, two NASCAR teams, including one owned by Michael Jordan, have filed a lawsuit over NASCAR's new revenue sharing model, 2311 Racing and Front Row Motorsports say the new charter system limits competition, but unfairly binding teams by unfairly binding teams to the series its tracks and suppliers.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at Las Vegas from Fox 5, the sphere right there, one of the big stories there tonight. The Las Vegas Space Port begins the licensing process in an effort to build a launch site for space planes. Company officials say they are working with Space Force leaders to try to build this new age facility. That's tonight's live look outside the Beltway from Special Report. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: A massive blast heard in the last few hours inside Beirut city. Witnesses can see smoke rising from the buildings. Security sources there say the strike hit within the city limits, not far from downtown.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DANNY DANON\uc2 , ISRAELI AMBASSADOR TO U.N.: Israel will not stand by in the face of such aggression. Israel will respond. Our response will be decisive, and yes, it will be painful.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Would you support an attack on Iran's nuclear sites by Israel?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: The answer is no.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: For analysis on the situation in the Middle East and what may come next, let's bring in Fox News senior strategic analyst, retired General Jack Keane. General, thanks for being here. What's your 