 border consistently ranks as one of the top issues for American voters.\par \par \uc2 Senator Vance, your campaign is pledging to carry out the largest mass deportation plan in American history, and to use the U.S. military to do so. Could you be more specific about exactly how this will work?\par \par \uc2 For example, would you deport parents who have entered the U.S. illegally and separate them from any of their children who were born on U.S. soil? You have two minutes.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: So, first of all, Margaret, before we talk about deportations, we have to stop the bleeding.\par \par \uc2 We have a historic immigration crisis because \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  started and said that she wanted to undo all of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's border policies, 94 executive orders, suspending deportations, decriminalizing illegal aliens, massively increasing the asylum fraud that exists in our system.\par \par \uc2 That has opened the floodgates. And what it's meant is that a lot of fentanyl is coming into our country. I had a mother who struggled with opioid addiction and has gotten clean. I don't want people who are struggling with addiction to be deprived of their second chance because \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  let in fentanyl into our communities at record levels.\par \par \uc2 So you have got to stop the bleeding. You have got to reimplement \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's border policies, build the wall, reimplement deportations.\par \par \uc2 And that gets me to your point, Margaret, about, what do we actually do? So we have got 20, 25 million illegal aliens who are here in the country. What do we do with them? I think the first thing that we do is we start with the criminal migrants.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: About a million of those people have committed some form of crime, in addition to crossing the border illegally. I think you start with deportations on those folks. And then I think you make it harder for illegal aliens to undercut the wages of American workers. A lot of 