hio, we had a referendum in 2023, and the people of Ohio voted overwhelmingly, by the way, against my position.\par \par \uc2 And I think that what I learned from that, Norah, is that we have got to do a better job at winning back people's trust. So many young women would love to have families. So many young women also see an unplanned pregnancy as something that's going to destroy their livelihood, destroy their education, destroy their relationships.\par \par \uc2 And we have got to earn people's trust back. And that's why \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I are committed to pursuing pro-family policies, making childcare more accessible, making fertility treatments more accessible, because we have got to do a better job at that. And that's what real leadership is.\par \par \uc2 O'DONNELL: Governor, your response?\par \par \uc2 WALZ: Well, I'm going to respond on the pro-abortion piece of that.\par \par \uc2 No, we're not. We're pro-women. We're pro freedom to make your own choice. We know what the implications are to not be that, women having miscarriages, women not getting the care, physicians feeling like they may be prosecuted for providing that care.\par \par \uc2 And as far as making sure that we're educating our children and giving them options, Minnesota's a state with one of the lowest teen pregnancy rates. We understand that too. We know that the options need to be available. And we make that true.\par \par \uc2 We also make it -- we're a top three state for the best place to raise children. But these two things -- to try and say that we're pro-children, but we don't like this, or you guys are pro-abortion, that's not the case at all. We are pro freedoms for women to make their choices.\par \par \uc2 And we're going and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is making the case to make options for children more affordable, a $6,000 child tax credit. But we're not going to base that on the backs of making someone like Amber Thurman drive 600 miles to try and get health care.\par \par \uc2 O'DONNELL: Senator?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: May I respond to that?\par \par \uc2 First of all, Governor, I agree with you. Amber Thurman should still be alive, and there are a lot of people who should still be alive. And I certainly wish that she was.\par \par \uc2 And maybe -- you're free to disagree with me on this and explain this to me, but as I read the Minnesota law that you signed into -- into -- into law, the statute that you signed into law, it says that a doctor who presides over an abortion where the baby survives, the doctor is under no obligation to provide lifesaving care to a baby who survives a botched late-term abortion.\par \par \uc2 That is, I think...\par \par \uc2 WALZ: That's not true. That's not how the law is.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Whether you're pro-choice or pro-abortion, that is fundamentally barbaric.\par \par \uc2 And that's why I use that word, Norah, is because some of what we have seen -- do you want to force Catholic hospitals to perform abortions against their will? Because \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has supported suing Catholic nuns to violate their freedom of conscience.\par \par \uc2 We can be a big and diverse country, where we respect people's freedom of conscience and make the country more pro-baby and pro-family, but please.\par \par \uc2 O'DONNELL: Yes, Governor, please respond.\par \par \uc2 WALZ: Look, this is one where there's always something there. This is a very simple proposition.\par \par \uc2 These are women's decisions to make about their health care decisions and the physicians who know best when they need to do this. Trying to distort the way a law is written to try and make a point, that's not it at all.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: What was I wrong about, Governor?\par \par \uc2 WALZ: This would...\par \par \uc2 VANCE: I -- please tell me, what was I wrong about?\par \par \uc2 WALZ: That is not the way the law is written.\par \par \uc2 Look, I have given...\par \par \uc2 VANCE: But how?\par \par \uc2 WALZ: I have given this advice on a lot of things, that getting involved, getting against -- that's been misread. And it was fact-checked at the last debate.\par \par \uc2 But the point on this is, there's a continuation of these guys to try and tell women or to get involved. I use this line on this, just mind your own business on this. Things worked best when Roe v. Wade was in place. When we do a restoration of Roe, that works best. That doesn't preclude us from increasing funding for children.\par \par \uc2 It doesn't increase us from making sure that once that child is born, like in Minnesota, they get meals, they get early childhood education, they get health care. So that -- hiding behind, we're going to do all these other things, when you're not proposing them in your budget -- \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is proposing them. She's proposing all those things to make life easier for families.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: I asked a specific question, Governor. You gave me a slogan as a response.\par \par \uc2 WALZ: It's not the case. It's not true. That's not what the law says.\par \par \uc2 So, they fact-checked it with President Trump.\par \par \uc2 O'DONNELL: Gentlemen, there's a lot to discuss. We have to move on.\par \par \uc2 And we're going to be right back with much more of the CBS News vice presidential debate in just a moment.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [21:58:44]\par \par \uc2 O'DONNELL: Welcome back to the CBS News vice presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 We want to turn now to America's gun violence epidemic. The leading cause of death for children and teens in America is by firearms.\par \par \uc2 Senator Vance, you oppose most gun legislation that Democrats claim would curb gun violence. You oppose red flag gun laws and legislation to ban certain semi-automatic rifles, including AR-15s.\par \par \uc2 So let me ask you -- earlier this year, for the first time, the parents of a school shooter were convicted of involuntary manslaughter and sentenced to 10 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Do you think holding parents responsible could curb mass shootings?\par \par \uc2 I'll give you two minutes.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Yeah. Well, Norah, on that particular case, I don't know the full details. But I certainly trust local law enforcement and local authorities to make those decisions.\par \par \uc2 I think in some cases, the answer is going to be yes, and in some cases, the answer is going to be no, and the details really matter here, of course.\par \par \uc2 For example, if a kid steals a gun, that's going to be different than if a parent hands over a gun, knowing that their kid is potentially dangerous.\par \par \uc2 Look, I -- I want to just sort of speak as a father of three beautiful little kids, and our oldest is now in second grade. And like a lot of parents, we send our kids to school with such hope and such joy.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FXLV000020241002eka10002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 J.D. Vance To Grill \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  On Web Of Lies During Debate; \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  Surrendered His State To Radical Progressives; Biden-Harris Administration Ignoring Major Crises; Biden-Harris Administration Ignoring Major Crises; Americans Feel Abandoned By Biden And Harris; Iran Launches Ballistic Missile Attack On Israel; Biden Yet To Speak With Netanyahu; Panel Weighs In As Vance And Walz Face Off In V.P. Debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Laura Ingraham, Jacqui Heinrich, Aishah Hasnie,  Jeanine Pirro, Mike Tobin, Byron York, Mollie Hemingway \par \uc2 8,081 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: Remember, if you can't catch us live, set your DVR 6:00 PM in the East, 3:00 PM on the West Coast. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight and every night. That's is for this Special Report. Fair, balanced and still unafraid. Remember, special debate coverage tonight, and The Ingraham Angle starts next. I want to keep talking here.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from New York City tonight. My Angle in moments. But first, in just two hours, you'll see what will likely be the final debate of this long election season.\par \par \uc2 J.D. Vance versus \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . It comes on a day of chaos around the globe and more suffering here at home, with two major crises unfolding, a port strike that could end up costing the U.S. about $5 billion a day, and the human tragedy and infrastructure collapse from one of the deadliest hurricanes in American history. Now the death toll has stood now, I think it's at about 159 people. Tragic entire communities flattened. Americans are still struggling to get the basic necessities like water.\par \par \uc2 And overseas, a significant escalation, Iran retaliated against Israel's successful decapitation of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 's leadership and launched at least 180 missiles into Israel, lighting up the sky. Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  warning Iran that it will learn a painful lesson. We attack back.\par \par \uc2 Now, Americans are watching all this, and they're wondering who is really running the country tonight. After all, you know, they dumped Joe from the ticket because he presumably was not up to the task. But the vice presidential debate, which you can watch live right here on Fox News, will tell us a lot about the future, how either of these administrations could perhaps handle the next crisis.\par \par \uc2 Let's go live now to the debate site where Fox News Senior White House Correspondent Jacqui Heinrich is standing by. Jacqui, do we have any indication of how \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  prepped for tonight?\par \par \uc2 JACQUI HEINRICH, FOX NEWS WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Well, Laura, all we really know is Transportation Secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  has been standing in for J.D. Vance and Walz's debate prep, and despite more help from two aides who also prepared the Vice President for her debate, Walz is reportedly nervous, scared he'll disappoint Harris, and even warned her that he's a bad debater. Now, it could be a standard play to try to lower expectations, but one Democrat from his state lent some credence to this, saying that Walz can be very, that's it, I'm done. So, his temperament will certainly be under the microscope tonight.\par \par \uc2 The campaign has really kept Walz out of the media circuit since joining the ticket, except for one joint interview with Vice President Harris, where he squirmed under questions about misrepresenting his military record. Today, the campaign ducked new questions about Walz's fudging the details on the time he spent in China, and he's faced no questions about controversial bills he signed as Minnesota's governor, like granting driver's licenses to illegal immigrants and making Minnesota a sanctuary state for children seeking transgender surgeries.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the goal is to put Trump in the room