he do this? Well, because most normal people would think it's really odd for a candidate for the vice presidency to feel so close, so connected with Communist China. Of course, it's a brutal dictatorship that persecutes religious minorities and dissidents, no biggie. And now, Congressman \uc2 Jim Comer\uc2  is telling us that whistleblowers are coming forward to reveal more about their true nature of these trips, very disturbing. And that's not all we're learning about. Another Walz lie courtesy of the Washington Free Beacon, now always trying to burnish his resume. Don't you love people like that?\par \par \uc2 Walz had claimed over the years to have been in China during the Tiananmen massacre in 1989.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WALZ: I was in Hong Kong on June 4, 1989, when, of course, Tiananmen Square happened. An opportunity to be in a Chinese High School at that critical time seemed to me to be really important, and it was a very interesting summer, to say the least.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But the truth is, he was in Nebraska, where apparently it wasn't as interesting. Now, of course, there's another reason why they wouldn't let him do interviews. This is just obvious and why he avoids reporters like the plague. The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reported that he's a surprisingly bubble wrapped campaigner. It's not surprising at all.\par \par \uc2 The Harris people know he's a huge negative and because apparently no one knows how to vet VP contenders, they can't let him do interviews because his background is so shady, thus all they can do leading up to this debate is lower expectations, and it's been something to behold.\par \par \uc2 First, Walz supposedly let it be known that he was nervous about the Vance matchup, just what you want in the VP, and now he -- all of his friends at Axios are claiming that some Democrats are in a state of panic about how Walz will perform tonight. They note that Walz has a tendency to get heated when attacked and to ramble and trip himself up in unscripted settings. Sounds like Kamala.\par \par \uc2 Well, any of this it's not news. He's a liberal blowhard who rolls over for the Far-Left, and really hates being questioned.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: What's your reaction to the six hostage being found in Gaza?\par \par \uc2 WALZ: Right. Thanks, everybody.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Thanks, everybody. Have a vanilla malt. Now, what everyone needs to keep in mind tonight is that it's highly unlikely that the \uc2 CBS\uc2  moderators will challenge Walz on any of the tough questions and go around the edges a little bit. But I have a belief that they'll probably work to protect him every chance they get. If the past is prolog, they will let him ramble on about all the good folks that he's had the chance to meet along the way, and how Washington needs a little Minnesota nice.\par \par \uc2 He'll attack J.D. Vance, who came from nothing, of course, attack him as anti-women, anti-female elitist. And after it's all over tonight, \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 , \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  and other media outlets will all declare that \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  won because he was more relatable.\par \par \uc2 But at a time of crisis at home and abroad, we need a vice president whose judgment and intellect is exceptional. We're not voting for an assistant coach or best buddy or a high school history teacher as wonderful as all those positions are. We're voting for the candidate whom we can trust to be able to step in if something should happen to the president. And do we really want this man to be a heartbeat away from the nuclear codes.\par \par \uc2 In Minnesota, he bowed to almost every demand. He supported almost every Left-wing agenda item. And as VP, yes, he would do the same. From letting a city burn in the summer of 2020 and calling in the National Guard too late, to supporting a so-called trans refuge law that gives the state the right to nullify parental rights, allowing abortions of babies through the ninth month of pregnancy and refusing infants medical care, if they're born alive after an abortion attempt. Of course, signing legislation to not only give illegal immigrants the right to get driver's licenses, but also free college tuition.\par \par \uc2 But in the end, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  always focuses on making one group, the Far-Left, very happy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: My pronouns are she her. I represent District 66A in the Minnesota House of Representatives, and I'm the Chief House Author of House File 146. Trans refuge law, which is being signed into law today by Governor Walz.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, don't be fooled by the aw-shucks demeanor, because Walz is an extremist. Is there any daylight between him and \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , the Congresswoman from his home state? If there is, I don't see it, maybe he'll show us some daylight tonight.\par \par \uc2 Remember, the purpose of these debates isn't to highlight substantive differences between the candidates or to give equally tough questions to both sides. Debates today, sadly, are simply another opportunity for the media to proclaim how great the Democrats are.\par \par \uc2 Well, as for Vance, well, he should be ready, because he's been tangling with the hostile press for years now, especially since he got the nod from Trump.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. J.D. VANCE (R-OH), 2024 VICE PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: It very often is how the process works, Margaret --\par \par \uc2 MARGARET BRENNAN, \uc2 CBS\uc2  NEWS ANCHOR: It is not.\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Biden Administration has been scandalous in not properly vetting these people. Absolutely done this stuff. It's not crazy. John, come on. You should not be able to take people's children away from them --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And that's not what he proposed --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: If you disagree with decisions about gender reassignment. Yes, he has proposed that, John.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He knows they're going to pummel him with questions about his statements about Haitian food choices, and he knows that they're going to spend more time on abortion and January 6th than they will on China or immigration. And the Angle suspects that Vance, without being arrogant, will methodically answer each question and then turn the tables on both Walz and the moderators.\par \par \uc2 But the fundamental question remains for voters tonight, are you happy with the way things are going, with the cost of food, the cost of gas, with the explosion of migrants, the handling of crises, foreign and domestic? Because there's no indication that either Walz or Harris will be any more competent than Biden and Harris. They'll probably be worse in effect, and all the bubble wrap in the world won't insulate us from the pain that will follow. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 All right, up next, the Biden-Harris administration refusing to intervene and another completely avoidable disaster.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's failure, as far as America can see with Biden and Harris at the helm or pretending to be. As if our economy wasn't already on the edge. Now, dock workers at 36 ports across America, the East Coast, Gulf of Mexico, are now on strike. Now, a president fully engaged using the bully pulpit to get all parties to the table would have had at least some chance at averting this strike.\par \par \uc2 But of course, that's not what happened here. And if this keeps going, we could see supply chain issues and even more price hikes for American families. So, where is the administration on this?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Where are the issues most prominent? Where have you been kind of focused and hearing on what would happen if the strike goes, let's say longer than a week?\par \par \uc2 GINA RAIMONDO\uc2 , COMMERCE SECRETARY: Again, I have not been very focused on that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, why on earth would our Commerce Secretary be focused on a strike that could cripple commerce? Now this is just an unserious bunch at a very serious time for the United States, unless you think it was more important for our Secretary of Transportation to do debate prep with \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  when a hurricane was threatening our transportation sector.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Judge Jeanine Pirro, co-host of The Five. Judge, six days ago, Reuters reported that the White House was monitoring the port talks and considering the effects of a strike. They do a lot of monitoring.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, THE FIVE CO-HOST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And they do a lot of considering. They did that before the hurricane. But that -- the job doesn't require monitoring; it requires using that bully pulpit and the power of the presidency.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, there's no question, this campaign, everything about what we're seeing now, and this is like an October surprise, is about a lack of leadership. It's about a lack of initiative. It's about recognizing what's going to happen. Everybody knew when this contract was up. Everybody knew in June that that was the last discussion anybody had, whether it's the secretary of commerce or the secretary of labor.\par \par \uc2 The truth is, \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2  is the one who said after two assassination attempts on Trump, she said Trump needs to be eliminated. She's the one who said, oh, no, we didn't lose 800,000 jobs. Yes, you did.\par \par \uc2 I mean, she's not keyed into the job. You've got to prepare. You've got to know what's going to happen. This is going to cost the American people a lot of money. These are the holidays. And this is how --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They don't care.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: -- you bring them both together. You've got people in a flood. I lost my house in a flood when I was a kid. My family, our house went away.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You know what that's like.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: They need canned goods. Eighty-five percent of the canned goods come through the longshoremen, OK? Now we're not going to get those. Eighty-five percent of canned goods. These people cannot predict a problem and deal with it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: NBC reported yesterday, for everyone criticizing, anyone criticizing the administration's response. I guess NBC's in on the conspiracy because they reported that over in North Carolina, Buncombe County manager Averill Pinder said, we requested water even before the storm started because we felt that some people were going to be cut off because of how much rain was coming.\par \par \uc2 But despite the advance request, Pinder said Buncombe County received its first shipment of water at 2:30 A.M. yesterday.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No surprise.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Judge.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: This is an administration that only reacts, and you've got to hope that they react in time. You get water -- the storm makes landfall on Thursday night, they get water today? I mean, that's crazy. We've got helicopters, supposedly, we've got all ways of transporting.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, they had to have private helicopters got involved because they couldn't get enough government personnel. They have 3,000 people there now.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But the point is, you can't predict everything about a hurricane.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Oh, by again.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Given how devastating the path looked, you can't just dump stuff at the Big Bend area of Florida and some in Georgia. You've got to have some provisions on the ground ready for the people, ready to deploy to the people right away.\par \par \uc2 She didn't go to the hurricane briefings annually, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . We learned that tonight.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That didn't happen. Again, why do that when you can spend time just traveling around the country doing whatever they're doing?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Or doing a podcast about legalizing weed when you put 2,000 people in jail for smoking weed. I mean, the truth is that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is not focused. These people are not serious. And the sad part about all this is that Americans are suffering.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wanted to solve the longshoremen, he could bring in the Taff Hartley Act.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He said he's not doing it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Of course he's not doing it. He wants the labor support.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, imagine if this went down in the last year of the Trump administration. What do you think the media -- do you think they would say, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  engaged in monitoring the talks.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Do you think they would slaughter him, metaphorically, for not doing more.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, but the good news is, in the four years, if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becomes president, everything is going to be taken care of. It's like the baby formula. They were shutting down baby formula factories and then saying, gee, I didn't know. Is there a shortage of baby formula? Only in the stores.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I forgot about that. There's been so many things that have happened. I forgot about that baby --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And by the way, not at the border. There was no shortage at the border of the formula.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I want to play this. Biden says he's in constant contact with the key players over in the Middle East. Obviously, another crisis brewing there. Let's watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Do you think the government is doing enough?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Honestly, I don't know how you did not have a formal -- a formal press conference or something from either President Biden or \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . I mean, how do you not say anything for four days? They've been stranded for four days and this is the first we've heard from them at all. FEMA is not on the ground there.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I guess she's in on the conspiracy, too. Obviously, that's not the Middle East clip, but I'm glad we played that because, again, the people are suffering. She's not a right-wing pundit. That's a woman in need. And people in need in the Middle East now too, and people are very afraid of what's going to happen next there.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yeah, they are afraid. And what is the first thing that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says last night after they take down Nasrallah and all the pages of walkie talkies? Cease fire now. It's the same thing he said on October 8th, but you know, we're going to assist Israel in its defense. Maybe you ought to just stay back, let Israel fight the fight, because they can do it and they can win.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm never using a pager again, are you? Do you have any old pagers? Do you ever use pagers, Judge?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No. You know, I had one when I was married. I should have kept that.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You get a lot for that these days. They actually don't blow up. All right, Judge, great to see you, as always. All right, Iran escalates its assault on Israel, as the judge was just saying, while Biden and Harris too busy staging photo ops. Next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: More instability, more chaos, and another crisis unfolding under Biden and Harris's watch. Now imagine blowing through more than 180 missiles intended for your target to basically no effect.\par \par \uc2 Fox News international correspondent Mike Tobin is live from Haifa, Israel. Mike, you spent so many years reporting from there. Remember, I saw you back in 2006 in 