rail. They had at least one M16 style weapon with them and a knife. Six, seven people were killed, several injured. The attackers themselves were killed.\par \par \uc2 And in the middle of all that tension, Israel has been sending messages into South Beirut, the South Beirut suburbs, warning people to get out, and that's something they do before new airstrikes go in. Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Mike, thanks so much. Joining me now is Nathan Sales, former ambassador at large and coordinator for counter-terror under President Trump. Nathan, good to see you. Now your old boss spoke today about these strikes. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT, 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I've been talking about World War III for a long time and I don't want to make predictions because the predictions always come true. I not going to make, but they are very close to global catastrophe. We have a non-existent president and a non-existent vice president.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Nathan, the situation around the United States with a hurricane suffering and now we see more concern about what's unfolding in the Middle East. Is President Trump, right? Are we on the verge without strong American leadership of a catastrophe in the Middle East?\par \par \uc2 NATHAN SALES, FORMER COUNTERTERRORISM COORDINATOR: Well, Laura, thanks for having me on. The world is on fire, and the only way to put it out is for America to assert leadership. That's how you have peace, peace through strength. You know, President Biden keeps telling Iran, don't, and the Iranians keep ignoring him.\par \par \uc2 This is the second time in six months that the Iranians have felt emboldened enough to launch a direct attack on Israel. And Israel can't afford for that to become the new normal nor can the United States afford for that to become the new normal.\par \par \uc2 What we need to do is bloody Iran's nose. We just hit him in the nose and that way we can avoid a much bigger fight further down the road. It's all about restoring deterrence. Once you lose deterrence, as we have under President Biden and Vice President Harris's watch, it's really, really hard to get it back.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, President Biden addressed the issue of an Israeli response to today's missile barrage. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: That's an active discussion right now. We've got to get all the data straight. We've been in constant contact with the Israeli government and our counterparts, and that remains to be seen.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: What is your message to Prime Minister Netanyahu, and have you spoken with him today?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I haven't spoken with him. We have spoken with all his people, and I'll be talking to him, and my message will depend on what we finally conclude is needed.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Nathan, I'm not an expert in foreign diplomacy and these kinds of issues, but he says he is in constant contact with Israeli government officials. But you haven't spoken to Netanyahu? What is that all about?\par \par \uc2 SALES: Yes, not exactly a message that's calculated to strike fear in the heart of the supreme leader, is that, I mean, we're going to talk and we're going to look at the data. This isn't hard. One, we support Israel's right to defend itself against genocidal terrorist regimes like the Islamic Republic of Iran. Two, we're going to make you pay a price. We said don't. We said there's going to be severe consequences.\par \par \uc2 Now it's time to match the actions to the words, because if you don't, if you threaten, if you cry wolf and then don't deliver, the Iranians are going to think, you know what? We can get away with murder, literally.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, right now, Nathan, Americans are very worried tonight. They don't see an active engaged president. He shows up in the Oval, I know he's in the situation room, but everyone knows what it looks like when we have a commander in chief who's truly there and engaged, and that is not what we see tonight in the United States. And I'm sad to say that, but that is not what we see. Nathan, thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right, what to expect from tonight's big face-off between J.D. Vance and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . We'll get into it next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We're a little over an hour away from J.D. Vance and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  squaring off on that V.P. debate. We got some new video of Walz arriving earlier, waving and his spirit fingers to all of his adoring fans in the press.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Fox News contributor Byron York, Mollie Hemingway, alongside content creator Anton Daniels, Minnesota radio host Jon Justice. This is quite the panoply we have tonight. Byron, you're stuck here with me in New York. What are your predictions tonight?\par \par \uc2 BYRON YORK, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, I think J.D. Vance has to do a couple of things. First of all, as much as \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  wants to talk about himself as a coach or a teacher, he's been the governor of Minnesota during some really bad times, specifically the George Floyd riots. Kind of sat by while a lot of Minneapolis was destroyed. And then the COVID lockdowns as well. So, remind people of that, and then tie it all to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, I do think that Walz is going to take everything that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has ever said that Democrats didn't like and try to tie it all to J.D. Vance.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Mollie, I expect that things like January 6 and Charlottesville, all of that will get another airing tonight, as it did in the previous debate. What do you think J.D. Vance's biggest hurdle is tonight?\par \par \uc2 MOLLIE HEMINGWAY, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, you're right to expect that, because corporate media, frequently in these debates, it's not really about finding answers to important questions or seeing who people are, so much as pushing narratives. Now, I do think that will be the biggest barrier for J.D. Vance, is dealing with not just his Democrat opponent on the stage, but also the two opponents who will be the moderators.\par \par \uc2 He does seem to excel in this though. He's very good at questioning the assumptions put forth by left-wing media and articulating a coherent policy position. He might be one of the more effective people at that, so it should not be too much of a hurdle.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, they're the game of lowering expectations, Anton. It seems like they really want everyone to think that \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  basically can't even walk to the stage for the debate because he's so inept. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: They're actively trying to lower expectations for Walz. Vance is very good at this. And he was chosen for that. Walz was chosen for that affability, that warmth. And the question is, you know, is it going to be a Labrador Retriever versus a Coyote?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. Anton, I guess they're saying that the Labrador is \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . I had two labs. I love them dearly. But right now, we need leadership and clear into leadership.\par \par \uc2 ANTON DANIELS, YOUTUBER AND CONTENT CREATOR: Yeah, I think that he's a reflection of his candidate, the running mate that he has, and that is very difficult to get them to go off a script. And so, what I'm trying to understand is, because I have no doubt in my mind that J.D. Vance is going to absolutely mop the floor with him, what I'm trying to understand is, is J.D. Vance going to push him to be accountable because you've never seen them actually be able to deal with a question that is completely off of whatever it is that somebody is pushing the narrative of.\par \par \uc2 So, for example, if he holds him accountable for how was he going to solve for a problem that they created in the immigration crisis, right? If he asked him a question about how it is that he would solve for inflation considering that the port workers are on strike and we've seen the Biden administration go and advocate with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  members, while at the same time they remain silent with this whole port worker crisis, which is much more impactful to the U.S. economy considering that \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has never held a private position nor has his running mate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . How would he respond to something like that?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He's not going to.\par \par \uc2 DANIELS: He's never been pushing that way. And I think that J.D. Vance is more suited to pushing --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. I don't mean to interrupt, but he will not be pressed on any of those specifics. I will be shocked if he is. I mean, I don't know if anyone else agrees that.\par \par \uc2 Jon Justice, look, you know \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  better than anyone else in Minnesota. Love your radio show there. Tell us about the real \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , given what has happened to Minnesota, a state I love so much. I've spent so much time over the years.\par \par \uc2 JON JUSTICE, RADIO HOST, TWIN CITIES NEWS TALK: Listen, Halloween comes early tonight, because the \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  on stage is not the real \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . It's a caricature. He's an elitist wannabe. He's a radical leftist who is masquerading as a moderate. He's a fake and a phony.\par \par \uc2 It's going to be up to J.D. Vance tonight to strip off that mask to show the country who the real \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is. He's faced almost no scrutiny here in the state of Minnesota, apart from his past runs as a governor. And even then, he's skipped debates before.\par \par \uc2 And so, they say he's nervous. I think that's to lower expectations, I agree. But if I were \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , I would be nervous because he actually has to face the questions, and hopefully J.D. Vance addresses those embellishments and lies that have been plaguing him this entire campaign with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, I think it's going to have to, it's up to J.D. Vance to do any of that tonight. But you think -- if you think people are going to get policy specifics from Walz, well, watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  needs to be \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . Talk about what they're going to do for America and the hope and the joy that \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  brings. I talk about my old football team that walked out on that stage at the DNC. That was a moment, folks.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 YORK: I think the joy moments, I think the weird moments --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Shock that he's no longer in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 YORK: Yeah, I think those are over. I think people actually do want to deal with these issues. I don't know how Walz is going to deal with this criticism, but I think that Vance will probably be pretty good. You know, all the things that Vance said, the criticisms that Vance said of Trump in 2015, right, said a lot, it's all on the record.\par \par \uc2 When Vance ran for the Senate, talked to somebody on his campaign, they said he had 75 town halls. And at every single one, he was asked that question. Why'd you say all those bad things about Trump, and now you like him? He's dealt with stuff, specifically about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , for many years.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Mollie, it looks like, right now, we have a kind of frozen election, right? If you like the status quo, you got to vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . With all that entails, the so-called joy, the abortions for people in Alabama, I guess they're worried about that. But other than that, if you like the status quo, vote for her. If you want to change, you've got to vote for Trump and Vance. In the end, that's what I think Vance has to say tonight.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: And it's something that we really haven't experienced in modern history, this side-by-side comparison of two administrations and their policies. It makes the job fairly easy for J.D. Vance to just talk about how things went during the Trump administration. It also makes it difficult for \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , since he's having to defend a very unpopular set of policies and a candidate who is having trouble expressing competency.\par \par \uc2 But ultimately for Americans, the vice-presidential debate only matters insofar as this referendum on, do you want the peace and the prosperity of the Trump era, or do you want the chaos. I mean, whether it's in North Carolina or globally at the border, at the docks, with the economy. It's not a fun night to be a Democrat candidate.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, chaos as far as the eye can see. Anton, quickly, minority voters watching this tonight. What's the outreach that J.D. Vance can make? Is it -- should it stay on the economy, stay on the border? Nuts and bolts issues.\par \par \uc2 DANIELS: No, I think that the thing is that people are paying attention to identity a lot more because we've seen the advancement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  being given to us and not necessarily having to debate her way out of a primary. But instead, they've seen the promotion of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And so, I think that the vice-presidential debate is more important than ever, because they're looking at these two candidates and seeing can they fit into the role and step into the role similarly to how \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was given to us if anything was to ever happen on that front.\par \par \uc2 So, I think that identity is playing a bigger role in a vice-presidential debate, as much more important thing today. And people are paying more attention than ever, especially in the social media era.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, well, Jon, I think that Walz is relatable. I mean, that's all you hear. He's so relatable, Coach Walz, you know, et cetera, et cetera. But right now, Americans are poorer than they were back in 2020, much poorer. And everything's more expensive, and there's more chaos. So, I don't care how relatable you are. That's not a good story to have to refute.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE: No, it's not. And again, he's a fake and a phony, and I think that the country is going to see that tonight. He's as much a danger to this country as he is an embarrassment to the state of Minnesota, the way that he's been acting out on the campaign trail. And it all comes off as bizarre and strange and weird, as he says, because none of it is genuine and authentic.\par \par \uc2 And I think the country is going to see that tonight. And I think J.D. Vance is going to be exposed that side of Walz. That's what I'm looking forward to seeing tonight.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: My big question is will he do that strange bowing motion? That isn't the oddest thing I've ever seen for an American candidate for national office. All right, panel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us tonight. Stay with Fox all night long for coverage. You can even watch the debate right here. Jesse Watters takes it from here. And I'll be on, later on, with the panel.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020241002eka100001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Trump Visits Georgia After Hurricane Helene\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Charlie Hurt, Joe Concha, Tammy Bruce \par \uc2 7,410 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 September 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And tonight, we are tracking multiple major stories both here at home and abroad. At this hour, we are monitoring southern Lebanon where Israel is now poised to expand operations against \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 . Now, this after obliterating -- I mean, obliterating the terrorist organization's entire command structure, including its 32-year terrorist leader \uc2 Hassan Nasrallah\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also tonight, we're going to get reaction to Kamala's idiotic, insulting photo-op trip to the southern border. Now, the mother of Rachel Morin, remember her? She was the mother of five, the mother of little 12-year-old Jocelyn Nungaray, they will join us tonight. And according to local authorities, their daughters were both brutally murdered by unvetted illegal aliens allowed into our country by your border czar, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But, first, our top story tonight, complete and total devastation from Hurricane Helene, across Florida, Georgia, Tennessee, North Carolina, Virginia, entire towns literally wiped out by flood waters, as the death toll continues to rise with hundreds, still missing tonight, and with roads and bridges wiped out, thousands still stranded, many without power, Internet, even the ability to communicate, many without clean tap water. This is by every measure a national emergency.\par \par \uc2 And today, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he flew to Valdosta, Georgia, to witness the devastation upfront and personal and firsthand and meet with disaster relief specialists from \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2  himself and \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2 . Let's take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT & 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Many thousands are without power. They're running low on food and fuel. We brought a lot of it down with us. It's going to be distributed now or soon throughout Georgia as well as North Carolina, South Carolina, Florida, Virginia, Alabama and Tennessee. Homes, hospitals, highways and cars have been plunged underwater, entire neighborhoods have been turned into lakes. Nobody's seen anything like it, and to every family that's been displaced here in Georgia and North Carolina, who's -- which has really been hit.\par \par \uc2 We're going there also, and they don't have communication. They don't have anything right now, that they're -- we're trying to -- I just spoke to Elon. I'm getting him -- I want -- we want to get Starlink hook up because they have no communication whatsoever. And Elon -- Elon will always come through, and we know that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, noticeably missing on the ground, the current president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Now, Kamala -- well, she spent the weekend on the West Coast where she attended a very glitzy fundraiser in Los Angeles with her Hollywood friends. What have I been saying?\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Party today is now a party of coastal elites. Hollywood, New York, D.C., Republicans are now the party of the hardworking men and women, the people that really make this country great, and, of course, Kamala did however, she did find the time to post a stage picture on X, at least pretending to care about the people in the Southeast.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , he spent all weekend at the beach in Delaware, you know, claiming to be on his phone but we know he was relaxing. They said in -- that Joe was on his phone a lot, managing the disaster recovery from afar. Well, that's, you know, hands on and compassionate. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: On the hurricane, Mr. President, why weren't you and Vice President Harris here in Washington commanding this -- this weekend?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I was commanding it. I was on the phone for at least two hours yesterday and the day before as well. I command to call a telephone, all my security people.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Is it not important for the country to see --\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Time for a "Hannity" history lesson. Let's go back to 2005, \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 , you might recall he was vilified. He was demonized. He was called a racist. Why? For flying over the devastation, he didn't want to get in the way of recovery efforts two days after Hurricane Katrina and looking down from Air Force One, two days.\par \par \uc2 Now, it's been nearly five days since what happened last week, two days after that hurricane made landfall, you might recall the hysteria and the name-calling and the blame that came his way. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LOUIS FARRAKHAN\uc2 , NATION OF ISLAM: I believe that we can charge the government with criminal neglect of the people of New Orleans, Louisiana, Mississippi and Louisiana in particular.\par \par \uc2 HILLARY CLINTON\uc2 , FORMER SECRETARY OF STATE: And if there were ever any evidence needed as to why we need a hands-on president, all we have to do is think back to what happen along the Gulf Coast. You know, that was an -- that was a natural disaster that was turned into a national disgrace. The incompetence, the indifference, the insensitivity.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I think the administration got embarrassed with the response that Hurricane Katrina. They were embarrassed.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And unacceptable here, sadly, leads to people dying and people being harmed. Hopefully, the president as we speak is in somewhere in Mississippi I guess right now, and the fact is that hopefully, he will - - you know, as I've many -- said many times, synchronize his conduct with his conscience.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We are now more than twice that time, four plus days after Helene touched down in Florida. And neither Biden nor Harris have bothered to even fly over the wreckage. Biden literally couldn't even come back from the beach at his beach house and his beach chair early. Harris, she was too busy living it up with her big money donors, you know, the \uc2 George Clooney\uc2  types, jackass that he is in Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 Well, where where's the same outrage from the media mob. And then to make matters worse, we're now just a few hours away from a devastating strike from, you know, the East Coast, and Gulf Coast, dockworkers, longshoremen, this could literally cripple all logistics in the entire country. And every single supply chain in America at a time when so many on the east coast in particular are trying to rebuild and recover from the devastation of this hurricane.\par \par \uc2 Think about this, last week, both Biden and Harris were so quick to step in front of a microphone and proudly announce $8 billion in new funding for Ukraine. All told, military, humanitarian aid, they've already given $175 billion of your dollars to Ukraine. Now, where are the billions and billions for North Carolina, Tennessee, Virginia, Georgia, Florida and any other state that needs help? Why are there no grand gestures for our fellow Americans in need?\par \par \uc2 And as per usual, both Biden and Harris are now being shamed into action. Biden will finally make a trip to the Southeast in coming days? Why? Because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did it. But no Trump -- no trip for Harris is planned as of now. I'm sure we will embarrass her into it although we haven't been able to embarrass her into doing a press conference.\par \par \uc2 So why does it always seem like the Biden-Harris administration is always behind the eighth ball during every major crisis? Why is it they have zero empathy for Americans who are suffering, especially Democrats that claim to have a monopoly of compassion and when real Americans are in need, where are they? Eight billion for Zelenskyy. What about the people of North Carolina, Georgia, South Carolina, Virginia, Tennessee, Florida? How about helping them?\par \par \uc2 We know -- we see this now with the hurricane and also with inflation that they said was transitory for three-plus years and with the victims of illegal immigration. Of course, the border's secure, the border's closed, the border's secure, they lied about that for three years. They lied about and are proud of the botch withdrawal in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 But despite four years of nothing but feckless failed leadership, the race is still close -- too close to call. Over the weekend, we have a slight edge for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in multiple polls. Now, AtlasIntel rated the top, along with Insider Advantage, Trafalgar, Rasmussen, well, it does show \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with the lead in Wisconsin, Michigan, Pennsylvania. Rasmussen has Trump up in North Carolina, Georgia, Arizona, Nevada. Trafalgar with a new poll has \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  up with a two-point lead in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 There are now more than six polls showing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a significant lead in Pennsylvania. If Trump wins Pennsylvania, it will be very hard for Harris to get to 270 electoral votes that would be needed to win.\par \par \uc2 But North Carolina and Georgia, if you're in those states, it is critical for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if he's going to win this election. So let's be very clear, you now have 36 days until election day, early voting is now starting all over the country, and anything can happen and this is an inflection point for the country. This is a tipping point election and this race remains for my comfort too tight.\par \par \uc2 The latest polling out of Virginia shows that the state is to the surprise of many very much in play.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, joining us now with reaction, the governor of the great Commonwealth of Virginia, \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2 , is with us.\par \par \uc2 Governor, great to have you back. And I'm sorry for all the devastation in your state as well. How are things looking in the commonwealth?\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 GLENN YOUNGKIN\uc2  (R), VIRGINIA: Sean, the devastation is just shocking and it's heartbreaking. I spent both Saturday and Sunday in southwest Virginia, in communities that have literally been washed away. People have lost everything and, of course, when you look at the devastation in North Carolina and Tennessee and South Carolina, Georgia and Florida, with 120- plus deaths, and we had two tragic deaths in Virginia, it is a moment for us to come together and to help one another.\par \par \uc2 Listen, what I saw last Friday in Virginia was the extraordinary demonstration of heroism. Virginia state police flying to Unicoi County in Tennessee and rescuing patients off the roof of a hospital that was being flooded. Virginia national guardsmen repelling out of Blackhawk helicopters into rushing waters, pulling people out of cars. And when I visited yesterday with electricity out for hundreds of thousands of Virginia and cellphone coverage completely disabled, they need food, they need water, people have gone to work.\par \par \uc2 And, Sean, I'll tell you, it is in fact in these moments of absolute crisis that the character of a community comes forth, and this is about Virginians helping Virginians, Americans helping Americans and in a moment where we need to all pull together, I am encouraged by what I have seen in southwest Virginia where people coming together what we've seen with folks sending resources to North Carolina for search and rescue missions.\par \par \uc2 There's still hundreds of people accounted for. We've seen what President Trump was doing in Georgia today, across the whole Southeast, we're watching people come together in a real moment of tragedy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm trying -- I'm trying to understand this and I'm -- this really isn't political for me. I think it's just basic common sense 101. I had spoken with Governor DeSantis and Governor Kemp. They had prepositioned all of -- all of these electrical trucks to get power up and running in their respective states.\par \par \uc2 Everybody knew was going to be a cat 3, maybe a cat 4 hurricane. They knew it was a big storm. They were prepared. They were ready and they mobilized immediately and they're still helping people.\par \par \uc2 Nobody really anticipated that North Carolina would get whacked as hard as it did, our prayers are with them. You know, one of the things that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did today is not only was he with \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2  and \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2 , who I have great admiration for, by the way, I urge people to donate to \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2 . I'm going to send the donation myself, and because people are in real need.\par \par \uc2 But he also got on the phone with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and, you know, he's trying to get Starlink. We -- we have people in pretty large portions of Asheville and other parts of North Carolina where they have no communications at all, Governor. You know, we don't know if people's lives are endangered they're not able to get to anybody to help them. You know, why isn't the administration, how did Joe sit on the beach all weekend and why was Kamala out you know with her Hollywood friends all weekend?\par \par \uc2 YOUNGKIN: Yeah. Well, so the innovation that comes to bear when there's a moment of crisis is critical, and it is exactly as you said moments like this that we have to try new things. Listen in southwest Virginia this week, we literally saw an entire community that was lost and so, we've had to bring in all kinds of makeshift routes in order to -- in order to get them communication, in order to get them temporary electricity, in order to provide shelter, food, a warm shower.\par \par \uc2 This has been a moment where we've got to stretch and do things that we hadn't thought we could do and listen, I think the Starlink idea is brilliant and we got to get moving here. We have been coordinating across all fronts, I have to say, pre-positioning all of the resources ahead of the storm was critical and we were able to do the exact same thing.\par \par \uc2 We have been, Sean, I have to say working well with FEMA. They, in fact, were moving very quickly over the last few days for us, and getting these resources has been critically important.\par \par \uc2 I'm going to go back. You just said -- you were just talking about \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2  and we're working with United Way and Southwest Virginia. The nonprofit communities have really moved quickly, feeding people, clothing people, showing up with medicine, really important, oxygen tanks for older folks who need the oxygen tanks.\par \par \uc2 This has been an all hands-on-deck moment and we need it all.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah. We really do.\par \par \uc2 Is there -- what do you think people can do that can help you around the country? We have one -- you know, I find the American people to be the most generous especially in times of need. What do -- what do you recommend? What -- what can people in other states be doing to help?\par \par \uc2 YOUNGKIN: So, yeah, so first of all, we've had offers of resources from governors all over. \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  called me today and said, governor, what do you need? And so, first and foremost, that expression of willingness to send whatever is needed is America at its best and then the ability for Americans to donate is really important.\par \par \uc2 As I said, \uc2 the United Way\uc2  in Southwest Virginia is the -- is the top deployer we've got on the ground, although churches and religious organizations are moving quickly. I think you're exactly right, \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2  is doing amazing work across the entire region. We actually have a group called God's Pit Crew in Virginia, that has gone to work to support things.\par \par \uc2 And so, I just ask folks if you can donate, please do. I appreciate all of the offers of support from, you know, governors around the country and governor's -- Governor Huckabee Sanders, thank you for your offer today. We're -- we're -- we're not going to put a moment's rest at night until we know that we have got everybody in a safe place.\par \par \uc2 Sean, this is going to be a long recovery. That's the other reality. When you have people who have been devastated the way that they have, this is going to be a long recovery period and therefore, this help is not just a 24, 48-hour surge. We're going to need to do it for a long period of time.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Governor, praying for the people in your state and the Commonwealth of Virginia. Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 All right, here with more reaction, FOX News contributor Charlie Hurt, former White House chief of staff, Reince Priebus is with us.\par \par \uc2 Reince, let me put back up on the screen some of the polls here. If you go back in 2020, AtlasIntel, Trafalgar, Rasmussen, Insider Advantage, those were the top pollsters. They had the best scores. They were the most accurate.\par \par \uc2 And Atlas shows a lead of Trump in Wisconsin, Michigan, Pennsylvania. Rasmussen has him up in North Carolina, Georgia, Arizona, Nevada. Trafalgar has Trump up two in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 How do you assess the race at this point? Because, you know, at the end of last week, there were polls I would argue that are flawed in terms of the methodology but they showed Kamala up. So I know a lot of people, you know, they're going through these emotional mood swings as a result of this. It's like emotional ping pong.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS, FORMER WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF: Right, right. Yeah, we -- and we all go through those mood swings with this election, that's for sure.\par \par \uc2 But I would just tell people that, you know, the entire race is going to come down to about 50,000 to 60,000 people. But how it assess it based on the polling is that if you look at the polling in 2020 and 2016, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  outperformed that polling by many percentage points.\par \par \uc2 So, for example, in Wisconsin, the average of all polls on election day in 2020 was that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was supposed to win Wisconsin by the average of all polls by 6.7 percent. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  only lost Wisconsin by 0.7 percent. So they were off by six percentage points. And that's the same pattern that you see across the country.\par \par \uc2 So in 2020, we were told that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was going to get killed by even all -- even the some of the polls that you've cited, but he didn't get killed. In fact, it was -- it was razor thin.\par \par \uc2 So when you look at the things that you just cited, Hispanics, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is at 40 percent with Hispanics. He's at plus 70 percent with non-white non-college educated voters. He's ahead with blue collar workers. He's plus 31 percent from people that graduated from trade organizations. This is much stronger than he was in 2020 and 2016.\par \par \uc2 The final thing, we're going to know a lot about where this is heading in about two weeks because the returns on the early votes in states like Florida, North Carolina and even Pennsylvania will start to tell you the pattern and how it looks compared to 2016 and 2020.\par \par \uc2 2020 is tough because it was a COVID year --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But we expect Democrats --\par \par \uc2 PRIEBUS: -- and everyone voted by mail.\par \par \uc2 HANNIYT: -- to have an advantage there.\par \par \uc2 PRIEBUS: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's a good point, but we would expect Democrats to have an advantage here. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 PRIEBUS: They will have an advantage on early vote but it may not be as much.\par \par \uc2 So in 2016, we knew that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was looking great at the final two days of the election because we saw that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's returns on early vote in Florida, he was 120,000 votes ahead of where \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  was. So we had more confidence going into that last than we did at any point in the election.\par \par \uc2 HANNITTY: Well, Charlie, less than 100,000 votes, three states in 2016, less than 50,000 in 2020 in three states.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yeah, yeah. No, I feel very confident about how things look right now. But in terms of the polling, you know, I don't -- I don't believe any of the polls. I don't believe the polls that I like. I don't believe the polls I don't like.\par \par \uc2 All that matters, all the people should be focused on is in their state and in their localities, how do they get people out to the polls, people who might not otherwise vote or people who think that their vote doesn't count or people who think that, well, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's already going to win, so I don't need to go out and vote.\par \par \uc2 In Virginia, early voting has already begun. A lot of conservatives are very suspicious of doing something new, like voting early. Well, this is the environment we live in. Go out and vote. I voted today, so go out and vote. It's very important because your vote does count and if you don't go out and vote, then you're going to wind up letting the election go to some people who do not care about your country as much as you do.\par \par \uc2 And so, no matter what the -- you know, your cynicism may be, you need to get out and vote and get people to go with you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Get out.\par \par \uc2 All right. Charlie, appreciate it. Reince Priebus, thank you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, two mothers whose daughters brutally murdered by Harris- Biden illegal immigrants suspects. They're going to tell us what they think of Kamala's photo-op stunt at the border on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Also, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  attend college football games this weekend. Yeah, two very different receptions, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: On Friday, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  went to the southern border for a photo- op where she pretended to actually care about the crisis that she and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , well, themselves created. Her half-hearted work as borders are to address the root causes of illegal immigration was clearly obviously nothing but a colossal failure and arguably the biggest national security threat in the history of this country.\par \par \uc2 Our country is now filled with the victims of what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has called migrant crime, people who have suffered at the hands of Harris Biden illegal immigrants people that didn't respect our laws, our borders, our sovereignty, people that never should have been allowed out into this country.\par \par \uc2 And sadly, some of those victims were lost to the ultimate crime. They were murdered, they are no longer with us. Only their loved ones now remain to warn and remind us of all the dangers of their open borders.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, how many dozens of Americans murdered? We scroll their names all the time. How many Americans have been raped, including children? We scroll their names also. How many Americans -- hundreds, victims of violent crimes. We scroll their names too.\par \par \uc2 Anyway joining us now, two mothers whose daughters were murdered. The suspects both Harris-Biden illegal immigrants. Alexis Nungaray is the mother of Jocelyn, a 12-year-old little girl who was killed in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Patty Morin is also with us and she is the mother of Rachel Morin who was herself a mother of five and was killed in Maryland while out on a run in a local park.\par \par \uc2 Alexis, let me start with your brave little 12-year-old girl who -- she was brutalized for hours. This young 12-year-old girl according to all reports fought back, bit these attackers, scratched these attackers, fought for her life and that went on for a significant period of time and then they murdered and threw in a river. I don't know how you recover from that.\par \par \uc2 And then you see \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  now who' been telling you for three years that the border is secure, out of her own mouth that you know, the border's closed, the border secure. What was your reaction to this trip on Friday?\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS NUNGARAYT, JOCELYN NUNGARAY'S MOTHER: I think \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's border trip this past Friday was such a sham it was the most disgraced, hollow effort I've ever seen from a candidate for presidency, quite frankly, it pissed me the hell off when I saw it.\par \par \uc2 She's been in charge for over the border for more than three years. She's done absolutely nothing infects to that. She not once has gone to the border until recently to what was there maybe a matter of 20 minutes. She had a pit stop there from one destination to another. She had all her right people there to get all the right angles for all her photos.\par \par \uc2 If I wasn't invited, I was invited to the border the last time with Trump. I was not invited this time. And if I was there this time, and I would have would have witnessed how she handled that entire interaction, I would have walked up to her and I would have asked her with this same effort you're giving which is not any, would it be the same if this was your daughter that you had to bury? Would you move the same way?\par \par \uc2 Because it's just -- it's not okay. It's not okay. It was very disgusting that she was there a matter of 20 minutes, didn't speak with any -- any ground people, any agents, any border people of council. No, she spoke with members of management and like I said was like what's been said, was there for a photo op.\par \par \uc2 Nothing was done. She's done nothing, and it was a complete disgrace. It was very, very appalling that she -- it's very convenient she wanted to be there one month before elections, how convenient she did this for a political gain for herself because she's not once reached out to me nor my family to even just give condolences regardless of the right side or the left side.\par \par \uc2 It's about humane and I lost my 12-year-old daughter to illegal immigrants that the Biden-Harris administration policies, border policies have let in this -- let in this country and we're not safe anymore. We do not have safe border control anymore.\par \par \uc2 She's done absolutely nothing and it's because of people like \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Colin Allred who is going to -- who's running for senator of Texas which is where I'm at. People like that, they don't keep the people safe. They don't keep our children safe.\par \par \uc2 We need somebody who will actually make change and actually do something, and that's not Kamala.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm so sorry. I mean, I think -- I don't think there's anything tougher in life than to lose a child.\par \par \uc2 Patty, your daughter was out jogging. Rachel, she was a mother of five. Now, you -- I know you have -- you're mourning the loss of your daughter and you're also a grandmother. And now, you've got five grandkids that'll never see their mom again and you'll never see your daughter again.\par \par \uc2 And there's \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , but it goes further than just show up. I want your thoughts on what you thought of her trip, but then her policies. She mocked border walls. She wants to decriminalize illegal immigration, offer free food, housing, health care, education, legal driver's license, her running mate does, and free college, a path to amnesty.\par \par \uc2 We have known terrorists, gang members, murderers, rapists, other violent criminals gangs, that have all drugs that have all come into this country as a result. You have paid the ultimate price.\par \par \uc2 What would you say to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ? what did you think of this?\par \par \uc2 PATTY MORIN, RACHEL MORIN'S MOTHER: I thought the whole thing was so ridiculous. The American people know that she is not sincere at all. She's done nothing the last four years. She's denied that there's been a problem. She hasn't even acknowledge the murders of my daughter or Alexis or some of the other victims.\par \par \uc2 She's the kind of person that, you know, if I -- if I don't look, if I don't acknowledge, it doesn't exist. So this whole thing going to the border is just a political stunt, hoping that she's going to check off a box and win some points. When I was in Congress, for one of the hearings -- go ahead.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, no, no. You go ahead, Patty. I'm sorry.\par \par \uc2 MORIN: Oh, okay. When I was in Congress for one of the hearings, a lot of the congressmen on the left were talking about this Senate bill and they're hoping that the American people hasn't read 370 pages of this bill where 5/6 of the money is going to foreign interest. It's not even going to the border. It's like $120,000 -- $120 billion, and I think only 18 or 16 of that actually going to the border, and it's not to keep immigrants out. It's actually to help facilitate them coming into our country.\par \par \uc2 So she's not -- she has not done anything to keep America safe at all.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Alexis and Patty, just an exit question. It's -- it's -- and I don't have a lot of time.\par \par \uc2 Alexis, did \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , did either of those three ever call you?\par \par \uc2 NUNGARAY: The one and only person that has called me out of the three would be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and it wasn't him calling me as a previous president. It was him calling me as a father, as someone who has kids, someone who couldn't even imagine what it would be like if this was their child. So I felt the empathy from him. He was very sincere.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Pat, same question.\par \par \uc2 MORIN: Yes, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Patty?\par \par \uc2 MORIN: Yes, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  nor Biden has reached out to my family at all during this whole time, even when they knew that it was an illegal immigrant and basically they let this person into our country.\par \par \uc2 President Trump has reached out to our family multiple times, to multiple members and we've had conversations and they'll just call to say, how are you doing? Is there anything we can do for you? How can we help you?\par \par \uc2 So he's been very compassionate and genuinely cares about our family and our recovering from this tragedy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I know that -- I speak for this audience, we're all praying for you and your family, and I can't imagine your loss, and I'm so sorry that this happened to both of you, and this can't happen in this country. It can't. This has to stop.\par \par \uc2 It is the biggest national security. Now we have known terrorists in the country.\par \par \uc2 Alexis, thank you. Patty, thank you, and your families, I promise you are in all of our prayers tonight.\par \par \uc2 Now, as Harris tries to rewrite the history of her failed record, her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has been holed up at a golf resort in northern Michigan this week preparing for tomorrow's debate with J.D. Vance, with Transportation Secretary pothole \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  playing J.D. Vance. I wonder how that's going.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, Walz did get the opportunity to leave debate camp for a few hours on Saturday. He headed to Ann Arbor, Michigan, to watch his neighbor