e a political impact either.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRIMBLE (on camera): Economists predict a port workers strike could cost the U.S. economy up to $2 billion in a single week. That's on the low end. There are some estimates that suggest it could cost 4-1/2 billion every single day that this potential strike lasts. John?\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: Well, the cargo stops moving. I don't know how the New York governor makes good on her pledge. We'll see. Maybe she is got an ace up her sleeve.\par \par \uc2 Grady, thank you very much. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, we take a look at the Senate race in Michigan. Democratic Representative Alyssa Slotkin and former Republican Representative \uc2 Mike Rogers\uc2  are running to fill Democrat \uc2 Debbie Stabenow\uc2 's seat after she opted not to run for reelection.\par \par \uc2 The current balance of power in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  is 51 Democrats, and those who caucus with them to 49 Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Rogers comes to the race after serving in the house for 14 years, four of those chairing the House Intelligence Committee. He also has the endorsement of former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 Slotkin was first elected to the House in 2018 after serving as a Middle East analyst with the CIA and the director for Iraq with the National Security Council.\par \par \uc2 A recent \uc2 New York Times\uc2 /Sienna poll has Slotkin leading Rogers by five points among likely voters. The latest Fox News power rankings has this race is leaning toward the Democrats, but Slotkin and her supporters are taking nothing for granted after she warned donors that her internal polling shows Vice President Harris underwater in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 FEC\uc2  reports, as of June 30, Slotkin has raised 24.1 million, compared to Rogers $5.4 million.\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential vice presidential nominee J.D. Vance has arrived in New York ahead of tomorrow's debate. He held several events