alf in particular is ending the American dream.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Are you surprised by all of this attention and all this vitriol around this document? Are you surprised by it when it started happening?\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: I'm surprised by the scope of it, to be sure. I'm not surprised that it happened. And the lesson that we learned, and we have learned loud and clear, is that when we do this again, and we're going to do it every election cycle because it's what Heritage does, that when the left combines to mischaracterize, figuratively, we are going to punch them back in the nose.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Well, Kevin, we appreciate you coming on. We will continue to go through policy by policy and deal with the facts.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: Thanks for having me.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Up next, the panel with analysis of the new FOX polling and what's behind the teamster's non-endorsement decision.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , (R) U.S. PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I have never seen the spirit like I have seen right now for this race. It blows it away from 2016, from 2020.\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , (D) VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Friends, we have some work to do. In fact, a lot of hard work ahead of us. But we like hard work.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: She has not just met sort of the generic benchmark, she is actually doing slightly better. Maybe \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her campaign know what they're doing despite the fact that folks don't like the economy.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The Democrats have always taken for granted that they are going to get our vote no matter what. And the Republicans are fancying themselves as the working people's party. I think right now both sides have to take a step back.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: That was something, the teamsters not endorsing Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , a