ve in the freedom to live safe from gun violence will finally pass an assault weapons ban, universal background checks and red flag laws.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: So much, so much is at stake in this election. So much is at stake in this election.\par \par \uc2 And understand this is not 2016 or 2020, for a number of reasons, including why the stakes are higher, because, two months ago, the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  basically told the former president that he will effectively be immune no matter what he does in the White House.\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Think about that. Think about that. Just imagine \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with no guardrails.\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Right? He who has vowed that, if reelected, he will be a dictator on day one.\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: That he will weaponize the Department of Justice against his political enemies, and has called for the -- quote -- "termination" of the Constitution of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Think about that. And let us be very clear. Somebody who suggests we should terminate the Constitution of the United States should never again stand behind the seal of the president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Never again. Never again. Never again.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: And one of the points that I mentioned on Tuesday, so let -- the people who served under him at the White House, who saw him every day, right, his national security adviser, his defense secretary, his chief of staff, and his vice president, all have warned -- all who worked with him every day in the White House, sat with him in the Oval Office, have warned America. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is not fit to be president of the United States and should never again occupy our nation's highest office.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: So...\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE: Not going back! Not going back!\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: And we're not going back.\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE: Not going back! Not going back! Not going back!\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: So it comes down to this. It comes down to this.\par \par \uc2 We are here together because we love our country. We love our country. (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: And we understand the awesome, the awesome responsibility that comes with the greatest privilege on earth, the privilege and pride of being an American.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE: USA! USA! USA!\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: That's right. That's right. That's right.\par \par \uc2 And so I believe it is the highest form, then, of patriotism to fight for the ideals of our country and to fight to realize the promise of America.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: So, North Carolina, we have 54 days until Election Day, 54 days.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: ... 54 days, and just 35 days, just 35 days until early voting begins. (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: And it's not only the presidency that's on the ballot. There are many important races, including Josh Stein running for governor...\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: ... whose opponent was handpicked by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and wants a ban, a total ban on abortion in this state, right.\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: So these are the stakes in this election up and down the ballot, up and down the ballot. But we know the power is with the people.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: The power is with the people. And your voice is your vote, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HA