et to keep it?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Well, listen, the idea is that everyone gets access to medical care, and you don't have to go through the process of going through an insurance company, having them give you approval, going through the paperwork, all of the delay that may require, who of us has not had that situation where you got to wait for approval and the doctor says, well, I don't know if your insurance company is going to cover this. Let's eliminate all of that. Let's move on.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, so did she co-sponsor the bill that she didn't actually support or is she lying?\par \par \uc2 That brings us to the border. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: The \uc2 United States Congress\uc2 , including some of the most conservative members of the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 , came up with a border security bill which I supported and that bill would have put 1,500 more border agents on the border to help those folks who are working there right now over time trying to do their job.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I believe if someone crosses over the border, it's -- illegally, it is illegal and you would -- you would decriminalize it?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: I would not make it a crime punishable by jail. I -- it should be a civil enforcement issue but not a criminal enforcement issue.\par \par \uc2 Listen, I think there's no question that we've got to critically reexamine ICE and its role and the way that it is being administered and the work it is doing and we need to probably think about starting from scratch.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So does the borders are that allowed, what, 11 million illegal immigrants to pour into this country unvetted really care about border security? Was she lying at the debate and using a deeply flawed political bill that would allow 4,000 or 5,000 illegals in before it even kicked in and then it was discretionary?\par \par \uc2 The answer is obvious and as reported by fake news CNN, Kamala previously vowed to end the detention of illegal immigrants, decrease funding for ICE, and ICE detainers, force you to cover the bill for transgender surgeries for illegal immigrants and convicts in jail.\par \par \uc2 These are radical beliefs and they don't just magically change overnight. Kamala's new vague policy positions mysteriously adopted only after she became the nominee are about as fake as her weird faces that she was making during last night's debate. There is nothing authentic about the Harris campaign. This is a candidate in the -- in the media mob protection program, and she literally threw her name on every socialist bill in the Senate and dissolved America's borders during her time as vice president and borders czar.\par \par \uc2 But now, she'll do and say anything she needs to do or say to win, and advance her career, even if that means throwing her cognitively impaired boss under the bus and right on cue, look who just boarded the Trump train. This was funny earlier today in Pennsylvania, the president himself \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  dawned a red Trump hat in front of a crowd in Shanksville in a fire station. The White House said he did it to show bipartisan unity on 9/11. Kamala's campaign is probably not very happy about the gesture, but Biden really doesn't hate Kamala after all, right? Who could blame him if he does?\par \par \uc2 Anyway, joining us now, the host of "Outkick's" "Tomi Lahren is Fearless", Tomi Lahren, FOX News contributor Charlie Hurt, Project 2021 chairman Horace Cooper.\par \par \uc2 Tomi, start with you.\par \par \uc2 All right. You know, the frustrating thing to me and I went into this last night in detail is all of these major radical left position she staked out, bills she sponsored, we have no idea if she still supports them? How does ABC Disney not ask those fundamental questions?\par \par \uc2 TOMI LAHREN, OUTKICK HOST: Well, they gave her a pass and I think 