cs. She also failed to explain why she has embraced all of these wildly radical positions that she now conveniently says she has changed her position on. You and I both know that the only reason she's changed her position is because she'll say absolutely anything to get elected.\par \par \uc2 And as Tomi just pointed out, all the Trump campaign has to do is run the footage of what she said last night compared to all the footage that she said before just as you just did. All you have to do is run that and let her sink herself with her own words in their ads and that's why she lost.\par \par \uc2 People don't trust her. They don't know her. The onus is on her and she failed last night.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, I'm looking at -- and we'll get into this later in the program, Horace, but I'm looking at even "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " and "Reuters", and I've spoken to a lot of pollsters today, they said no change, no real impact here.\par \par \uc2 And the fact that she was rehearsed, okay, got to give her credit. She did a little homework and she got her prepared lines. ABC did a horrible job in terms of asking really important pertinent questions that the -- I think the American people need to know before they start voting and they're starting to vote now.\par \par \uc2 And that to me is a colossal failure. They're the biggest loser in all of this, but I guess the question I have for you is, you know, if she can't move the ball because she can't really speak her true beliefs, how does that end even though she has all the -- all the aid and assistance of the media?\par \par \uc2 HORACE COOPER, PROJECT 21 CHAIRMAN: There's something that happened last night that's actually bigger than the aspirations of former President Trump or Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and that is that on December 15th, 1791, our founders got ratified the First Amendment. It is the only part of the Constitution that protects a commercial enterprise. That is the Fifth Estate. And