ight before your eyes and America is no longer respected in the world under Harris-Biden, and a woke far-left Harris administration -- that would only make things worse.\par \par \uc2 Now, today marks 23 years since September the 11th, 2001. Remember, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is more concerned about preventing you, the American people. She wants you to be courageous and abandon using the term radical Islamic terrorism, you know, the people that attacked us on 9/11.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: We must have the courage to object when they use that term "radical Islamic terrorism", which ignores how Muslims have overwhelmingly been the greatest victims of terror.\par \par \uc2 And we must also have the courage to reject that term "illegal alien". I have seen some of the worst of criminal behavior. I have seen the worst of crime. An undocumented immigrant is not a criminal.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Here now with the reaction, \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2  senior fellow, Victor Davis Hanson.\par \par \uc2 After last night, is it possible that we are going to have a Democratic presidential candidate that has taken on all of these radical positions, supported all of these radical bills, including the new green deal, eliminating private health insurance, you know, defund, dismantle the police and decriminalize illegal immigrants and free housing health care education and sex change operations, and she's not going to be asked a single question about it or have to explain herself? Is that -- is that the America we're now living in?\par \par \uc2 VICTOR DAVIS HANSON, HOOVER INSTITUTION SENIOR FELLOW: Yeah, I think so. I think that was a Candy Crowley debate, only much worse, and I think they've totally discredited themselves, ABC, and the whole genre of having media people conduct any presidential debate in the -- in the future, it's not going to be disinterested, it's going to be biased.\par \par \uc2 But I think more importantly, Sean, as to your earlier comments, the world is looking at all of this and the developments the last three and half years, they see a window of opportunity that might not come up again, and there and a lot of people bad actors are going to try something stupid, maybe next four and a half months of the Biden lame duck tenure, you know, Putin didn't go in and four administrations -- four administrations, he only did not go in during the Trump. All three of the earlier ones he did.\par \par \uc2 As soon as Biden came in, the Afghanistan pull out, the crazy comments about the reaction would depend from the United States on whether it was a major or minor invasion, and suddenly, we have the biggest war in Europe since World War II.\par \par \uc2 China, that -- if you add in the dressing down in Anchorage, the Chinese balloon, this inane comments that China from Biden he said is not really a rival, it's -- it doesn't post a challenge, and suddenly they're threatening Taiwan, they're ramming Philippine ships.\par \par \uc2 And you look at the Houthis, we lift the terrorist designation under Biden, and they control the Red Sea. We restore money to \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and the Palestinian authorities, we get October 7th. We give a sweetheart oil deal, allow that with Syria, they're attacking troops. You mentioned Iran, as soon as we lifted the embargo and begged them to get in the Iran deal, they're supplying all of Israel's existential enemies.\par \par \uc2 And when you look at why this is -- I mean we're 50,000 troops short in the military. We're mothballing major ships of the merchant marines. We've got a president who and a State Department team that has this therapeutic view, and these people are going to do something stupid because we're still a strong country.\par \par \uc2 But they think that in the next few months, in this lame duck presidency and the possibility that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  either will act as de facto president or get elected, that 